  <para style="h">Utom Mme Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="toc1">Utom Mme Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="toc2">Utom Mme Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="toc3">Utom</para>
  <para style="mt1">Utom Mme Abọsịd</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="ACT 1" />
  <para style="s1">Eben Yisọs Edọọk Hefịn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 1:1" />Ke akpa ñwed mmi, Tiofilọs, ami mmaawet mbaña afịd se Yisọs aketọọñọ adinam ñnyʌñ ñkpeep <verse eid="ACT 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 1:2" />tutu usen e-ekebenne anye edọọk hefịn. Mbemiso ekeben anye edọọk, anye amaanọ mme abọsịd a-anye akemekke ewʌhọ ato Adisana Sịbidịd. <verse eid="ACT 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 1:3" />Ke anye amaakebọ ndutʌhọ ama, anye amaawọt ammọ idem ye mme uwak idiọọñọ i-imiikidooho se efaaña, ke imọ mmọdo iba ke uwem. Anye amaawọt ammọ idem ke idaha ñkpọ nte usen aba anyʌñ atañ ikọ abaña abioubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 1:4" />Ini keed, idaha anye akesʌkkọ adia ndidia ye ammọ, anye amaanọ ewʌhọ abo, <char style="wj">“Ikiikpọñ Yeruselem, ado itie ibet enọ e-Ete mmi akenwọñọke inọọ ndufo, a-ndufo ekekoppo ento miin.</char> <verse eid="ACT 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 1:5" /><char style="wj">Sia Yọọn akekama mmọọñ anịm uduọkmmọọñ, ado ke mme usen ifañ adiidi, eyainịm ndufo uduọkmmọọñ ye Adisana Sịbidịd.”</char><verse eid="ACT 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 1:6" />Ndin, ke ini ammọ eketieghe ekanna anye ekʌk, ammọ emaebịp anye ete, “Abọọñ, afo ayaatịmme ayaak ukara abioubọọñ anọ Isrel idahami?”<verse eid="ACT 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 1:7" />Anye amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, <char style="wj">“Inaaha ndufo ediọọñọ mme ini me usen se Ete akenịm ke adudu amọ.</char> <verse eid="ACT 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 1:8" /><char style="wj">Ado ndufo eyaebọ adudu Adisana Sịbidịd amaadidoro ndufo ke idem. Ndufo eyaenyʌñ edo mme ntiense mmi ke Yeruselem, ke afịd Yudia ye Sameria, tutu asịm ke akpatre ederimbod.”</char><verse eid="ACT 1:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 1:9" />Ke anye amaaketañ ikọ ami ama, emaeben anye edọọk anyọñ ke iso ammọ tutu ntọñanyọñ afʌk anye, ammọ ikịtte anye aba.<verse eid="ACT 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 1:10" />Ke ammọ ekesʌkkọ ewuuk anyen ese anyọñ naña anye adọọk, ete ise, awo iba e-ekesiineke mfia afọñ emaedida ke ñkañ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 1:11" />Ammọ emaebịp mme mbed mbuume ete, “Ndufo ideen Kalili, nsoo inam ndufo edudak mi ewuuk anyen ese ikpaanyọñ? Yisọs e-ebenne ikpọñ ndufo mi edọọk ke hefịn, ayaatịmme adi ke ukem usʌñ a-ndufo ekịtte naña anye adọọk aka hefịn.”<verse eid="ACT 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emek Matayas Adat Itie Yudas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 1:12" />Ndin mme abọsịd emaetịmme ekpọñ Abod Ọlif enyọñ Yeruselem, a-akedooho isañ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte kilomita keed</char></note> usen Sabad keed. <verse eid="ACT 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 1:13" />Ke ini ammọ emaekediwuọ, ammọ emaedọọk ufọk anyọñ ekaa ubeed a-ammọ ekebaaha. Mbon se ikiba do ekedo:</para>
  <para style="b" vid="ACT 1:13" />
  <para style="li1" vid="ACT 1:13">Pita, Yọọn, Yems ye Andru;</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="ACT 1:13">Filib ye Tọmọs;</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="ACT 1:13">Batolomiu ye Matiu;</para>
  <para style="li1" vid="ACT 1:13">Yems ayịn Alfiọs, Saimọn Amaidʌñ ye Yudas ayịn Yems.<verse eid="ACT 1:13" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 1:14" />Afịd ammọ, uwak ibaan, Mmeri eka Yisọs, ye nditọeka amọ ideen, emaeboho itie keed ebọñ akam afịd ini.<verse eid="ACT 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 1:15" />Ke mme usen ado, Pita amaadakka ada ke ufọọd mme andinịm ke akpanikọ (e-ekeyọhọke ñkpọ nte awo ikie mme edịb) anyʌñ <verse eid="ACT 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 1:16" />abo ate, “Mme nditọeka<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">adelfọi </char><char style="ft" closed="false">a-awuọñọke </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nditọeka </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ideen ye ibaan </char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌñ asʌk ada anọ mbon e-enịmme Krais ke akpanikọ, me edo ideen me edo ibaan ke atu ubon Abasi; se ñko ke Utom 6:3; Utom 11:29; Utom 12:17; Utom 16:40; Utom 18:18, 27; 21:7, 17; 28:14, 15. </char></note> ke Krais, ana ikọ Abasi asu kpa naña Adisana Sịbidịd amaaketañ ke usen edem ato inua Defid abaña Yudas a-akedatta mme andikimʌm Yisọs usʌñ. <verse eid="ACT 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 1:17" />Anye akedo keed ke atu ñnyịn, amaanyʌñ anie udeeme ke utom ñnyịn.”<verse eid="ACT 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 1:18" />(Yudas amaaben akʌk ibak amọ akedep ikọd. Do ke anye aketo iwuod aduọ, afịd nsia anyʌñ awuọñọ. <verse eid="ACT 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 1:19" />Afịd awo ke Yeruselem emaekop ebaña ñkpa amọ, ndin emaeben itie ado ekoot Akeldama ke usem ammọ, awuọọñọke Inwañ Iyiib).<verse eid="ACT 1:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 1:20" />Pita amaadian do ate, “Sia, ewewet ke ñwed mme Saam:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 1:20">“ ‘Yak itie idʌñ amọ akappa ndoon;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 1:20">yak awo ndomokeed akuunyʌñ udʌñ do,’</para>
  <para style="m" vid="ACT 1:20">ñko,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 1:20">“ ‘Yak awo mfen adat itie amọ.’<verse eid="ACT 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 1:21" />Ke ntoro, a-afọn adimek keed ke atu mbon e-ekebaaha ye ñnyịn afịd ini se Abọọñ Yisọs akeba ye ñnyịn, <verse eid="ACT 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 1:22" />tọọñọ ke ini uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn tutu asịm ini ekebenne anye ikpọñ ñnyịn. Sia ana keed ke atu ammọ ado ntiense ye ñnyịn ke abaña adised Yisọs ke ñkpa.”<verse eid="ACT 1:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 1:23" />Ndin ammọ emaesiak anyịñ awo iba, Yosef a-akekereke Basabas (e-ekenyʌññọ esikoot Yọstus) ye Matayas. <verse eid="ACT 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 1:24" />Ammọ ndin emaebọñ akam ebo, “Abọọñ, afo adiọọñọ afịd esịd awo, iwọt ñnyịn ke atu awo iba ami, anye a-afo amekke <verse eid="ACT 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 1:25" />abo adidat itie utom abọsịd, a-Yudas akewuọhọ akpọñ aka usʌñ amọ.” <verse eid="ACT 1:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 1:26" />Akema ammọ emaesịn afia, ndin afia amaasana Matayas. Ke ke ntoro emaedat Matayas edian ke atu mme abọsịd duob mme keed.<verse eid="ACT 1:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="ACT 2" />
  <para style="s1">Enọ Adisana Sịbidịd ke Usen Pentikọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 2:1" />Ke usen Pentikọs amaakedikem, mme mbed emaesoobo itie keed. <verse eid="ACT 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 2:2" />Ke unana idodanyen, akpọsọñ uyom amaato hefịn adiyọhọ ufọk a-ammọ eketieghe. <verse eid="ACT 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 2:3" />Ndin ammọ emaekịt ñkpọ e-ekebaaha nte mme edemeikañ naña esuana edoro ammọ keedekeed ke idem. <verse eid="ACT 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 2:4" />Afịd ammọ emaeyọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd enyʌñ etọọñọ adisem mme nsio-nsio usem naña Sịbidịd akenọọ ammọ ukeme.<verse eid="ACT 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 2:5" />Ke ini ado mme Yuu se ikinie mbaak Abasi, e-eketooho mme nsio-nsio idịd ke afịd ederimbod ke idak hefịn emaeba ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 2:6" />Ke ini ammọ ekekoppo uyom ami, ammọ emaewuọñọ edi ke ñkpaidem, sia mme awo keedekeed emaekop naña mme mbed esem usem idʌñ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 2:7" />Ke ataa ñkpaidem, ammọ emaebịp, “Nte afịd mme awo e-esemme mme usem ami idooho mbon Kalili? <verse eid="ACT 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 2:8" />Anam die ndin nọ ñnyịn keedekeed ikop se ammọ etañ ke mme usem ukañ ñnyịn? <verse eid="ACT 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 2:9" />Ñnyịn ido mbon Peet, mbon Medes, mbon Elam, mbon e-edʌññọ ke Mesopotemia, Yudia, Kapadosia, Pọntus ye Esia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ikpeghe ukara Rom a-akekereke Esia</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 2:10" />Frikia ye Pamfilia, Iyib ye mme ubaak itie ke Libia e-ekpereke Siriin; isenawo e-eketooho Rom <verse eid="ACT 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 2:11" />(mme Yuu ye mbon se ikappa esịd idʌk edu ukpono mme Yuu); Mbon Kred ye mbon Arab, ñnyịn ikop nte ammọ etañ ebaña mme utịppeñkpọ Abasi ke mme edemeikọ ñnyịn.” <verse eid="ACT 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 2:12" />Ke ayọhọ ñkpaidem, ammọ emaebịp emọ-emọ ete, “Nsoo ke ñkpọ ami awuọñọ?”<verse eid="ACT 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 2:13" />Ado ubaak awo emaesaha ammọ enyʌñ ebo, “Ukọd anaam ammọ.”<verse eid="ACT 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pita Atañ Ikọ Anọ Atu Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 2:14" />Ndin Pita amaadakka ada ye mme abọsịd duob ye keed anyʌñ abọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio anọ atu awo ate: “Inekke ikpañ utọñ, afịd ndufo mme emọ-emọ Yuu ye mme andidʌñ ke Yeruselem, yak nnam nọ inwaña ndufo; inekke ikpañ utọñ ikop se ami ntañ. <verse eid="ACT 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 2:15" />Idooho ukọd anaam ibon ami naña ubaak ndufo ekere. Abak abọhọ; awo isikpaaha mmịn ke ñkanika usʌkkeed ubakusen! <verse eid="ACT 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 2:16" />Iyoo, se prọfed Yuel aketañ anịm ado ami:<verse eid="ACT 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 2:17" />“ ‘Ke mme akpatre usen, Abọọñ Abasi atañ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">ami ñyaanwañña Sịbidịd mmi nduọk afịd uduud awo.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:17">Nditọ ideen ye nditọ ibaan ndufo eyaetañ prọfesi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">ñkparawa ideen ndufo eyaenyʌñ ekiit ñkukịd,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">ikpọ ideen ndufo eyaedappa ndab.<verse eid="ACT 2:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 2:18" />Ñko ñyaanwañña Sịbidịd mmi nduọk nditọufọk mmi ideen ye ibaan</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:18">ke mme usen ado,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:18">ammọ eyaenyʌñ etañ prọfesi.<verse eid="ACT 2:18" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 2:19" />Ami ñyaawọt mme utịppeñkpọ ke hefịn ye mme</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:19">idiọọñọ ke isọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:19">iyiib ye ikañ ye mme eboho nsʌñikañ.<verse eid="ACT 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 2:20" />Utịn ayaakappa ado ekịm</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">afiọñ anyʌñ akappa iyiib</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">mbemiso usen Abọọñ Abasi adi, akwa usen itooro.<verse eid="ACT 2:20" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 2:21" />Ndin awo akeedodo a-akoodo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:21">anyịñ Abọọñ Abasi ayaabọkkọ.’<verse eid="ACT 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 2:22" />“Nditọ Isrel ñnyịn, ikpañ utọñ ikop se ami ntañ inọọ ndufo: Yisọs a-aketooho Nasared akedo awo a-Abasi akebenne iwọt ndufo anwa-anwa ato ke mme utịppeñkpọ, mme ñkpọ ñkpaidem ye mme idiọọñọ a-Abasi akenamma ke ufọọd ndufo ato ke ubọk amọ, nte ndufo ke idem ndufo ediọọñọke. <verse eid="ACT 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 2:23" />Emaeyaak anye inọ ndufo ato ke uduak ye ubonoñkpọ a-Abasi akenieghe, ndin ato ke unwam mbon ibak, ndufo emaewot anye ke adikọñ ke krọs. <verse eid="ACT 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 2:24" />Ado Abasi amaanam anye aset ke ñkpa, anam anye abọkkọ ndutʌhọ ñkpa, sia ñkpa ikinieghe adudu adisịn anye ukad. <verse eid="ACT 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 2:25" />Ñko Defid amaatañ ami abaña Yisọs:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:25">“ ‘Ami mmaakịt Abọọñ Abasi ke iso mmi afịd ini.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:25">Sia anye aba ke ubọk nnasia mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:25">ñkpọ ndomokeed idintəkkoke miin.<verse eid="ACT 2:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 2:26" />Ke ntak ado esịd andat, edeme mmi anyʌñ akwọ itooro Abasi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:26">ikpọkidem mmi ñko ayaanie nduọkadudu ke idodanyen,<verse eid="ACT 2:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 2:27" />sia afo uduñkpọññọ miin ke abioekpo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:27">afo uduunyʌññọ uyak adisana awo mfo akịt mbiara.<verse eid="ACT 2:27" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 2:28" />Afo amenam ami ndiọọñọ mme usʌñ uwem;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:28">ayaannọ miin ayọhọ idadesịd ke iso mfo.’<verse eid="ACT 2:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 2:29" />“Ikọd ñnyịn Isrel, yak ntañ inọ ndufo uko-uko ke nsọbom ñnyịn Defid amaakpa, emaenyʌñ ebuuk anye, itiad udi amọ asʌk ababa awuọ mfịn. <verse eid="ACT 2:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 2:30" />Ado anye akedo prọfed, amaanyʌñ adiọọñọ ke Abasi amaanam akaakan enwọñọ adimek keed ke atu ayeyịn amọ ndot ke ebekpo amọ. <verse eid="ACT 2:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 2:31" />Defid amaanie ifiọk abaña ini iso ke anye adibemiso ntañ mbaña adised Krais ke ñkpa, ke awo idiikpọññọ anye ke abioekpo, ñko ke ikpọkidem amọ idiikịtte mbiara. <verse eid="ACT 2:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 2:32" />Abasi amaanam Yisọs ami aset ke ñkpa, ndin ñnyịn ido ntiense ibaña ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="ACT 2:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 2:33" />Ke emaekedịppe anye edot ke ubọk nnasia Abasi, anye a-abọ Adisana Sịbidịd ekenwọñọke ato Ete. Do ke anye aduọk ammọ Sịbidịd a-ndufo ekịtte enyʌñ ekop mi mfịn. <verse eid="ACT 2:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 2:34" />Sia Defid ke idem amọ ikidọọhọ ika hefịn, ado anye amaabo,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:34">“ ‘Abọọñ amaabo Abọọñ mmi ate:</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:34">“Tie ke ubọk nnasia mmi<verse eid="ACT 2:34" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 2:35" />tutu ami nnam mme asua mfo</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:35">edo ifịm udodukod mfo.” ’<verse eid="ACT 2:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 2:36" />“Ke ntoro, yak afịd ufọk Isrel ediọọñọ ayọhọ-ayọhọ ke Abasi amaanam Yisọs ami a-ndufo ekekọññọ ewot ke krọs ado Abọọñ ye Krais.”<verse eid="ACT 2:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 2:37" />Ke mme awo emaekekop ikọ ami esịd amaabʌññọ ammọ, ndin ammọ emaebịp Pita ye mme abọsịd mbon ako ebo, “Nditọeka, nsoo ke ñnyịn idiinam?”<verse eid="ACT 2:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 2:38" />Ndin Pita amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Afịd ndufo ikappa esịd inyʌñ ibọ uduọkmmọọñ ke anyịñ Yisọs Krais nọ efeen mme idiọọkñkpọ ndufo. Ndufo ñko eyaebọ enọ Adisana Sịbidịd. <verse eid="ACT 2:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 2:39" />Enwọñọ ami inie ndufo ye nditọ ndufo, ye afịd awo e-ebaaha ke anyan usʌñ, ye afịd mbon a-Abọọñ Abasi ñnyịn adiikoot inọ idem amọ.”<verse eid="ACT 2:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 2:40" />Ndin Pita amaakwọrọ ikọ akpeene, adʌt ammọ utọñ anyʌñ akpeiye ammọ ate, “Inyaaña idem ndufo isio ke mbiara emana ami.” <verse eid="ACT 2:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 2:41" />Mbon se ikitat esịd ikop ikọ amọ emaebọ uduọkmmọọñ, ndin ñkpọ nte awo tọsịn ita emaekeene edʌk ke atu ammọ usen ado.<verse eid="ACT 2:41" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ewuana mme Andinịm ke Akpanikọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 2:42" />Ammọ emaenekke esịn idem ke ukpeebñkpọ a-mme abọsịd ekenọọhọ ye ke ewuana, adiana ye adibuuñ uyo ye adibọñ akam. <verse eid="ACT 2:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 2:43" />Uteñe amaamʌm afịd awo adikịt uwak utịppeñkpọ ye mme utom idiọọñọ a-mme abọsịd ekenaññake. <verse eid="ACT 2:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 2:44" />Afịd mbon se ikinịm ke akpanikọ emaesisoobo itie keed, enyʌñ ewawana afịd ñkpọ enie. <verse eid="ACT 2:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 2:45" />Ammọ emaenyaam se ammọ ekenie edeeme enọ mme awo akeene naña mfịna awo keedekeed akedo. <verse eid="ACT 2:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 2:46" />Afịd usen ammọ emaesisoobo ke mme afe tembịd. Ñko ammọ emaesibuuñ uyo ke ufọk ammọ, enyʌñ ewuana edia ke inemesịd, <verse eid="ACT 2:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 2:47" />etooro Abasi, enyʌñ ekịt asaña-asaña mfọn ke iso afịd awo. Ke usen ke usen, Abọọñ amaadian mme awo ekebọọhọ adinyaaña anọ ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 2:47" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="ACT 3" />
  <para style="s1">Pita Akọk Mbʌñọ Abeeñe Ebeeñe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 3:1" />Usen keed Pita ye Yọọn emaekaa tembịd ke ini ubọñ akam, ke ñkanika ita uweemeayio. <verse eid="ACT 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 3:2" />Nte ammọ ekekpereke tembịd, ammọ emaekịt awo a-akemanake mbʌñọ naña eben eka inuaatob tembịd e-ekekoodo Uyaiya Inuaatob, nọ anye atie do abeeñe mme awo se ikikaa tembịd ñkpọ. <verse eid="ACT 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 3:3" />Ke ini anye akekịtte naña Pita ye Yọọn eka tembịd, anye amaabeeñe ammọ akʌk. <verse eid="ACT 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 3:4" />Pita ye Yọọn emaewuuk anyen ese anye, ndin Pita amaabo anye, “Nekke ise ñnyịn.” <verse eid="ACT 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 3:5" />Ndin awo mbʌñọ ado amaanekke ase ammọ, abeeñe idem adibọ ñkpọ nto ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 3:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 3:6" />Akem Pita amaabo anye, “Ami nnieghe silfa me kold, ado se nnie ke ami unọọ. Ke anyịñ Yisọs Krais awo Nasared, dakka da saña.” <verse eid="ACT 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 3:7" />Ndin Pita amaanyan ubọk nnasia abenne anye ke anyọñ, ndin kpa ataa idahado, ñkpad ye itọñ ukod ammọ emaesọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 3:8" />Anye amaatamma ada ke ukod atọọñọ adisaña. Ndin anye amaakeene ammọ adʌk mme afe tembịd, asaaña, ataam anyʌñ atooro Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 3:9" />Idem amaanekke akpa mme awo ke ini ammọ ekekịtte naña anye asaña anyʌñ atooro Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 3:10" />Ammọ emaetoiyo ke anye ado awo a-akesitieghe ke inuaatob tembịd e-ekoodo Uyaiya Inuaatob, ndin idem amaakpa ammọ abaña se ikitịppe inọ anye.<verse eid="ACT 3:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pita Atañ Ikọ Anọ mme Atu Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 3:11" />Ke ini awo ado akesʌkkọ amʌm Pita ye Yọọn akama, afịd awo emaefeeñe ekaa Mben Esa Sọlọmọn ke akpọsọñ ñkpaidem. <verse eid="ACT 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 3:12" />Pita akekịt ami, anye amaabo ammọ: “Nditọ Isrel ñnyịn, ntak a-ñkpọ ami ikpaaha ndufo idem-e? Ntak a-ndufo iseeghe ñnyịn nte ebo ke ato ke adudu me eti uwem ñnyịn anam awodeen ami asaña-a?” <verse eid="ACT 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 3:13" />Abasi mme eteete ñnyịn, Ebraham, Aisik, ye Yekọb a-anọ isʌñutom amọ Yisọs ubọọñ. Ndufo emaeyaak anye enọ ete ewot, emaekañ anye ke iso Pailed, akpesʌkado a-Pailed akeyemme adisaana anye ñyaak. <verse eid="ACT 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 3:14" />Ndufo emaesịn Eti ye Adisana Awo, etịmme ebo esaana awodawo eyaak. <verse eid="ACT 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 3:15" />Ndufo emaewot andinọ uwem, ado Abasi amaanam anye aset ke ñkpa. Ñnyịn ido ntiense ibaña ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="ACT 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 3:16" />Awo a-ndufo ekịtte enyʌñ ediọọñọ mi, akop nsọñidem ato mbuọdidem ke anyịñ Yisọs. Mbuọdidem ke anyịñ Yisọs anọ anye nsọñidem, nte afịd ndufo ekịtte.<verse eid="ACT 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 3:17" />“Nditọ Isrel ñnyịn, idahami ami mmediọọñọ ke ndufo ekenam ñkpọ ami ke unana adidiọọñọ ukem naña mbọọñ i-ikarake ndufo ekenam. <verse eid="ACT 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 3:18" />Usʌñ naña Abasi akenam se anye aketañ ato inua afịd mme prọfed asu, abo ke Krais ayaabọ ufen, ado ami. <verse eid="ACT 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 3:19" />Ikappa esịd inyʌñ itịmme ikeene Abasi, nọ ato do efeen mme ndiọiñkpọ ndufo, nọ ini adidemme a-atooho Abọọñ isịm ndufo, <verse eid="ACT 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 3:20" />ñko nọ anye anọ Krais e-ekemekke enịm inọọ ndufo, a-adooho Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 3:21" />Anye ayaaba ke hefịn tutu ini akem a-Abasi adiinọ afịd se anye akenwọñọ ke usen edem ato ke mme ndisana prọfed amọ. <verse eid="ACT 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 3:22" />Sia Moses amaabo, ‘Abọọñ Abasi ndufo ayaasio prọfed a-abaaha nte ami ke atu ndufo. Ana ndufo ekpañ utọñ ekop afịd se anye atañ inọ ndufo. <verse eid="ACT 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 3:23" />Ndin awo imiikpañña utọñ inọ prọfed, eyaebịne anye esio afịd-afịd ke atu mbon ammọ.’<verse eid="ACT 3:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 3:24" />“Ke akpanikọ, afịd mme prọfed, tọọñọ ke Samwel, e-emaeketatañ ikọ ebaña, emaebak etañ ebaña mme usen ami. <verse eid="ACT 3:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 3:25" />Ndufo edo mme adiaakpa mme prọfed ado, emenyʌñ esịne ke enwọñọ a-Abasi akenamma ye mme eteete ndufo, a-akebooho Ebraham, ‘Adiito ke ubon mfo afịd awo ke ederimbod ebọ adidiọñ.’  <verse eid="ACT 3:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 3:26" />Ke Abasi amaakenam isʌñutom amọ Yisọs aset ke ñkpa, anye aketo anọ anye adidiọñ ndufo, ke adinam ndufo ekappa ekpọñ mme ibak usʌñ ndufo.”<verse eid="ACT 3:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="ACT 4" />
  <para style="s1">Pita ye Yọọn ke Iso Sanhidrin</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 4:1" />Ndin ke ini Pita ye Yọọn ekesʌkkọ etañ ikọ enọ mme awo, mme aku ye adaiso mme akpeme tembịd, ye mme Sadusi, emaesaña ebịne ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 4:2" />Ukpeebñkpọ se ibaña adised ke ñkpa ke anyịñ Yisọs a-mme abọsịd ekekwọrọke amaafịna mme aku ye mme Sadusi eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 4:3" />Ndin sia akedooho ndubiayio ammọ emaemʌm Pita ye Yọọn esịn ke ufọk ñkpakọb tutu asịm edem usen. <verse eid="ACT 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 4:4" />Ado uwak mbon e-ekekoppo etob ado emaenịm ke akpanikọ, ndin ado amaanam ibad awo e-ekenịmme ke akpanikọ amaasịm ñkpọ nte tọsịn ition.<verse eid="ACT 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 4:5" />Edem usen, mme adaukara, mme ñkpisọñ, ye mme akpeeb mbed emaesoobo ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 4:6" />Anas, ekamba aku, ye Kaifas, Yọọn, Aleksanda, ye afịd mbon se ikito ufọk akwa aku emaeba do ñko. <verse eid="ACT 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 4:7" />Ammọ emaeben Pita ye Yọọn edi ke iso ammọ enyʌñ etọọñọ adibịp ammọ mbuume: “Ke nsutọ adudu, ye ke anyịñ anie ke ndufo ekenam afịd ami?”<verse eid="ACT 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 4:8" />Ndin Pita, amaakeyọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd, amaabo ammọ ate: “Mme andikara abio ye mme ñkpisọñ ke Isrel! <verse eid="ACT 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 4:9" />Adieke ndufo ibịppe ñnyịn mfịn ami ebaña mfọn a-ñnyịn ikifọnnọ ye awo mbʌñọ ye naña anye akesaña abọ nsọñidem, <verse eid="ACT 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 4:10" />afịd ndufo, ye afịd ubon Isrel, idiọọñọ ami: Ato anyịñ Yisọs Krais awo Nasared, a-ndufo ekekọññọ ke krọs, a-Abasi akenamma anye aset ke ñkpa, ke awo a-adaaha mi ke iso ndufo anie nsọñidem. <verse eid="ACT 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 4:11" />Yisọs ado</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:11">“ ‘itiad a-ndufo mme abọbufọk ekesịnne,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:11">ndin anye adikappa ado itiad inuuk.’<verse eid="ACT 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 4:12" />Adinyaaña ibaaha ke awo mfen ndomokeed, sia anyịñ ndomokeed mfen ibaaha ke idak hefịn e-enọọhọ ubonawo, a-ñnyịn inaaha ibọ adinyaaña ito.”<verse eid="ACT 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 4:13" />Ke ini ammọ ekekịtte uko Pita ye Yọọn, enyʌñ ediọọñọ ke ammọ ikikaaha ñwed, ado ke ammọ ekedo mme ñkaña awo, idem amaakpa ammọ eti-eti. Ammọ emaenyʌñ ediọọñọ ke Pita ye Yọọn ekeba ye Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 4:14" />Ndin sia ammọ emaekekịt awo a-akebọọhọ nsọñidem nte ada ye ammọ, uyio ikibaaha ammọ aba ke itọñ. <verse eid="ACT 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 4:15" />Ke ammọ emaekenọ uyio ete Pita ye Yọọn ekpọñ atu mbono esob Sanhidrin ekeba ke anwa, ammọ emaenie nneme ke atu idem ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 4:16" />Ndin ammọ emaebịp idem ammọ ete, “Nsoo ke ñnyịn ikpinam ye ibon ami? Afịd awo se idʌñ ke Yeruselem e-ediọọñọ ke ammọ e-enam ekamba utom idiọọñọ, ndin ñnyịn idiikanna ifaaña. <verse eid="ACT 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 4:17" />Ado mbaak ñkpọ ami adika iso asuana asịm afịd awo idem, ana ñnyịn ikpan ammọ ite ammọ ekuumaana etañ ikọ aba enọọ awo ndomokeed ke anyịñ ami.”<verse eid="ACT 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 4:18" />Ke emaekema, ammọ emaemaana ekoot Pita ye Yọọn ebo edʌk edi esob, enyʌñ ewuuk ammọ ete keetañ ikọ, keenyʌñ ekpeep ñkpọ ndomokeed ke anyịñ Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 4:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 4:19" />Ado Pita ye Yọọn emaebọọrọ ammọ ete, “Itʌm ibiide ke idem ndufo ise me afọn ke iso Abasi adikop uyio ndufo ñkan uyio Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 4:20" />Sia ñnyịn idiikanna itre aditañ mbaña se ñnyịn ikikịt inyʌñ ikop.”<verse eid="ACT 4:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 4:21" />Ke emaekemaana edịkke ammọ uwem, emaesaana ammọ eyaak. Esob Ikpaisọñ mme Yuu ikikanna ibiide se ufen ekpenọọ ammọ, sia adooho afịd awo ekesʌk etooro Abasi ke se ikitịppe. <verse eid="ACT 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 4:22" />Sia awo a-akebọọhọ utịppe idiọọñọ ukọk udọñọ ami amaabọhọ isua aba ke emana.<verse eid="ACT 4:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Andinịm ke Akpanikọ Ebọñ Akam</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 4:23" />Ke emaekesaana ammọ eyaak, Pita ye Yọọn emaenyọñ ebịne mbon ammọ enyʌñ ekedọkkọ ammọ afịd se mme ikpọ aku ye mme ñkpisọñ ekebo ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 4:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 4:24" />Ke ini ammọ ekekoppo ado, afịd ammọ emaebenne uyio ini keed ebọñ akam enọ Abasi, ete: “Abọọñ Andikara, afo akebot anyọñ ye isọñ ye akpainyañ ye afịd ñkpọ se iyọhọ ke esịd. <verse eid="ACT 4:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 4:25" />Ato ke Adisana Sịbidịd afo amaatañ ikọ ke inua isʌñutom mfo, ete ñnyịn Defid, abo ate:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:25">“ ‘Nsoo inam mme idịd eduọ abom,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:25">mme awo enyʌñ eduak ikpu-ikpu uduak?<verse eid="ACT 4:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 4:26" />Mme ndidem isọñ edaaña eda,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:26">ndin mme andikara eboho ammọ-ammọ</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:26">enyʌñ enwana ye Abọọñ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:26">ye anye e-emaekeyet adan<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4:26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho Mesaiya me Krais</char></note> enịm.’<verse eid="ACT 4:26" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 4:27" />Ado akpanikọ ke Herọd ye Pọntiọs Pailed emaesoobo atọ keed ye mme Gentile ye mbon Isrel ke abio ami nọ ediana keed enwana ye adisana ayịnutom mfo Yisọs, a-afo akeyette adan anịm. <verse eid="ACT 4:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 4:28" />Ammọ ekenam se adudu ye uduak mfo emaekebebiere enịm ebo atịppe. <verse eid="ACT 4:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 4:29" />Ndin idahami, Abọọñ, se baña udịkke ammọ idịkkeke ñnyịn nyʌñ nọ mme isʌñutom mfo adudu aditañ ikọ mfo ye ayọhọ uko. <verse eid="ACT 4:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 4:30" />Sio ubọk mfo nyan ke adikọk udọñọ, ye ke adinam mme ikpọ utom idiọọñọ ye mme utịppeñkpọ ñkpaidem ke anyịñ adisana isʌñutom mfo, Yisọs.”<verse eid="ACT 4:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 4:31" />Ke ammọ emaekebọñ akam ema, itie a-ammọ eketieghe amaanyeeñe, ndin afịd ammọ emaeyọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd, enyʌñ ekwọrọ ikọ Abasi uko-uko.<verse eid="ACT 4:31" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Andinịm ke Akpanikọ Ewuana Inie Ammọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 4:32" />Afịd mme andinịm ke akpanikọ ekenie esịd keed ye akikere keed. Ndomo awo keed ikibooho ke se imọ inie akedo akpọ-akpọ inie imọ, ado afịd awo ekewaawana afịd ñkpọ se ekenie. <verse eid="ACT 4:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 4:33" />Ke ayọhọ adudu, mme abọsịd emaekaa iso ke aditie ntiense mbaña adised Abọọñ Yisọs ke ñkpa. Ndin mfọn Abasi amaakem ammọ udeeme, <verse eid="ACT 4:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 4:34" />anam mbon unana ndomokeed ikibaaha ke atu ammọ. Sia ke ini ke ini, mbon se ikinieñe isọñ ye mme ufọk emaenyaam, ekoono akʌk se ikido ekọmudua <verse eid="ACT 4:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 4:35" />edinọ mme abọsịd, ndin emaesideeme enọ awo keedekeed akeene mfịna se awo akenie.<verse eid="ACT 4:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 4:36" />Yosef, awo Lifai a-aketooho Saiprọs, a-mme abọsịd ekekootto Banabas (a-awuọñọke “ayịn idọñesịd”), <verse eid="ACT 4:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 4:37" />amaanyam isọñ a-anye akenieghe anyʌñ aben akʌk ado akenịm ke ukod mme abọsịd.<verse eid="ACT 4:37" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="ACT 5" />
  <para style="s1">Ananayas ye Safira</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 5:1" />Ndin awo keed ekekoodo Ananayas ye anwaan amọ Safira, emaenyam isọñ ammọ ñko. <verse eid="ACT 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 5:2" />Ado Ananayas, ke ayọhọ unyịmme anwaan amọ, amaabakka ubaak akʌk isọñ ado anịm anọ idem amọ, ndin aben ubaak akenọ mme abọsịd.<verse eid="ACT 5:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 5:3" />Do ke Pita akebo anye, “Ananayas, asaña die ayak Setan anekke udʌk esịd tutu afo asʌhọ nsu anọ Adisana Sịbidịd, anyʌñ amʌm ubaak akʌk akenyamma isọñ anịm anọ idem mfo? <verse eid="ACT 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 5:4" />Nte isọñ ado ikidooho ake mfo naña awo imiikinyamma anye? Ndin ke emaekenyam anye, nte ukusʌkkọ unie unen adidat akʌk se ekenyam nnam naña afo ama? Nsoo ñkpọ ikinam nọ afo akere adinam utọ ñkpọ a-abaaha ntom? Afo usʌhọke nsu unọ awo kpọd, ado asʌhọ anọ Abasi.”<verse eid="ACT 5:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 5:5" />Ke Ananayas amaakekop mme ñkpọ ami, anye amaaduọ ke isọñ akpa. Ndin ekamba ndịk amaanam afịd mbon se ikikop ñkpọ ami. <verse eid="ACT 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 5:6" />Ndin mme ñkparawa emaedi ediben akpo amọ ewañ ke afọñ, eben ewuọ ekebuuk.<verse eid="ACT 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 5:7" />Ke ñkpọ nte awa ita amaakeboiyo, anwaan amọ amaadʌk adi, ado anye ikidiọọñọke se ikitịppe. <verse eid="ACT 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 5:8" />Ndin Pita amaabịp anye ate, “Tañ nnọ ise, udua a-ndufo ekenyamma isọñ ndufo ado ami?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 5:8">Safira amaabo, “Ii, ekọmudua isọñ ado adodo.”<verse eid="ACT 5:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 5:9" />Pita amaabo anye, “Nsinam nọ ndufo eda uyio keed edomo Sịbidịd Abọọñ idomo? Kpañ utọñ! Mbon se ikibuuk ebe mfo mmọdo eda ke inuausʌñ, ndin ammọ ñko eyauben fiin ewuọ.”<verse eid="ACT 5:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 5:10" />Kpa ke ukem ini ado anye amaaduọ anaa ke ukod Pita anyʌñ akpa. Ndin mme ñkparawa emaedʌk edi, edikịt ke anye akpa, enyʌñ eben anye ewuọ ekebuuk ediana ebe amọ. <verse eid="ACT 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 5:11" />Ekamba ndịk amaamʌm afịd ufọkabasi ye afịd mbon se ikikop ibaña mme ñkpọ ami.<verse eid="ACT 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mme Abọsịd Ekọk Uwak Awo Udọñọ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 5:12" />Mme abọsịd emaenam uwak idiọọñọ ye mme utịppeñkpọ ke atu mbon awo. Ndin afịd mme andinịm ke akpanikọ ekesisoobo ke Esa Sọlọmọn. <verse eid="ACT 5:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 5:13" />Awo ndomokeed mfen ikidʌkkọ atu ammọ, akpesʌkado mme awo ekenekkeke ekpono ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 5:14" />Ado ibad ideen ye ibaan se ikikeene ammọ inịm Abọọñ ke akpanikọ amaakaa iso atọt. <verse eid="ACT 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 5:15" />Ndin mme awo emaekoono mbon udọñọ ewuọñọ edi ke mme efaak, ebon ammọ ke ikʌk ye ke aya, nọ ato do naña nte akpedodo, ke ini Pita amaasaña aboiyo, ndukpọñ amọ akpesʌk atuuk ubaak ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 5:16" />Atu awo emaewuọñọ ñko ke mme abio se ikida ikpere Yeruselem edi, enyʌñ ekoono mbon udọñọ edi, ye mbon se ndedeghe sịbidịd eketʌkkọ, ndin afịd ammọ emaekop nsọñidem.<verse eid="ACT 5:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọbọ mme Abọsịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 5:17" />Ndin ekamba aku ye afịd mme nsaña amọ e-ekebaaha ke ñka mme Sadusi emaeyọhọ ye ufịb. <verse eid="ACT 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 5:18" />Ammọ emaemʌm mme abọsịd, enyʌñ edọñ ammọ ke ufọk ñkpakọb afịd awo. <verse eid="ACT 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 5:19" />Ado ke akonayio, enyere Abọọñ amaataat mme usʌñ ufọk ñkpakọb, asịññe ammọ asuuk, <verse eid="ACT 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 5:20" />anyʌñ abo ammọ, “Ikaa ikida ke mme afe tembịd inyʌñ itañ inọ mme awo afịd ikọ a-abañake ufa uwem ami.”<verse eid="ACT 5:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 5:21" />Ke ammọ emaekekop ado, ammọ emaedʌk mme afe tembịd ke usiere, enyʌñ etọọñọ adikpeep mme awo ñkpọ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 5:21">Ke ini ekamba aku ye mme nsaña amọ emaekedisịm, ammọ emaekoot mme esob Sanhidrin mme Yuu, a-adooho ayọhọ mbono afịd mme ñkpisọñ Isrel, enyʌñ edọñ ebo eka ekesịññe mme abọsịd ke ufọk ñkpakọb edi. <verse eid="ACT 5:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 5:22" />Ado ke mme isʌñutom emaekekewuọ ufọk ñkpakọb, mme adaaha ikikịtte mme abọsịd do. Ndin ammọ emaetịmme enyọñ ekedọkkọ ammọ ete, <verse eid="ACT 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 5:23" />“Ñnyịn imikikịt ufọk ñkpakọb nte asʌk abebere, ye mme akpeme ufọk ñkpakọb naña eda ke mme inuausʌñ, ado ke ñnyịn imaikibeede usʌñ, ñnyịn ikikịtte awo ndomokeed ke esịd ufọk.” <verse eid="ACT 5:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 5:24" />Ke mme akamautom ke tembịd ye mme akpeme ufọk ñkpakọb ye mme ñkpoon aku emaekekop etob ami, ammọ ikidiọọñọke se ekpenam, idem amaanyʌñ akpa ammọ abaña se utọ ñkpọ ami akpewuọñọ.<verse eid="ACT 5:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 5:25" />Akema, awo keed amaadi adibo ammọ ate, “Se! Mbon a-ndufo ekedọññọ ke ufọk ñkpakọb mmọ ko eda ke mme afe tembịd esʌk ekpeep mme awo ñkpọ.” <verse eid="ACT 5:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 5:26" />Ke adaiwuod ekọñ ye mme adaaha utom amọ emaekekop ami, ammọ emaeka ekeben mme abọsịd edi. Ado ammọ ikinamma ke afai mbaak mbon awo editọọñ ammọ ke itiad.<verse eid="ACT 5:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 5:27" />Emaeben mme abọsịd edʌk edi enyʌñ enam ammọ eda ke iso esob Sanhidrin mme Yuu, nọ ekamba aku abiime ammọ mbuume. <verse eid="ACT 5:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 5:28" />Anye amaabo ammọ ate: “Ñnyịn imainekke iwuuk ite ndufo ikiikpeep ñkpọ aba ke anyịñ ami, ado ndufo emenam ukpeebñkpọ ndufo akara afịd isọñ Yeruselem, enyʌñ ebeeñe idem adinam iyiib awo ami idodo ñnyịn ke idem.”<verse eid="ACT 5:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 5:29" />Pita ye mme abọsịd mbon ako emaebọọrọ ete: “Ñnyịn inie adikop uyio Abasi, idooho uyio awo! <verse eid="ACT 5:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 5:30" />Abasi mme ete ñnyịn amaanam Yisọs a-ndufo ekewotto ke adikọñ anye ke krọs aset ke ñkpa. <verse eid="ACT 5:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 5:31" />Abasi amaabenne anye anịm ke ubọk nnasia amọ nte Akpan Abọọñ ye Andinyaaña nọ anye anam Isrel ekappa esịd, anye ñko anyʌñ afeen mme idiọọkñkpọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 5:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 5:32" />Ñnyịn ido mme ntiense ibaña mme ñkpọ ami, ntoro ñko ke Adisana Sịbidịd ado, a-Abasi anọọhọ mbon e-ekoppo uyio amọ.”<verse eid="ACT 5:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 5:33" />Ke ammọ emaekekop mme ikọ ami, esịd amaayat ammọ eti-eti, ndin ammọ emaeyem adiwot mme abọsịd. <verse eid="ACT 5:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 5:34" />Ado awo Farisi keed a-akekereke Kamaliel, akpeeb mbed, a-afịd awo ekekponoke, amaadakka ada ke esob Sanhidrin anyʌñ anọ uyio ate enam mme abọsịd ewuọñọ diin ekebet etək ke anwa esiin. <verse eid="ACT 5:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 5:35" />Ndin anye amaabo mbon esob Sanhidrin ate: “Ndufo mbon Isrel, inekke ikere ibaña se ndufo eduak adinam ye ibon ami. <verse eid="ACT 5:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 5:36" />Ke usen edem, Tiudas amaadakka ada, adat idem amọ nte awuọiso awo, ndin ñkpọ nte awo ikie inaañ emaewuọñọ ekeene anye. Emaewot anye, ndin afịd mme mbed amọ emaenyʌñ esuana; ke akpatre afịd ñkpọ se anye akenam akewuọñọ ikpu-ikpu. <verse eid="ACT 5:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 5:37" />Ke Tiudas amaakekpa, Yudas a-aketooho Kalili amaawuọ adi ke ini ekenamma ubadawo, anyʌñ akoono uwak awo e-ekedianake ye anye esịn ntịme ke abio. Emaewot anye ñko, ndin afịd mme mbed amọ emaesuana. <verse eid="ACT 5:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 5:38" />Ndin idahami, ami mmenọ item mbo yak ndufo esịññe idem ekpọñ ibon ami! Isaana ammọ iyaak nọ enyọñọ! Sia akpedo uduak ye adinam ammọ ato awo, ayaakpu. <verse eid="ACT 5:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 5:39" />Ado akpedo se ammọ enam ato Abasi, ndufo idiikanna ikpan ammọ, utu ke ado ndufo ediikappa inwana ye Abasi.”<verse eid="ACT 5:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 5:40" />Ammọ emaekop ikọ se Kamaliel aketañ. Ke ntoro emaekoot mme abọsịd edi, enyʌñ enam emia ammọ. Ndin emaenọ ammọ uyio ete ammọ ekuukpeep ñkpọ aba ke anyịñ Yisọs, enyʌñ esaana ammọ eyaak.<verse eid="ACT 5:40" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 5:41" />Mme abọsịd emaekpọñ esob Sanhidrin, edaara sia emaebat ammọ nte mbon e-edotto adidia abuud ke ntak anyịñ Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 5:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 5:42" />Ke usen ke usen, ke mme afe tembịd ye ke ufọk ke ufọk, ammọ ikitreke adikpeep ye adikwọrọ eti mbʌk mbo ke Yisọs ado Krais.<verse eid="ACT 5:42" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="ACT 6" />
  <para style="s1">Umek Awo Itiaba</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 6:1" />Ke mme usen ado, nte ibad mme mbed e-ekekeeneke Krais akesʌkkọ atọt, mme Yuu<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Mme Yuu ake ekesemme usem Greek enyʌñ edu eduuwem mbon Greek.</char></note> e-ekesemme usem Greek emaesuuk mme Yuu ukañ Hibru uyio sia ammọ ikiseeghe ñkpọ ibaña mme ebekpa ammọ ke ini udeeme ndidia. <verse eid="ACT 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 6:2" />Ndin mme mbed duob mme iba emaesoobo itie keed ye mbon se ikeene Krais enyʌñ ebo, “Ikpifọnnọ ñnyịn adikpọñ utom ikọ Abasi nnịm ñkappa ñkedeeme ndidia. <verse eid="ACT 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 6:3" />Nditọeka ke Krais, imek ideen itiaba ke atu ndufo e-eyọhọke ye Adisana Sịbidịd ye aniọñ. Ñnyịn iyaiyaak utom ami isịn ammọ ke ubọk, <verse eid="ACT 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 6:4" />ndin ñnyịn iyaitʌm ise akpan utom ñnyịn adooho ubọñ akam ye ukwọrọ ikọ Abasi.”<verse eid="ACT 6:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 6:5" />Akikere ami amaanem afịd atu awo esịd. Ndin ammọ emaemek Stifịn, awo a-akeyọhọke ye mbuọdidem ye Adisana Sịbidịd; ñko Filib, Prokorus, Nikanọ, Timọn, Pamenas ye Nikolas awo Antiọk, a-akekappake esịd akeene edu ukpono Abasi ke ido mme Yuu. <verse eid="ACT 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 6:6" />Ammọ emaeben ideen itiaba ami enịm mme abọsịd ke iso, ndin ammọ emaebọñ akam enyʌñ edot ammọ ubọk.<verse eid="ACT 6:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 6:7" />Ndin ikọ Abasi amaakaa iso asuana. Ibad mme mbed ke Yeruselem amaatọt eti-eti, ndin uwak mme aku Abasi emaenyʌñ esuuk iwuod enọ mbuọdidem ke Yisọs.<verse eid="ACT 6:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emʌm Stifịn</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 6:8" />Ndin Stifịn, awo a-akeyọhọke ye mfọn ye adudu Abasi amaanañña ikpọ utịppeñkpọ ye utom idiọọñọ ke ufọọd atu awo. <verse eid="ACT 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 6:9" />Ado mfịna ye utọk amaatọọñọ, ato mbon Sinakọk Mbon Uwuọufʌn (nte naña ekesikoot ammọ), e-ekedoññoke mme Yuu e-eketooho Siriin ye Aleksandra, ñkọrọ mbon Silisia ye Esia, e-ekedaañake eda etọọñọ mfaaña ye Stifịn. <verse eid="ACT 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 6:10" />Ado ammọ ikikanna anye ke ifiọk a-Sịbidịd akenọọhọ anye idaha anye aketañña ikọ.<verse eid="ACT 6:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 6:11" />Ke ntoro ammọ emaedọọñ mme awo ke ndịbe, nọ ekebo, “Ñnyịn imikop naña Stifịn atañ ikọ asappa adian Moses ye Abasi.”<verse eid="ACT 6:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 6:12" />Ndin ammọ emaesịn nsọk, enam esịd abịmme mbon abio, mme ñkpisọñ, ye mme akpeeb mbed. Ammọ emaekpappa Stifịn edat edi esob Sanhidrin. <verse eid="ACT 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 6:13" />Ndin ammọ emaesio mme atie ntiense nsu e-ekebooho ete, “Akenam awo ami itreke aditañ idiọọk ikọ ndian adisana itie ami ye mbed Moses. <verse eid="ACT 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 6:14" />Sia ñnyịn imaikop naña anye abo ke Yisọs ayịn Nasared ayaabiat itie ami anyʌñ akpəho mme ido ake Moses akeyaaha inọọ ñnyịn.”<verse eid="ACT 6:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 6:15" />Afịd awo e-eketieghe ke esob Sanhidrin emaewuuk anyen ese Stifịn, enyʌñ ekịt ke iso amọ akebit iso enyere.<verse eid="ACT 6:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="ACT 7" />
  <para style="s1">Ikọ a-Stifịn Aketañña Anọ Esob Sanhidrin</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 7:1" />Ndin ekamba aku amaabịp Stifịn abo, “Se etañ ami udian fiin ado akpanikọ?”<verse eid="ACT 7:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 7:2" />Anye amaabọọrọ: “Nditọeka ye mme ete, ikpañ utọñ innọ miin! Ubọọñ Abasi amaayaara anọ ete ñnyịn Ebraham, ke ini anye akesʌkkọ aba ke Mesopotemia, mbemiso anye akedʌñ ke Haran. <verse eid="ACT 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 7:3" />Abasi amaabo anye ate, ‘Kpọñ idʌñ mfo ye mbon mfo, nyʌñ kaa ke isọñ a-nduuwọt fiin.’ <verse eid="ACT 7:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 7:4" />“Ndin anye amaakpọñ isọñ mbon Kaldi akaa akedʌñ ke Haran. Ke ete amọ amaakekpa, Abasi amaanọ anye akaa abio a-ndufo edʌññọ mfịn ami. <verse eid="ACT 7:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 7:5" />Abasi ikinọọhọ anye udeeme amọ mi, ukpọk etək itie isọñ se anye awuuk ñkpad. Ado Abasi amaanwọñọ abo ke anye ye ubon amọ eyaedat isọñ ado enie, akpesʌkado Ebraham imiikinieghe ayịn idahado. <verse eid="ACT 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 7:6" />Ntom ke Abasi aketañ ikọ anọ anye abo: ‘Ke isua ikie inaañ, mme ubon mfo ediido isenawo ke idʌñ i-imiidooho ake ammọ, ñko eyaesịn ammọ ufʌn, enyʌñ etʌkkọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 7:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 7:7" />Abasi abo: Ado ami ñyaamia idịd a-ammọ enamma ñkpọ enọ nte ifʌn ufen;’ ndin ke ado amaaboiyo, ammọ eyaewuọñọ ke idịd ado enyʌñ ediñkpono miin ke itie ami. <verse eid="ACT 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 7:8" />Ndin anye amaanọ Ebraham edioomo ufọọrọ edʌd. Akema Ebraham amaabon Aisik, anyʌñ afọọrọ anye edʌd ke ayọhọ usen itiaita. Aisik amaanyʌñ abon Yekọb, Yekọb anyʌñ adikappa ado ete anọ mme nsọbom ñnyịn duob mme iba.<verse eid="ACT 7:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 7:9" />“Sia mme nsọbom ami ekefịbeke Yosef ufịb, ammọ emaenyam anye nte afʌn enọ Iyib. Ado Abasi amaaba ye anye, <verse eid="ACT 7:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 7:10" />anyʌñ anyaaña anye asio ke afịd mfịna amọ. Abasi amaanọ Yosef ifiọk anyʌñ anam anye akịt mfọn ke iso Fero, adidem Iyib. Ndin Fero amaanam anye ado andikara Iyib ye afịd ufọk amọ.<verse eid="ACT 7:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 7:11" />“Akem akañ amaadidʌk afịd isọñ Iyib ye Kenan, adat ekamba ukuud adi, ndin mme eteete ñnyịn ikinieghe ndidia se edia. <verse eid="ACT 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 7:12" />Yekọb akekop ke abakpa amaaba ke Iyib, anye amaasio mme eteete ñnyịn adọñ akpa ini. <verse eid="ACT 7:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 7:13" />Ke etịmmeke eka, Yosef amaakeyaara idem amọ anọ nditọete amọ, ndin Fero amaadidiọọñọ ñkpọ abaña ubon Yosef. <verse eid="ACT 7:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 7:14" />Ke ami aboiyoke, Yosef amaadọñ ate ekeben ete amọ, Yekọb, ye afịd ufọk amọ e-ekedooho awo ata mme duob mme ition edi. <verse eid="ACT 7:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 7:15" />Ndin Yekọb amaaben isañ akaa Iyib. Do ke anye ye mme eteete ñnyịn ekekekpañña. <verse eid="ACT 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 7:16" />Emaekoono akpo ammọ etịmme edi Sekem edibuuk ke udi e-Ebraham akedeppe ato nditọ Hamọ ke ekọmudua.<verse eid="ACT 7:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 7:17" />“Ke ini a-Abasi akenwọñọke anọ Ebraham akedikpereke, ibad nditọ ñnyịn ke Iyib emaetọt eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 7:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 7:18" />Akem ufa adidem, a-Yosef imiikidooho ñkpọ ndomokeed inọ anye, amaadida ukara ke Iyib. <verse eid="ACT 7:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 7:19" />Anye akedu uwem ñkara-ñkara ye ikọd ñnyịn anyʌñ atʌkkọ mme eteete ñnyịn, anam ammọ etoomo mme ufa nsek nditọ e-ekemanake eduọọñọ nọ ekekpañña.<verse eid="ACT 7:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 7:20" />“Ke ini ado ke Moses akemana, ado anye ikidooho ñkaña ayịn, akedo asaña-asaña ayịn ke iso Abasi. Ete ye eka amọ ekebọọk anye ke ufọk ammọ ke ñkpọ nte afiọñ ita. <verse eid="ACT 7:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 7:21" />Ke emaekesio anye enịm ke anwaesiin, adiaha Fero amaaben anye abọọk, akama anye nte ayịn amọ. <verse eid="ACT 7:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 7:22" />Moses amaabọ ukpeebñkpọ ke afịd usʌñ ifiọk nditọ Iyib, anyʌñ akappa ado akpọsọñ awo ke ikọ inua ye ke edu unam ñkpọ.<verse eid="ACT 7:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 7:23" />“Ke ini Moses amaakeyọhọ isua aba ke emana, anye amaabiide ke esịd amọ adika ñkese nditọete amọ, nditọ Isrel. <verse eid="ACT 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 7:24" />Anye akekịt naña ayịn Iyib keed afʌnnọ ayịn ammọ keed, anye amaakaa adinyaaña anye, ndin amaawot ayịn Iyib ke usiene anọ awo ammọ e-ekefʌnnọke. <verse eid="ACT 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 7:25" />Moses akekere ke mbon amọ eyaediọọñọ ke Abasi akikama imọ anyaaña ammọ, ado ammọ ikidiọọñọke ntoro. <verse eid="ACT 7:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 7:26" />Edem usen, Moses amaakịt nditọ Isrel iba naña enwana anwan. Anye amaanwana adisịn emem nnọọ ammọ ke adibo: ‘Ukañ ñnyịn, ndufo edo nditọeka; ntak a-ndufo eyemme inam emọ-emọ ibak-a?’<verse eid="ACT 7:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 7:27" />“Ado awodeen andikinam ntịme ye awodeen anye ako amaanək Moses asio, abo anye, ‘Anie awo ikumek fiin andikara ye abiideikpe inọọ ñnyịn? <verse eid="ACT 7:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 7:28" />Ayem adiñwot miin naña akewot awo Iyib ñkpọñ a-akeboiyoke?’ <verse eid="ACT 7:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 7:29" />Moses akekop ami, anye amaafeghe akedʌñ ke abio Midian nte asenawo anyʌñ abon nditọ ideen iba do.<verse eid="ACT 7:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 7:30" />“Ke isua aba amaakeboiyo, enyere Abasi amaayaara idem awọt Moses ke edemeikañ a-aketaaha ikọd ke akpautatan a-akekpereke Abod Sainai. <verse eid="ACT 7:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 7:31" />Moses akekịt ami, idem amaakpa anye. Ndin anye akesaña akpere adikinekke nse utọ utịppe ñkpọ ami, anye amaakop uyio Abọọñ naña abo: <verse eid="ACT 7:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 7:32" />‘Ami ndo Abasi mme eteete mfo, Abasi Ebraham, Aisik ye Yekọb.’ Idem amaanyeñ Moses, ndịk amaamʌm anye, anye ikideeghede idomo adise aba.<verse eid="ACT 7:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 7:33" />“Akem Abọọñ amaabo anye ate, ‘Sịññe ikpaukod mfo ke ukod, sia itie a-afo adaaha do ado adisana isọñ. <verse eid="ACT 7:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 7:34" />Ke akpanikọ, ami mmekịt naña efʌnnọ ikọd mmi ke Iyib. Mmekop ñkuun ammọ, anam mmedi adisio ammọ ke ukuud. Di idahami, ami ñyaudọñ fiin atịmme akaa Iyib.’<verse eid="ACT 7:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 7:35" />“Kpasʌk Moses a-ammọ ekesịnne do ado ami, e-ekebooho, ‘Anie awo ikumek fiin andikara ye abiideikpe?’ Kpa Moses ado ke Abasi akedọñ enyere a-akewọttọ anye idem ke ikọd ado ate anye akedo andikara ye andinyaaña nditọ Isrel. <verse eid="ACT 7:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 7:36" />Anye amaadat ammọ awuọ ke isọñ Iyib anyʌñ anañña mme utịppeñkpọ ye utom idiọọñọ ke Iyib, ke Ndad-ndad Akpainyañ ye anaan ke isua aba.<verse eid="ACT 7:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 7:37" />“Anye asʌk ado kpa Moses ado a-akebooho nditọ Isrel, ‘Abasi ayaasio prọfed a-abaaha nte ami ke atu ndufo inọ ndufo.’ <verse eid="ACT 7:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 7:38" />Anye akeba ke mbono ke anaan ye enyere a-akenemeke nneme ye anye ke Abod Sainai, ye mme eteete ñnyịn, anyʌñ abọ aduuwem ikọ isọk ñnyịn.<verse eid="ACT 7:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 7:39" />“Ado mme eteete ñnyịn ikikoppo uyio amọ. Utu ke do, ammọ emaesịn anye, ndin ke esịd ammọ, emaetịmme ekaa Iyib. <verse eid="ACT 7:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 7:40" />Ammọ emaebo Erọn, ‘Bot mme abasi mfen e-ediidat ñnyịn usʌñ. Amaado awo ami, Moses, a-akidatta ñnyịn usʌñ awuọ ke isọñ Iyib, ñnyịn idiọọñọke se itịppe inọ anye!’ <verse eid="ACT 7:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 7:41" />Ini ado ke ammọ ekenam ubobodñkpọ ke mbid abaakenañ. Ammọ emaewa uwa enọ anye, enyʌñ enam usọrọ adidat ñkpono se ubọk ammọ akebot. <verse eid="ACT 7:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 7:42" />Ado Abọọñ amaawọññọ iso akpọñ ammọ anyʌñ anam ammọ ekappa ekpono mme udịm anyọñ nte utịn, afiọñ ye mme ntantaafiọñ, nte Abasi ammọ. Ami asaña akekem ke se ewet ke ñwed mme prọfed ebo:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:42">“ ‘Ubon Isrel, nte ndufo emaekoono uwa ye mme enọ ensọk miin,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:42">ke isua aba a-ndufo ekebaaha ke anaan?<verse eid="ACT 7:42" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 7:43" />Ndufo emedịppe atayad Mọlek</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">ye ntantaafiọñ abasi ndufo Refan,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">ye mme ñkpọ a-ndufo ekebotto ebon ekpono.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:43">Ndin ami ñyaibịne ndufo nsịññe ke abio tutu ndufo esuana ebọhọ Babilọn.’<verse eid="ACT 7:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 7:44" />“Mme eteete ñnyịn emaenie atayad edioomo mbed enwọñọ ke ini ammọ ekebaaha ke anaan. Ekebọp anye naña Abasi aketemme Moses akeene mbid se anye akekịt. <verse eid="ACT 7:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 7:45" />Atayad ami amaakaa iso aboiyo ke ubọk mme eteete ñnyịn tutu Yọsua akeben anye adʌk isọñ mme idịd a-Abasi akebịneke asiooño ke iso ammọ. Do ke atayad ado akeba tutu asịm ukara Defid, <verse eid="ACT 7:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 7:46" />a-akekịtte mfọn Abasi anyʌñ abeeñe Abasi abo ayak nọ imọ ibọp itieidʌñ inọ Abasi Yekọb.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7:46 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ñkaan ikpañwed ewet </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">ufọk Yekọb</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 7:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 7:47" />Ado Sọlọmọn akekappa abọp ufọk ado anọ Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 7:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 7:48" />“Ado, Abasi Andikoñ Ñkan idʌññọ ke ufọk u-ubọk awo abọppọ. Nte prọfed abooho:<verse eid="ACT 7:48" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="ACT 7:49" />“ ‘Hefịn ado ebekpo mmi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">isọñ anyʌñ ado udodukod mmi.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:49">Nsoo utọ ufọk ke afo uduubọp unnọ miin?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">Abọọñ abo.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">Itie nduọkadudu mmi adiiba ke ñke?<verse eid="ACT 7:49" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="ACT 7:50" />Idooho ubọk mmi akenañña afịd mme ñkpọ ami?’<verse eid="ACT 7:50" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="ACT 7:51" />“Ndufo mbon nsọñiwuod! Esịd ye utọñ ndufo asʌk adodoro ufiọọn. Ndufo enyʌñ eba nte mme eteete ndufo: Esʌk ebọọbiọñọ Adisana Sịbidịd afịd ini! <verse eid="ACT 7:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="ACT 7:52" />Akee prọfed ke mme eteete ndufo imiikikọbọke? Ado ammọ ekekap ewot mbon e-ekeyaarake adidi Adinen Ayịn Awo. Idahami, ndufo emetap anye enyʌñ ewot anye, <verse eid="ACT 7:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="ACT 7:53" />ndufo e-ekebọọhọ mbed eto mme enyere, ekap edo mbon i-imiinamma se mbed abo enam.”<verse eid="ACT 7:53" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Etọọñ Stifịn ke Itiad</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="ACT 7:54" />Mbon esob Sanhidrin ekekop ami, ammọ emaekop akpọsọñ ifiobesịd enyʌñ ekwaaha ntak eded ese anye. <verse eid="ACT 7:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="ACT 7:55" />Ado Stifịn, a-akeyọhọke ye Adisana Sịbidịd, amaawuuk anyen ase hefịn anyʌñ akịt ubọọñ Abasi, ye naña Yisọs ada ke ubọk nnasia Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 7:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="ACT 7:56" />Anye amaabo ate, “Ami mmekịt naña hefịn abeere ye naña Ayịn Awo ada ke ubọk nnasia Abasi.”<verse eid="ACT 7:56" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="ACT 7:57" />Ke ammọ ekekoppo ikọ ami, ammọ emaesiit ubọk ke utọñ, ebọñ ñkpo ke akpọsọñ uyio, afịd ammọ enyʌñ ebịmme ebịne anye emʌm, <verse eid="ACT 7:57" /><verse number="58" style="v" sid="ACT 7:58" />edʌt anye esio ke abio, enyʌñ eketọọñ anye ke itiad. Ndin mme ntiense emaebon afọñ ammọ ke iso akparawa keed a-akekereke Sọọl.<verse eid="ACT 7:58" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" sid="ACT 7:59" />Ke idaha a-ammọ ekesʌkkọ etọọñ anye ke itiad, Stifịn amaabọñ akam abo ate, “Abọọñ Yisọs, bọ sịbidịd mmi.” <verse eid="ACT 7:59" /><verse number="60" style="v" sid="ACT 7:60" />Ndin anye amaatọọñọ edọñ anyʌñ abọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio ate, “Abọọñ, kuudat idiọọkñkpọ ami udot ammọ ke iwuod.” Anye aketañ ami ama, amaakpa.<verse eid="ACT 7:60" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="ACT 8" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 8:1" />Sọọl amaaba ke itie ado anyʌñ anyịmme ate ewot Stifịn.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="ACT 8:1">Ukọbọ A-akesuanna Ufọkabasi</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 8:1">Ke usen ado ataa ekamba ukọbọ amaatọọñọ abaña ufọkabasi ke Yeruselem, ndin emaesuan afịd awo edọñ ke ukañ Yudia ye Sameria ibọhọke mme abọsịd. <verse eid="ACT 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 8:2" />Mme nti awo emaekeben Stifịn ebuuk enyʌñ efʌhọ anye eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 8:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 8:3" />Ado Sọọl amaatọọñọ akọbọ ufọkabasi, asaña ke ufọk ke ufọk, amuum ibaan ye ideen adọñ ke ufọk ñkpakọb.<verse eid="ACT 8:3" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Filib Akaa Sameria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 8:4" />Mbon e-ekefeeñeke emaekekwọrọ ikọ Abasi ke mme itie nte ammọ ekekaiya. <verse eid="ACT 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 8:5" />Ndin Filib amaakaa abio Sameria keed akekwọrọ eti etob Krais ke udo. <verse eid="ACT 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 8:6" />Ke ini mme atu awo emaekekop ikọ Filib enyʌñ ekịt mme utom idiọọñọ a-anye akenamma, ammọ emaenekke ekpañ utọñ ekop se anye aketañ. <verse eid="ACT 8:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 8:7" />Mme ndedeghe sịbidịd emaetuaña, ewuọñọ mme awo ke idem; mbon akpaubeñ ye mbʌñọ emaenyʌñ ekop nsọñidem. <verse eid="ACT 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 8:8" />Ndin akpọsọñ idaara amaaba ke abio ado.<verse eid="ACT 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Saimọn a-Adooho Abiamfa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 8:9" />Ke ñkpọ nte ufañ ini ifañ, amaaba awo a-akekereke Saimọn, a-akesikamake ndedeghe sịbidịd anañña mme utịppeñkpọ nọ idem akpa afịd awo ke abio Sameria. Anye amaasiwọk inua ke imọ iminekke inie se ido, <verse eid="ACT 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 8:10" />ndin afịd awo, ñkpoon ye ntək, emaenịm anye ke akpanikọ enyʌñ ebo ete, “Asʌk adot se ekoot awo ami Akwa Adudu Abasi.” <verse eid="ACT 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 8:11" />Uwak mbon awo emaekeene anye sia ke anyan ini mme utịppeñkpọ amọ emaesikpa ammọ idem eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 8:12" />Ado ke ini ammọ emaekenịm eti etob abioubọọñ Abasi ye anyịñ Yisọs Krais, a-Filib akekwọrọke ke akpanikọ, ammọ emaebọ uduọkmmọọñ, ideen ye ibaan. <verse eid="ACT 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 8:13" />Saimọn ke idem amọ amaanịm ke akpanikọ anyʌñ abọ uduọkmmọọñ. Anye amaakeene Filib akaa afịd itie, idem amaanyʌñ akpa anye ke adikịt mme ikpọ utom idiọọñọ ye utịppeñkpọ e-ekedatta itie.<verse eid="ACT 8:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 8:14" />Ke ini mme abọsịd e-ekebaaha ke Yeruselem ekekoppo ke mbon Sameria emaebọ ikọ Abasi, ammọ emaenọ Pita ye Yọọn eka do. <verse eid="ACT 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 8:15" />Ke ammọ emaekekewuọ, ammọ emaebọñ akam enọ ufa mme andinịm Abasi ke akpanikọ nọ ammọ ebọ Adisana Sịbidịd, <verse eid="ACT 8:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 8:16" />sia Adisana Sịbidịd ikisọiyọke idoro awo ndomokeed do diin, ke ntak ekenịmme ammọ uduọkmmọọñ ke anyịñ Abọọñ Yisọs ikpọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 8:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 8:17" />Pita ye Yọọn emaedot ammọ ubọk, ndin ammọ emaebọ Adisana Sịbidịd.<verse eid="ACT 8:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 8:18" />Saimọn akekịt ke aketo ke mme abọsịd adidot mme awo ubọk ke mbon Sameria ekebọọ Adisana Sịbidịd, anye amaanọ mme abọsịd akʌk, <verse eid="ACT 8:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 8:19" />anyʌñ abo ate, “Innọ miin ukem adudu ami ñko nọ mbon se ami ndot ubọk ebọ Adisana Sịbidịd.”<verse eid="ACT 8:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 8:20" />Pita amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Yak akʌk mfo atak ye afo, sia afo akere abo ke imikeme idep enọ Abasi ke akʌk! <verse eid="ACT 8:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 8:21" />Afo unieghe itie me udeeme ke iso utom ami, sia esịd mfo inenne ke iso Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 8:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 8:22" />Kappa esịd kpọñ ibak uwem nyʌñ bọñ akam nọ Abọọñ. Akeme ido anye ayaafeen unọ fiin ke afo adinie utọ idiọọk akikere ado ke esịd mfo. <verse eid="ACT 8:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 8:23" />Sia ami mmekịt ke afo asịne ke ukad idiọọkesịd ye idiọọkñkpọ.”<verse eid="ACT 8:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 8:24" />Ndin Saimọn amaabọọrọ ate, “Bọñ akam nọ Abọọñ nnọ miin mbaak ñkpọ ndomokeed ke atu se afo atañ ami aditịppe innọọ miin.”<verse eid="ACT 8:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 8:25" />Ke ini ammọ emaekemaana enọ ikọ ntiense ebaña Yisọs enyʌñ ekwọrọ ikọ Abọọñ ema, Pita ye Yọọn emaetịmme ekaa Yeruselem, ekekwọrọ eti etob ke uwak esịd idʌñ Sameria.<verse eid="ACT 8:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Filib ye Awo Etiopia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 8:26" />Ndin enyere Abọọñ amaabo Filib, “Kaa ke usuuk usʌñ akpautatan a-atooho Yeruselem akewuọ Kasa.” <verse eid="ACT 8:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 8:27" />Filib amaadakka isañ, ndin ke usʌñ anye amaakịt itọ a-aketooho Etiopia. Anye akedo ekamba akamautom a-akeseeghe ñkpọ abaña afịd akʌk anọ Kandake, abọọñanwaan Etiopia. Itọ ami akeka adikpono Abasi ke Yeruselem, <verse eid="ACT 8:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 8:28" />ndin ke unyọñọ ufọk anye amaatie ke sariọd amọ asʌk akoot ñwed prọfed Aisaiya. <verse eid="ACT 8:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 8:29" />Ndin Sịbidịd Abasi amaabo Filib, “Saña kpere sariọd ako nyʌñ ke da diana anye.”<verse eid="ACT 8:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 8:30" />Naña Filib akefegheke abịne sariọd, anye amaakop naña awo Etiopia asʌk akoot ñwed prọfed Aisaiya. Filib amaabịp anye abo, “Se afo akoot unwaña?”<verse eid="ACT 8:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 8:31" />Anye amaabọọrọ, “Akeme die adiñnwaña miin ibọhọke awo anam nọ añnwaña?” Do ndin ke anye akebo Filib adọọk aditie ye imọ.<verse eid="ACT 8:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 8:32" />Itie ñwed Abasi i-itọ ado akekoodo ado ami:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 8:32">“Ekedʌt anye nte edọñ ekaa itie esiwotto unam,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:32">nte ñyịn edọñ imiisioho uyio ke iso mbon se ikwaat anye ided,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:32">kpa ntoro ñko anye ikikʌppọke inua amọ.<verse eid="ACT 8:32" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 8:33" />Emaebọ anye unen enyʌñ esuenne anye.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:33">Anie awo ikan itañ ibaña nditọ-nditọ amọ?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:33">Sia emaekpịkke uwem amọ esio ke ederimbod.”<verse eid="ACT 8:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 8:34" />Itọ Etiopia ami amaabịp Filib abo, “Mbọk tañ nnọ ise, anie awo ke prọfed ami atañ abaña, idem amọ me awo mfen?” <verse eid="ACT 8:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 8:35" />Ndin Filib amaatọọñọ ke itie ñwed Abasi ado anyʌñ akwọrọ eti etob Yisọs anọ anye.<verse eid="ACT 8:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 8:36" />Naña ammọ ekesʌkkọ eka ke usʌñ, ammọ emaediwuọ itie a-mmọọñ akebaaha, ndin itọ ado amaabo, “Se mmọọñ mi. Nsoo ikpido ubiọọñọ ami adibọ uduọkmmọọñ?”<verse eid="ACT 8:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 8:37" />Filib amaabo anye, “Adieke afo anịmme ke afịd esịd mfo, amekeme.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 8:37">Itọ ado amaabọọrọ ate, “Ami mmenịm ke akpanikọ nte ke Yisọs ado Ayịn Abasi.” <verse eid="ACT 8:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 8:38" />Ndin anye amaanọ uyio ate awad a-sariọd atuak ada. Do ndin Filib ye itọ emaesọiyọ edọñọ mmọọñ, ndin Filib amaanịm anye uduọkmmọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 8:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 8:39" />Ammọ ekewuọñọ ke mmọọñ edi, Sịbidịd Abọọñ amaaben Filib adakka, itọ ado ikinyʌññọ ikịt Filib aba, ado amaanyọñ ke idaara. <verse eid="ACT 8:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 8:40" />Ndin Filib amaakewuọ Asotus, anyʌñ akaa iso ke isañ amọ, akwọrọ eti etob ke afịd idʌñ tutu akesịm Siseria.<verse eid="ACT 8:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="ACT 9" />
  <para style="s1">Sọọl Akappa Esịd</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 9:1" />Ado Sọọl akesʌk akaka iso ke adikọbọ ye adidịkke mme mbed Abọọñ uwem. Anye amaadakka abịne ekamba aku <verse eid="ACT 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 9:2" />akebo inọ imọ ñwed nọ iben ika mme sinakọk ke Damaskọs nọ ato do adieke akịtte awo ndomokeed do a-asañake ke usʌñ Krais, adooho awonwaan me awodeen, anye akoono ammọ ñkpọnọ anyọñ Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 9:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 9:3" />Ke anye amaakesaña akpere Damaskọs, unwana ikañ amaato hefịn idaha-idaha ado ayamma akanna anye akʌk. <verse eid="ACT 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 9:4" />Anye amaaduọ ke isọñ, anyʌñ akop uyio naña abo anye ate: <char style="wj">“Sọọl, Sọọl, nsoo ido ntak a-afo añkọbọke miin?”</char><verse eid="ACT 9:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 9:5" />Sọọl amaabịp abo, “Afo ado anie, Abọọñ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 9:5">Abọọñ amaabọọrọ, <char style="wj">“Ami ndo Yisọs a-afo akọbọke.</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 9:6" /><char style="wj">Dakka da, nyʌñ saña dʌk esịd abio, ndin eyautemme se ana nte anam.”</char><verse eid="ACT 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 9:7" />Mbon se ikisaña ye Sọọl emaeda ikanna uyio isio; ammọ emaekop uyio, ado ikikịtte awo ndomokeed. <verse eid="ACT 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 9:8" />Sọọl amaadakka ada ke isọñ, ado ke anye amaaketaat anyen, ikikanna ikịt ñkpọ ndomokeed aba. Ke ntoro, emaemʌm anye ubọk eben ekaa Damaskọs. <verse eid="ACT 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 9:9" />Anye amaatie usen ita ikịtte ñkpọ, idiaha ñkpọ, inyʌññọ inwọñ ñkpọ ndomokeed.<verse eid="ACT 9:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 9:10" />Ndin mbed keed amaaba ke Damaskọs a-akekereke Ananayas. Abọọñ amaatañ ikọ anọ anye ke ñkukịd ate, <char style="wj">“Ananayas!”</char></para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 9:10">Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Ii, Abọọñ se miin mi.”<verse eid="ACT 9:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 9:11" />Abọọñ amaabo anye, <char style="wj">“Dakka da nyʌñ kaa ufọk Yudas ke efaak akereke Nnen-Nnen, nyʌñ bịp baña Sọọl a-atooho Tasọs, sia anye asʌk abọñ akam.</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 9:12" /><char style="wj">Anye a-akịt ke ñkukịd nte awo a-akereke Ananayas adidot anye ubọk nọ anye atịmme amọọnọ ñkpọ.”</char><verse eid="ACT 9:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 9:13" />Do ke Ananayas akebọọrọ abo ate, “Abọọñ, ami mmekop uwak mbʌk nto uwak awo mbaña ete ami, ye uwak ndiọiñkpọ a-anye anamma ndisana awo mfo ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 9:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 9:14" />Ndin anye adi mi ke adudu mme ñkpoon aku nọ amʌm afịd mbon e-ekoodo anyịñ mfo.”<verse eid="ACT 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 9:15" />Ado Abọọñ amaabọọrọ Ananayas ate, <char style="wj">“Kaa! Awo ami ado ñkpọutom a-ami mmekke nnịm nnọ idem mmi, nọ anye aben anyịñ mmi akesuan anọ mme Gentile ye mme ndidem ammọ ye nditọ Isrel.</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 9:16" /><char style="wj">Ami ñyaawọt anye adaña uwak ukuud a-anaaha nte anye abọ ke ntak anyịñ mmi.”</char><verse eid="ACT 9:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 9:17" />Ndin Ananayas amaadakka akaa ufọk a-Sọọl akebaaha, akedot anye ubọk abo ate: “Sọọl, ayịneka mmi, Abọọñ Yisọs a-awuọhọ uwọt fiin idem ke usʌñ ini a-afo akediighe andọñ utom unọọ, nọ ato do afo amaana akịt usʌñ anyʌñ ayọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd.” <verse eid="ACT 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 9:18" />Ke ataa idahado, mme ñkpọ e-ekebaaha nte ikpọk emaediañña Sọọl ke anyen, ndin anye amaamaana amọọnọ ñkpọ. Anye amaadakka ada, emaenyʌñ eduọk anye mmọọñ, <verse eid="ACT 9:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 9:19" />ndin ke anye amaakedia ndidia, amaatịmme anie adudu.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="ACT 9:19">Sọọl ke Damaskọs ye Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 9:19">Sọọl amaaba ye mme mbed ke Damaskọs ke ñkpọ nte usen ifañ. <verse eid="ACT 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 9:20" />Inikeed-inikeed anye amaatọọñọ adikwọrọ ikọ ke mme sinakọk, abo ke Yisọs ado Ayịn Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 9:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 9:21" />Ado idem amaakpa afịd mbon ekekoppo naña anye akekwọrọ ikọ, ammọ emaenyʌñ ebịp ebo, “Idooho awo a-akesitʌkkọke mbon e-ekekoodo anyịñ Yisọs ke Yeruselem, akenyʌññọ adi Damaskọs ke ukem ntak ado, nọ ato do amuum mme mbed nte mbon ñkpakọb asọk mme ñkpoon aku ado mi?” <verse eid="ACT 9:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 9:22" />Ado Sọọl amaakaa iso akop adudu, anyʌñ anam idem akpa mme Yuu ekedʌññọ ke Damaskọs, ke adiwọt mbo ke Yisọs ado Krais.<verse eid="ACT 9:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 9:23" />Ke uwak usen emaekeboiyo, mme Yuu emaedʌk edioomo ammọ-ammọ adiwot Sọọl, <verse eid="ACT 9:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 9:24" />ado Sọọl amaakop abaña edioomo ammọ. Ammọ emaekpeme mme inuaatob abio akonayio ye uweemeayio nọ ato do enie ufañ ewot anye. <verse eid="ACT 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 9:25" />Ado ke akonayio mme nsaña amọ emaeben anye esịn ke akpasa esuuk ke isọñ ke adudu ke ndibene.<verse eid="ACT 9:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 9:26" />Ke Sọọl amaakedi Yeruselem, anye amaadomo ukeme adidʌk atu mme andinịm ke akpanikọ, ado afịd ammọ ekebaabaak anye, inịmme ke akpanikọ ke anye akedo emọ-emọ mbed. <verse eid="ACT 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 9:27" />Ado Banabas amaaben anye abịne mme abọsịd. Anye amaatañ anọ ammọ naña Sọọl akekịt Abọọñ ke usʌñ, ye naña Abọọñ aketañ ikọ ye anye, naña anye akekwọrọ ikọ uko-uko ke Damaskọs ke anyịñ Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 9:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 9:28" />Ndin Sọọl amaasuuk aba ye ammọ, anyʌñ asikeene ammọ awuọ esiin naña amama ke Yeruselem, akwọrọ ikọ uko-uko ke anyịñ Abọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 9:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 9:29" />Anye amaasifaaña ye mme Yuu<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9:29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Mme Yuu ake ekesemme usem Greek enyʌñ edu eduuwem mbon Greek.</char></note> e-ekesemme Greek, ado mbon ami emaeyem usʌñ naña ekpewot anye. <verse eid="ACT 9:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 9:30" />Ado ke mme andinịm ke akpanikọ emaekediọọñọ ebaña uduak ami, ammọ emaeben anye esọiyọ ekaa Siseria enyʌñ ekenọ anye aka Tasọs.<verse eid="ACT 9:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 9:31" />Ndin ufọkabasi ke afịd Yudia, ye ke Kalili, ye ke Sameria emaebọ emem ye nsọọñọnda. Ke idak mbaak Abasi ye nsọọñidem Adisana Sịbidịd, ufọkabasi amaatọt ke ibad awo.<verse eid="ACT 9:31" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enias ye Dọkas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 9:32" />Naña Pita akekaaha mme itie, anye amaasaña akese ikọd Abọọñ e-ekedʌññọ ke Lida. <verse eid="ACT 9:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 9:33" />Anye amaakịt awodeen keed do a-akekereke Enias, a-akedọñọke akpaubeñ anyʌñ anaa ke ikʌk isua itiaita. <verse eid="ACT 9:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 9:34" />Ndin Pita amaabo anye ate, “Enias, Yisọs Krais a-anam udọñọ mfo akweeñe, dakka da, nyʌñ ben mbịd mfo.” Enias amaadakka ada ini keed. <verse eid="ACT 9:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 9:35" />Afịd mme andikidʌñ ke Lida ye Sarọn emaekịt anye, enyʌñ ekappa esịd ekeene Abọọñ Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 9:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 9:36" />Ado mbed keed amaaba ke Yopa a-akekereke Tabita, (a-awuọñọke Dọkas ke usem Krik). Mma ami akeyọhọ ye nti utom ye unyaaña mbon uweene. <verse eid="ACT 9:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 9:37" />Akem anye amaadọñọ anyʌñ akpa. Ndin emaeyet akpo amọ eben ekenịm ke ubeed keed ke ufọk anyọñ. <verse eid="ACT 9:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 9:38" />Lida akekpere Yopa, ndin ke mme mbed emaekekop ke Pita mmọdo akeba ke Lida, ammọ emaesio awo iba edọñ ekekoot anye, enyʌñ ekpeiye anye ete, “Mbọk di, usọp-usọp!”<verse eid="ACT 9:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 9:39" />Pita amaadakka ada akeene ammọ, ndin ke anye amaakesịm do, emaeben anye edọọk ubeed ufọk anyọñ. Afịd mme ebekpa emaeda ekanna Pita ekʌk, etua enyʌñ ewọt anye mme afọñidem ye mme afọñ mfen a-Dọkas akenamma ke ini anye akebaaha ke uwem ye ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 9:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 9:40" />Ado Pita amaasịññe afịd ammọ ke ubeed, anyʌñ atọọñọ edọñ abọñ akam. Ndin anye amaakanna iso ase akpo mma ado, anyʌñ abo ate, “Tabita, dakka da.” Do ke anye aketaat anyen, ndin ke anye amaakekịt Pita, anye amaadakka atietie. <verse eid="ACT 9:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 9:41" />Pita amaamʌm anye ke ubọk, anyʌñ anwam anye ada ke ukod amọ. Ndin anye amaakoot mme andinịm Abasi ke akpanikọ, akpan-akpan mme ebekpa, anyʌñ ayaak Dọkas ye uwem anọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 9:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 9:42" />Etob ñkpọ ami amaasuana akara ke afịd Yopa, ñko uwak awo emaenịm Abọọñ Abasi ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 9:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 9:43" />Pita amaaba ke Yopa uwak usen ye anamutom ikpa keed a-akekereke Saimọn.<verse eid="ACT 9:43" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="ACT 10" />
  <para style="s1">Kọneliọs Adọñ Ekoot Pita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 10:1" />Ete keed amaaba ke Siseria a-akekereke Kọneliọs. Anye akedo sentudiọn ke atu mme udịmekọñ mbon Itali. <verse eid="ACT 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 10:2" />Anye ye afịd ufọk amọ emaekpono enyʌñ ebaak Abasi; ñko anye amaasinọ mme awo enọ anyʌñ abọñ akam ke ini ke ini. <verse eid="ACT 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 10:3" />Usen keed, ke ñkpọ nte ñkanika ita uweemeayio, anye amaakịt ñkukịd inwañ-inwañ nte enyere Abasi adi ufọk amọ adikoot anye ke anyịñ ate, “Kọneliọs!”<verse eid="ACT 10:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 10:4" />Anye amaataat anyen ase enyere ke ndịk. Ndin anye amaabịp abo, “Abọọñ, ado die?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 10:4">Enyere amaabọọrọ ate, “Akam ye mme enọ mfo a-anọọhọ mbon uweene edọọk esịm Abasi nte ñkpọ uwa aditoiyo. <verse eid="ACT 10:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 10:5" />Ndin dọñ mme awo eka ke Yopa idahami, ekeyem awo a-akereke Saimọn, a-anyịñ amọ mfen adooho Pita. <verse eid="ACT 10:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 10:6" />Anye aba ye Saimọn, anamutom ikpa, u-ufọk amọ abaaha ke mben inyañ.”<verse eid="ACT 10:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 10:7" />Ke enyere a-aketañña ikọ anọ Kọneliọs amaakenyọñ, anye amaakoot awo iba ke atu nditọufọk amọ ye awo ekọñ a-akesikpemeke anye afịd ini, a-akesikponoke Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 10:8" />Anye amaatañ afịd ñkpọ anọ ammọ, anyʌñ adọñ ammọ eka Yopa.<verse eid="ACT 10:8" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkukịd Pita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 10:9" />Ke ñkpọ nte ufọọd uweemeayio edem usen, nte ammọ ekesañake ekpere abio Yopa, Pita amaadọọk anyọñ ufọk akaa adibọñ akam. <verse eid="ACT 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 10:10" />Abiọọñ amaadọñ anye, ndin anye amaayem se akpedia, ado idaha ekesʌkkọ enam ndidia ke ubọk, anye amaakịt ñkukịd. <verse eid="ACT 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 10:11" />Anye amaakịt hefịn nte abeere, ndin esuuk ñkpọ nte ekamba afọñ ekemʌmmọ ke inuuk amọ inaañ ke isọñ. <verse eid="ACT 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 10:12" />Mme nsio-nsio afịd utọ unam: Mme anie ukod inaañ-inaañ, mme ñkpọ se inyọnyọọn ye mme inuen anyọñ emaedọñọ do. <verse eid="ACT 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 10:13" />Ndin uyio amaabo anye ate, <char style="wj">“Pita, dakka da, wot nyʌñ ta.”</char><verse eid="ACT 10:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 10:14" />Ado Pita amaabọọrọ ate, “Ke akpanikọ, Abọọñ, idooho ntoro, sia kpaanam ami ndiaha ñkpọ i-imiisanake me se ideghe.”<verse eid="ACT 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 10:15" />Uyio ado amaamaana abo anye ayọhọ akañ iba, <char style="wj">“Kuubat ñkpọ ndomokeed se Abasi amaakenam asana ke ndek.”</char><verse eid="ACT 10:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 10:16" />Emaenam ntom akañ ita, ndin ke ndo-ndo ado emaemaana eben afọñ ado enyọñ hefịn.<verse eid="ACT 10:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 10:17" />Naña Pita akesʌkkọ akere abaña se ñkukịd ami awuọñọ, mme isʌñutom a-Kọneliọs akedọññọ emaekịt ufọk Saimọn enyʌñ esọñ eda ke inuaatob. <verse eid="ACT 10:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 10:18" />Ammọ emaekoot enyʌñ ebịp me Saimọn a-akekereke Pita akeba do.<verse eid="ACT 10:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 10:19" />Ado naña Pita akesʌkkọ akere abaña ñkukịd ami, Sịbidịd Abasi amaabo anye ate, “Saimọn, ideen ita<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10:19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Akaan ikpañwed keed ewet </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">iba</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; mbon mfen isiaha ibad.</char></note> esʌk uyem. <verse eid="ACT 10:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 10:20" />Dakka da, sọiyọ isọñ, kuunyʌñ unie eyịghe adikeene ammọ ndomokeed, sia ami ñkedọñ ammọ.”<verse eid="ACT 10:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 10:21" />Ndin Pita amaasọiyọ abịne mbon a-Kọneliọs akedọññọ, akebo ate, “Ami ndo awo a-ndufo eyemme. Nsoo ido ntak a-ndufo ediighe?”<verse eid="ACT 10:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 10:22" />Ammọ emaebo ete, “Kọneliọs, awo sentudiọn akidọñ ñnyịn. Anye ado adinen awo, afeghe Abasi, afịd mme Yuu enyʌñ ekpono anye. Adisana enyere akebo yak anye adọñ nọ ukoot fiin adi ufọk imọ nọ anye adikop se afo anie aditañ.” <verse eid="ACT 10:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 10:23" />Ndin anye amaakoot ammọ asịn ke ufọk anọ ammọ itie nnaa nte isenawo amọ.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="ACT 10:23">Pita akaa Ufọk Kọneliọs</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 10:23">Edem usen, Pita amaatọọñọ isañ ye ammọ, ndin usʌk mme andinịm ke akpanikọ e-eketooho Yopa emaekeene esaña. <verse eid="ACT 10:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 10:24" />Edem usen ammọ emaewuọ Siseria. Kọneliọs a-amaakediọọñọ ke ammọ esʌkedi amaakoot mme ayakka ye mme akpan ufan amọ abok. <verse eid="ACT 10:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 10:25" />Naña Pita akedʌkkọ adi, Kọneliọs amaasaña abịne anye, aduọ ke ukod amọ, atuak iwuod akpono anye. <verse eid="ACT 10:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 10:26" />Ado Pita amaanam anye adakka ada anyʌñ abo anye, “Ami ñko ndo awo nte afo.”<verse eid="ACT 10:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 10:27" />Idaha a-Pita aketañña ikọ ye Kọneliọs, anye amaadʌk ufọk anyʌñ akekịt uwak awo nte ebono itie keed. <verse eid="ACT 10:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 10:28" />Anye amaabo ammọ, “Ndufo emenekke ediọọñọ ke mbed akpan awo Yuu adinie ewuana me adika ufọk awo Gentile. Ado Abasi amaaben añwọt ate ke ami mbo ke awo mfen ifọnnọ inyʌññọ isana. <verse eid="ACT 10:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 10:29" />Ado anam nọ ami ndi, mfaañake idaha ñkekoppo ke asʌk añkoot. Yak ami ubịp fiin ndin me nsoo ikido nọ adọñ eñkoot miin?”<verse eid="ACT 10:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 10:30" />Kọneliọs amaabọọrọ abo ate, “Usen ita a-akeboiyoke, ñkeba ke akam ye utreudia ke ufọk mmi ke awa ami ke ñkanika ita uweemeayio. Nte nse awo amaada ke iso mmi ye nsem-nsem afọñ, <verse eid="ACT 10:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 10:31" />anyʌñ ambo miin, ‘Kọneliọs, Abasi a-akop akam mfo anyʌñ atoiyo mme enọ a-afo anọọhọ mme uweene. <verse eid="ACT 10:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 10:32" />Dọñ eka Yopa, ekekoot Saimọn a-akereke Pita. Anye ado asenawo ke ufọk Saimọn anamutom ikpa, a-adʌññọ ke mben inyañ.’ <verse eid="ACT 10:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 10:33" />Kpa idaha-idaha ado, ami mmaadọñ nte edukoot fiin, ndin afọn naña afo adi. Idahami afịd ñnyịn iba ke iso Abasi adikop se Abọọñ akenọọ uyio abo yak afo idọkkọ ñnyịn.”<verse eid="ACT 10:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 10:34" />Ndin Pita amaatọọñọ aditañ ikọ, ate, “Ke akpanikọ mmekịt idahami ke Abasi isattasat awo, <verse eid="ACT 10:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 10:35" />ado adadaara afịd awo ke afịd idịd e-eteeñeke anye anyen, enyʌñ enam se inen. <verse eid="ACT 10:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 10:36" />Ndufo emediọọñọ etob a-Abasi akenọọhọ esọk nditọ Isrel, a-akedooho eti etob emem ato ke Yisọs Krais a-adooho Abọọñ afịd awo. <verse eid="ACT 10:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 10:37" />Ndufo emediọọñọ se ikitịppe ke afịd Yudia, tọọñọ ke Kalili, ke Yọọn amaakekwọrọ ikọ uduọkmmọọñ amọ, <verse eid="ACT 10:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 10:38" />naña Abasi akeyet Yisọs Ayịn Nasared adan ke Adisana Sịbidịd ye adudu, ye naña anye akesaña anañña nti ñkpọ anyʌñ akọk afịd mbon udọñọ e-ekebaaha ke ukad andidiọọk, sia Abasi amaaba ye anye.<verse eid="ACT 10:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 10:39" />“Ñnyịn ido mme ntiense ibaña afịd ñkpọ a-anye akenamma ke isọñ mme Yuu ye ke Yeruselem. Ammọ emaewot anye ke adikọñ anye ke krọs. <verse eid="ACT 10:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 10:40" />Anye ke Abasi akenam aset ke ñkpa ke ayọhọ usen ita, anyʌñ anam ekịt anye anwa-anwa. <verse eid="ACT 10:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 10:41" />Idooho afịd awo ekekịt anye, ado mme ntiense a-Abasi amaakememek, ye ñnyịn i-ikiidiaha inyʌñ inwọñ ye anye ke anye amaakeset ke ñkpa. <verse eid="ACT 10:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 10:42" />Anye amaiwuuk ñnyịn abo yak ikwọrọ ikọ inọ mbon awo inyʌñ itañ ikọ ntiense ibo ke imọ ido awo a-Abasi akemekke nte abiide ikpe nnọọ mme aduuwem ye mme akpañkpa. <verse eid="ACT 10:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 10:43" />Ado anye ke afịd mme prọfed edo ntiense enọ, ebo ke anyịñ amọ eyaefeen ndiọiñkpọ afịd awo e-enịmme anye ke akpanikọ.”<verse eid="ACT 10:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 10:44" />Naña Pita akesʌkkọ atatañ ikọ, Adisana Sịbidịd amaadidoro afịd mbon e-ekekoppo etob ami. <verse eid="ACT 10:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 10:45" />Mbon e-emaekefọọrọ edʌd, e-ekenịmme ke akpanikọ, e-ekesañake ye Pita edi, emaeba ke ñkpaidem naña mme Gentile ñko ekebọọ enọ Adisana Sịbidịd. <verse eid="ACT 10:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 10:46" />Sia ammọ emaekop naña mme Gentile ami esem nsio-nsio usem, enyʌñ etooro Abasi.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 10:46">Ndin Pita amaabo ate, <verse eid="ACT 10:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 10:47" />“Ke akpanikọ awo ndomokeed ikanna ibiọọñọ ibon ami adibọ uduọkmmọọñ, ke ini ammọ emaekebọ Adisana Sịbidịd nte ñnyịn ñko.” <verse eid="ACT 10:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 10:48" />Anye amaanọ uyio ate eduọk ammọ mmọọñ ke anyịñ Yisọs Krais. Ndin ammọ emaebo Pita atie ye mmimọ ke ñkpọ nte usen ifañ.<verse eid="ACT 10:48" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="ACT 11" />
  <para style="s1">Pita Anam Adinam Amọ Anwaña Mbon Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 11:1" />Mme abọsịd ye mme nditọete e-enịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ ke afịd Yudia emaekop ke mme Gentile ñko emaebọ ikọ Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 11:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 11:2" />Ndin idaha a-Pita akekaaha Yeruselem, mbon e-enịmme ke akpanikọ, e-emaekefọọrọ edʌd emaesua enọ anye ebo ete, <verse eid="ACT 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 11:3" />“Afo amaadʌk ufọk mbon a-awo imiifọọrọke edʌd anyʌñ adia ñkpọ ye ammọ.”<verse eid="ACT 11:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 11:4" />Pita amaatañ afịd ñkpọ anọ ammọ naña aketọọñọ ke idaha ke idaha, <verse eid="ACT 11:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 11:5" />“Ami ñkeba ke abio Yopa mbọñ akam, ndin mmaakịt ñkukịd. Ami mmaakịt ñkpọ nte ekamba afọñ e-ekemʌmmọ ke inuuk amọ inaañ nte esuuk eto anyọñ akpere itie nte ñkeba. <verse eid="ACT 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 11:6" />Ami mmaase ñnyʌñ ñkịt se ekesuuk eto anyọñ: Mme unam se inie ukod inaañ-inaañ e-ebaññake ke iso isọñ, mme unam ikọd, se inyọnyọọn, ye mme inuen. <verse eid="ACT 11:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 11:7" />Ndin ami mmaakop uyio nte ambo miin ate, <char style="wj">‘Pita, dakka da. Wot nyʌñ ta.’</char><verse eid="ACT 11:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 11:8" />“Ami mmaabọọrọ, ‘Idooho ntoro Abọọñ! Akenaanam ñkpọ ndomokeed se miisanake me se imiifọnnọ indʌkkọ inua.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 11:9" />“Uyio ado amaato ke hefịn ayọhọ akañ iba abo, <char style="wj">‘Kuubat ñkpọ ndomokeed se Abasi amaakenam asana ke ndek.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 11:10" />Ñkpọ ami aketịppe akañ ita mbemiso emaana edʌt afọñ ado edọọk hefịn.<verse eid="ACT 11:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 11:11" />“Ke ndo-ndo ado ideen ita e-ekedọññọ ennọ miin, emaeto Siseria ediwuọ ufọk a-ami ñkebaaha. <verse eid="ACT 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 11:12" />Sịbidịd Abasi amambo miin ate ke nnie eyịghe adikeene ammọ. Nditọeka itiokeed ami emaesaña ye ami ñko, ndin ñnyịn imaikidʌk ufọk Kọneliọs. <verse eid="ACT 11:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 11:13" />Anye amaidọkkọ ñnyịn naña imọ ikikịt enyere Abasi ke ufọk imọ, akibooho imọ ate, ‘Dọñ eka Yopa ekekoot Saimọn a-akereke Pita. <verse eid="ACT 11:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 11:14" />Anye ayaadat etob a-aduunyaaña fiin ye afịd ufọk mfo usọk.’<verse eid="ACT 11:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 11:15" />“Ñkesʌk ntọtọọñọ aditañ ikọ, Adisana Sịbidịd amaadoro ammọ ke idem naña akidoro ñnyịn ke aditọọñọ. <verse eid="ACT 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 11:16" />Ndin mmaatoiyo se Abọọñ aketañ: <char style="wj">‘Yọọn akekama mmọọñ anịm uduọkmmọọñ, ado ediidat Adisana Sịbidịd inịm ndufo uduọkmmọọñ.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 11:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 11:17" />Adieke Abasi akenọọhọ ammọ ukem enọ a-anye akinọọhọ ñnyịn i-ikinịmme Abọọñ Yisọs Krais ke akpanikọ, ami ñkedo anie awo adikere ke mmekeme ibiọọñọ usʌñ Abasi?”<verse eid="ACT 11:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 11:18" />Ammọ emaekekop ami, ikinieghe mfaaña aba, ado emaetooro Abasi ete, “Awuọ Abasi afeen ndudue anọ mme Gentile, anọ ammọ ñkappa esịd ye uwem.”<verse eid="ACT 11:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ufọkabasi ke Antiọk</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 11:19" />Idahado mbon e-emaekesuana ato ke ukọbọ a-akebaaha ke ini ekewotto Stifịn, emaekaa ekewuọñọ Fonisia, Saiprọs ye Antiọk, enyʌñ esuan eti etob enọ mme Yuu ikpọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 11:20" />Ado usʌk ammọ, mme ideen e-eketooho Saiprọs ye Siriin emaekaa Antiọk ekekwọrọ ikọ enọ mbon Greek ñko, ekwọrọ eti etob ebaña Abọọñ Yisọs enọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 11:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 11:21" />Adudu Abasi amaaba ye ammọ, ado anam uwak mme awo emaenịm ke akpanikọ enyʌñ ekappa esịd ekeene Abọọñ Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 11:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 11:22" />Etob ami amaasịm ufọkabasi ke Yeruselem, ndin ammọ emaedọñ Banabas aka Antiọk. <verse eid="ACT 11:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 11:23" />Anye amaakediwuọ anyʌñ akịt idiọọñọ se mfọn Abasi akenam, anye amaanem esịd anyʌñ atañ ikọ nsọọñọidem anọ afịd ammọ, anyʌñ akpeiye ammọ ate emʌm mbuọdidem ammọ ke Abọọñ ekama ke afịd esịd. <verse eid="ACT 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 11:24" />Banabas akedo eti awo, ayọhọ ye Adisana Sịbidịd ye mbuọdidem, ndin uwak awo emaekeene Abọọñ.<verse eid="ACT 11:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 11:25" />Banabas amaadika Tasọs akeyem Sọọl, <verse eid="ACT 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 11:26" />ndin ke amaakekịt Sọọl, anye amaaben anye adi Antiọk. Banabas ye Sọọl emaeba do isua keed ye mbon ufọkabasi enyʌñ ekpeep ataa uwak awo ñkpọ. Ke Antiọk ke eketo ekoot mme mbed Kristian.<verse eid="ACT 11:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 11:27" />Ke ini ami, mme prọfed emaeto Yeruselem edi Antiọk. <verse eid="ACT 11:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 11:28" />Keed ke atu ammọ a-akekereke Akabọs amaadakka ada, abak atañ ato uyaara a-Sịbidịd ke ataa ekamba akañ ayaaba ke afịd abio Rom. (Ñkpọ ami akedat itie ke ini ukara Klaudius.) <verse eid="ACT 11:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 11:29" />Mme mbed, ke ukeme ammọ keedekeed, emaebiere edinọ nditọeka ammọ ke Abọọñ, e-ekedʌññọ ke Yudia unwam. <verse eid="ACT 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 11:30" />Ammọ emaenam ami ke adinọ Banabas ye Sọọl enọ ammọ nọ eben esọk mme adaiwuod ke ufọkabasi.<verse eid="ACT 11:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="ACT 12" />
  <para style="s1">Pita Abọkkọ Ñkpakọb ke Utịppe Usʌñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 12:1" />Akedo ke ñkpọ nte ini ntom ke Adidem Herọd akemuum usʌk mbon ufọkabasi nọ ato do anye atʌkkọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 12:2" />Anye amaanam nọ ewot Yems ayịneka Yọọn ke akañkañ. <verse eid="ACT 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 12:3" />Ke ini anye amaakekịt ke ñkpọ ami amaanem mme Yuu esịd, anye amaamʌm Pita ñko. Ami aketịppe ke ini Usọrọ Uyo a-Yiis Imiisịneke. <verse eid="ACT 12:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 12:4" />Ke Herọd amaakemʌm anye, amaasịn anye ke ñkpakọb, anyʌñ ayaak anye anọ mbon ekọñ inaañ ke ikpeghe inaañ ate ekpeme anye. Herọd akeduak isio anye ke ini Usọrọ Nsaña Mboiyo nọ ekpe ikpe amọ ke iso abio.<verse eid="ACT 12:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 12:5" />Ke ntoro emaesịn Pita ke ñkpakọb, ado mbon ufọkabasi emaesịn idem ebọñ akam enọ Abasi ebaña anye.<verse eid="ACT 12:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 12:6" />Ke akonayio mbemiso usen a-Herọd akeyemme iben anye ñkaa ikpe, Pita akena ke ufọọd mbon ekọñ iba, ebọp anye ke ñkpọnọ iba, mbon ukpeme enyʌñ eda ke inuausʌñ ufọk ñkpakọb. <verse eid="ACT 12:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 12:7" />Idaha-idaha ado enyere Abọọñ amaabiọññọ, unwana anyʌñ ayama ke ufọk ñkpakọb. Anye amaatuak Pita ke ñkañ, atọi anye ke idab abo, “Sọp dakka da!” Ndin mme ñkpọnọ emaekọọmọ Pita ke ubọk eduọññọ ke isọñ.<verse eid="ACT 12:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 12:8" />Enyere Abasi amaabo anye ate, “Sịne afọñ ye ikpaukod mfo.” Ndin Pita amaanam ntoro. Enyere Abasi amaamaana abo Pita, “Bọbọ mbọbọ afọñ mfo ke idem nyʌñ ñkeene miin.” <verse eid="ACT 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 12:9" />Pita amaakeene anye awuọ ke ñkpakọb, ado anye ikidiọọñọke ibo ke se enyere Abasi akenam akedo se ikitịppe ke akpanikọ; akekere ke idaadappa. <verse eid="ACT 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 12:10" />Ammọ emaeboiyo akpa ye udiana mbon ukpeme ñkpakọb, ekewuọ inuaatob ukwak, a-asañake akewuọ abio. Inuaatob ukwak ado amaabeere ke idem amọ ikpọọñ anọ ammọ, ndin ammọ emaeboiyo. Ke ammọ emaekesaña afịd anyan efaak keed, idaha-idaha ado enyere Abasi amaakpọñ anye.<verse eid="ACT 12:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 12:11" />Ke Pita amaakedidiọọñọ idem, anye amaabo, “Ke akpanikọ ami nnieghe eyịghe sia mmediọọñọ idahami nte ke Abọọñ akedọñ enyere amọ adimfak miin asio ke ukad Herọd ye afịd se mme Yuu ekekere ke ayaatịppe.”<verse eid="ACT 12:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 12:12" />Ke ami amaakenekke adinwaña Pita, anye amaakaa ufọk Mmeri eka Yọọn, e-ekenyʌññọ ekoot Maak, itie u-uwak awo ekebonoke ebọñ akam. <verse eid="ACT 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 12:13" />Pita amaakọñ udọk anwa esiin, ndin ayịnufọk awonwaan a-akekereke Roda amaawuọ adi. <verse eid="ACT 12:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 12:14" />Ke anye amaakediọọñọ uyio Pita, esịd amaanem anye eti-eti, anye amaatịmme edem afeghe akaa esịd ufọk, tutu afre adikʌkkọ usʌñ anyʌñ abọñ ñkpo ate: “Pita mmọ ke inuausʌñ ada!”<verse eid="ACT 12:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 12:15" />Ammọ emaebo anye, “Iwuod mfo ifọnnọ!” Ado anye amaakaa iso abo ke ntoro ke ado, ndin ammọ emaebo ete, “Ana ado enyere amọ ke ado.”<verse eid="ACT 12:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 12:16" />Ado Pita amaakaa iso akọñ, ndin ke ini ammọ ekekʌkkọke usʌñ ekịt anye, idem amaakpa ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 12:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 12:17" />Pita amaadịppe ubọk ate ammọ edop uyio ndin anye amaatañ naña Abọọñ akisio imọ ke ufọk ñkpakọb. Anye amaabo ammọ ate, “Itañ inọ Yems ye mme nditọete mfen ibaña ñkpọ ami.” Ndin anye amaakpọñ ammọ akaa itie mfen.<verse eid="ACT 12:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 12:18" />Ke ubakusen, ekamba aditịm amaaba ke ufọọd mbon ekọñ ke se ikitịppe inọ Pita. <verse eid="ACT 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 12:19" />Ke Herọd amaakenekke ayeem anye ado ikịtte, anye amaanekke aduuñọ mbon ukpeme abaña anye, anyʌñ anọ uyio ate ewot ammọ.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="ACT 12:19">Ñkpa Herọd</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 12:19">Herọd amaato Yudia adika Siseria anyʌñ akeba do ke etək ini. <verse eid="ACT 12:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 12:20" />Anye aketọọtọhọ ye mbon Tai ye Sidọn; ado idʌñ iba ami emaediana keed eyem adisoobo ye anye. Ke ammọ emaekebọ unwam ito Blastos, ayịnufọk a-adidem akemaaha, ammọ emaeyem adinam emem, sia ammọ ekenie idodanyen adinie ndidia nto abio adidem.<verse eid="ACT 12:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 12:21" />Usen akedikem, Herọd amaasịne afọñ ubọọñ, atie ke ebekpo amọ anyʌñ atañ ikọ anọ mbon abio. <verse eid="ACT 12:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 12:22" />Ammọ emaebọñ, “Uyio abasi ado ami, idooho uyio awo.” <verse eid="ACT 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 12:23" />Kpa ataa idahado, sia Herọd imiikinọọhọ Abasi ubọọñ, enyere Abọọñ amaamia anye anịm, mme utʌñ enyʌñ eta anye, ndin anye akpa.<verse eid="ACT 12:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 12:24" />Ado ikọ Abasi amaakaa iso akọt anyʌñ asuana.<verse eid="ACT 12:24" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Esio Banabas ye Sọọl Unyọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 12:25" />Ke Banabas ye Sọọl emaekema iso utom ammọ, ammọ emaekpọñ Yeruselem edat Yọọn e-ekenyʌññọ ekoot Maak nọ asaña ye ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 12:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="ACT 13" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 13:1" />Mme andikpeeb ye mme prọfed emaeba ke ufọkabasi ke Antiọk: Banabas, Simiọn e-ekekoodo Naiya, Lusiọs awo Siriin, Manen (a-akedʌññọ ye adaiwuod ukara, Herọd) ye Sọọl. <verse eid="ACT 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 13:2" />Ke ini ammọ ekesʌkkọ ekpono Abasi enyʌñ etre udia, Adisana Sịbidịd amaabo ate, “Isio Banabas ye Sọọl inịm innọ miin asaña-asaña ke abaña utom a-ami ñkoodo ammọ mbo edinam.” <verse eid="ACT 13:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 13:3" />Ndin ke ammọ emaeketie utreudia enyʌñ ebọñ akam, ammọ emaedot Banabas ye Sọọl ubọk, enyʌñ esio ammọ unyọñ.<verse eid="ACT 13:3" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sọọl ye Banabas Ekaa Saiprọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 13:4" />Ammọ awo iba se Adisana Sịbidịd akedọñ utom emaekaiya Selosia enyʌñ edʌk ubom do ewat ekewuọ Saiprọs. <verse eid="ACT 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 13:5" />Ke emaekewuọ Salamis, ammọ emaekwọrọ ikọ Abasi ke mme sinakọk mme Yuu. Yọọn amaaba ye ammọ nte anọ unwam.<verse eid="ACT 13:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 13:6" />Ammọ emaesaña ke afịd isọñ isu ado (utan a-mmọọñ akannake akʌk) tutu edisịm Pafọs. Do, ammọ emaekịt abiaidiọñ keed, awo Yuu a-akedooho prọfed abiaña a-akekereke Baa-Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 13:7" />Anye akeba nte awo unwam anọ ekamba awo ukara akọnsịn, Seyius Pọlus. Ekamba awo ukara akọnsịn ami, adiọọñọ ñkpọ awo, amaadọñ ekekoot Banabas ye Sọọl sia anye amaayem adikop ikọ Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 13:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 13:8" />Ado Elimas, abiaidiọñ (sia se anyịñ amọ awuọñọ adodo) amaayem ibiọọñọ ammọ anyʌñ ayem usʌñ adiwọññọ ekamba awo ukara akọnsịn ñkpọñ usʌñ mbuọdidem Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 13:9" />Sọọl, a-akenyʌññọ akere Pọọl, a-akeyọhọke ye Adisana Sịbidịd, amaasak iso ase Elimas ate, <verse eid="ACT 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 13:10" />“Afo ado ayịn setan ye asua nti ñkpọ! Afo ameyọhọ ye afịd aduuk abiaña ye ñkara. Nte afo uduutreke adisịn abiaña ye ubiọọñọ ke ndinen usʌñ Abọọñ? <verse eid="ACT 13:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 13:11" />Idahami ubọk Abọọñ udodo fiin ke idem. Afo ayaakanna ado nnan ke etək ini, ini ayaaba a-afo umuuduukịtte unwana utịn aba.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 13:11">Ataa idahado ntuhube ye ekịm emaefʌk anye, anye amaadutịn usʌñ, ayem awo se imʌm anye ubọk. <verse eid="ACT 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 13:12" />Ke ekamba awo ukara akọnsịn amaakekịt se ikiitịppe, anye amaanịm ke akpanikọ, sia idem amaakpa anye ke se Pọọl akekpeep anye abaña Abọọñ.<verse eid="ACT 13:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl ye Banabas Ekaa Antiọk ke Pisidia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 13:13" />Ke emaekekpọñ Pafọs, Pọọl ye nsaña amọ emaewat ekebeghe ke Peka ke Pamfilia. Do ke Yọọn akekpọñ ammọ atịmme anyọñ Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 13:14" />Ke emaekekpọñ Peka ammọ emaeboiyo ekaa Antiọk a-asịneke ke Pisidia. Ke usen Sabad ammọ emaedʌk eketie ke sinakọk. <verse eid="ACT 13:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 13:15" />Ke emaekekoot ñwed Mbed ye mme Prọfed ema, mme andikara sinakọk emaedọñ ekedọkkọ ammọ ete, “Nditọete, akpedo emenie ikọ nsọọñọidem aditañ nnọọ mme awo, mbọk ika iso itañ.”<verse eid="ACT 13:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 13:16" />Pọọl amaadakka ada, adịppe ubọk ke anyọñ abo: “Nditọ Isrel ñnyịn ye ndufo mme Gentile e-ekponoke Abasi, ikpañ utọñ innọ miin! <verse eid="ACT 13:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 13:17" />Abasi nditọ Isrel amaamek mme eteete ñnyịn; amaanyʌñ anam ammọ eforo ke ini ammọ ekebaaha ke Iyib; ke akpọsọñ adudu ke anye akeben ammọ awuọ ke idʌñ ado; <verse eid="ACT 13:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 13:18" />anye amaayọ ido<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13:18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk mme ikpañwed ewet </char><char style="fq" closed="false">anye </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">amaase ñkpọ abaña ammọ</char></note> ammọ ke ñkpọ nte isua aba ke anaan; <verse eid="ACT 13:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 13:19" />anye amaasobo mme idịd itiaba ke Kenan, anyʌñ ayaak isọñ ammọ anọ Isrel nte inie ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 13:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 13:20" />Afịd adinam ami akedat itie ke ñkpọ nte isua ikie inaañ mme aba mme duob.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 13:20">“Ke ado amaakeboiyo, Abasi amaanọ ammọ mme akpeikpe tutu adiwuọ ini prọfed Samwel. <verse eid="ACT 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 13:21" />Akema ammọ emaeyem adidem ndin Abasi amaanọ ammọ Sọọl, ayịn Kis, a-aketooho ekpək Benyamin, a-akekarake ke isua aba. <verse eid="ACT 13:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 13:22" />Ke amaakedooro Sọọl ke ifịm ukara, Abasi amaanam Defid ado adidem ammọ. Abasi amaatañ abaña anye abo: ‘Ami mmekịt Defid ayịn Yesi nte awo e-esịd mmi amaaha; anye ayaanam afịd ñkpọ se ami ñyem anye anam.’<verse eid="ACT 13:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 13:23" />“Abasi amaanọ Yisọs, Andinyaaña asọk Isrel ato ke ubon Defid kpa naña anye akenwọñọ. <verse eid="ACT 13:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 13:24" />Mbemiso Yisọs akedi, Yọọn amaakwọrọ adikappa esịd ye uduọkmmọọñ anọ afịd mbon Isrel. <verse eid="ACT 13:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 13:25" />Ke ini Yọọn akeyemme ikweeñe utom amọ, anye amaabo ate: ‘Ndufo ekere ebo ke ami ndo anie? Ami ndooho anye a-ndufo eyemme. Ado a-aba anye añkeeneke miin ke edem, a-adooho ami ndotto aditat udʌk ikpaukod amọ.’<verse eid="ACT 13:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 13:26" />“Nditọete, nditọ ubon Ebraham ñnyịn ye ndufo mme abaak Abasi ke atu mme Gentile, ado ñnyịn ke ekenọọ etob adinyaaña ami esọk. <verse eid="ACT 13:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 13:27" />Mbon Yeruselem ye mme andikara ammọ ikidiọọñọke Yisọs, ado ke adibiide ikpe ñkpa nnọọ anye, ammọ emaenam mme ikọ a-mme prọfed esikoodo kwa Sabad awuọ asu.” <verse eid="ACT 13:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 13:28" />Akpesʌkado a-ammọ imiikikịtte eti ntak a-anye akpedotto ñkpa, ammọ emaebo Pailed awot anye. <verse eid="ACT 13:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 13:29" />Ke ammọ emaekenam afịd se ekewet ebaña anye, ammọ emaekekọññọ anye ke krọs enyʌñ ebuuk anye ke udi. <verse eid="ACT 13:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 13:30" />Ado Abasi amaanam anye aset ke ñkpa, <verse eid="ACT 13:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 13:31" />ndin ke uwak usen mbon e-ekesañake ye anye eto Kalili eka Yeruselem emaekịt anye. Ammọ edoñño ntiense enọ mbon ñnyịn idahami.<verse eid="ACT 13:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 13:32" />“Ñnyịn idọkkọ ndufo eti etob: Se Abasi akenwọñọ anọ mme eteete ñnyịn, <verse eid="ACT 13:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 13:33" />Abasi a-anam anye asu inọ ñnyịn, nditọ ammọ, ke anye adinam Yisọs aset ke ñkpa. Kpa nte ewette ke udiana Saam:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:33">“ ‘Afo ado ayịn mmi;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:33">mfịn ami mmekappa ubon fiin.’<verse eid="ACT 13:33" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 13:34" />Abasi akenam anye aset ke ñkpa mbaak anye adikịt mbiara ke nsi-nsi. Nte Abasi atañña,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:34">“ ‘Ami ñyaunọ fiin mme ndisana ye akpan nsọọñọnda adidiọñ añkenwọñọke nnọ Defid.’<verse eid="ACT 13:34" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 13:35" />Ñko emaana etañ ke itie mfen:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:35">“ ‘Afo uduunyʌññọ uyak adisana awo mfo akịt mbiara.’<verse eid="ACT 13:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 13:36" />“Ke Defid amaakenam uduak Abasi ke emana amọ ama, anye amaadaiya ke Abọọñ; emaebuuk anye ye mme ete amọ ndin ikpọkidem amọ amaabu. <verse eid="ACT 13:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 13:37" />Ado anye a-Abasi akenamma aset ke ñkpa ikikịtte mbiara.<verse eid="ACT 13:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 13:38" />“Ke ntoro, mme ufan mmi, ami mmeyem nọ ndufo ediọọñọ ebo ke ato ke Yisọs ke ekwọrọ adifeen ke mme idiọọkñkpọ inọ ndufo sia mbed Moses ikanna ifeen afịd mme idiọọkñkpọ ndufo. <verse eid="ACT 13:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 13:39" />Ato ke Yisọs enam afịd mme andinịm ke akpanikọ ebọkkọ ke afịd idiọọkñkpọ, utoppo ikpe a-ndufo imiikpikikanna inie ke idak mbed Moses. <verse eid="ACT 13:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 13:40" />Ikpeme mbaak se mme prọfed eketañ aditịppe inọọ ndufo:<verse eid="ACT 13:40" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 13:41" />“ ‘Sese, ndufo mbon nsaha,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">iba ke ñkpaidem inyʌñ itak,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:41">sia ami ñyaanam ñkpọ ke emana ndufo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">a-ndufo imiidiinịmme ke akpanikọ tutu amama,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">akpekọm awo akpekidọọdọkkọ ndufo.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 13:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 13:42" />Nte Pọọl ye Banabas ekewuọñọke ke sinakọk, mme awo emaebo ammọ ete yak ammọ emaana editañ ikọ ebaña mme ñkpọ ami ke udiana usen Sabad mfen. <verse eid="ACT 13:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 13:43" />Ke ini atu awo emaekesuana ke ufọkabasi, uwak ke atu mme Yuu ye mme andikpono Abasi ke edu mme Yuu emaekeene Pọọl ye Banabas, e-eketañña ikọ ye ammọ, enyʌñ enam ammọ ediọọñọ ke afọn adika iso mba ke mfọn Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 13:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 13:44" />Ke udiana usen Sabad mfen, akeyak etək adido afịd idʌñ ekebono nọ ekop ikọ Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 13:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 13:45" />Ke mme Yuu emaekekịt mme atu awo, ufịb amaadʌk ammọ esịd ndin ammọ emaebiọọñọ Pọọl ke se anye aketañ enyʌñ etañ ikọ ke ido usọñanyen ye eniin.<verse eid="ACT 13:45" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 13:46" />Pọọl ye Banabas emaebọọrọ ammọ uko-uko ete: “Akena ñnyịn ibem iso itañ ikọ Abasi inọ ndufo. Sia ndufo emesịn adibọ ikọ Abasi, inyʌññọ ibat idem ndufo nte mbon e-edotto nsi-nsi uwem, idahami ñnyịn imibiide adiwọññọ ñkeene mme Gentile. <verse eid="ACT 13:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 13:47" />Sia ntom ke Abọọñ inọọ ñnyịn ewʌhọ abo inam:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:47">“ ‘Ami mmunam fiin ado unwana anọ mme Gentile,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:47">nọ afo aben adinyaaña aka ke mme utịd ederimbod.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 13:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 13:48" />Ke ini mme Gentile ekekoppo ami, ammọ emaedaara enyʌñ ekpono ikọ Abọọñ; ndin afịd mbon e-ekesioho enịm enọ nsi-nsi uwem emaenịm ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="ACT 13:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="ACT 13:49" />Ikọ Abasi amaasuana ke afịd ñkañ udo. <verse eid="ACT 13:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="ACT 13:50" />Ado mme Yuu emaedọọñ ibaan e-ekebaaha Abasi enyʌñ enie ñkoñ-ñkoñ idaha ye mme awuọiso ideen ke abio. Ammọ emaeben ukọbọ ekeene Pọọl ye Banabas, enyʌñ ebịne ammọ esio ke ukañ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 13:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="ACT 13:51" />Ado Pọọl ye Banabas emaekeñ ntan ñkpad ebon enọ ammọ nte ñkpọ ndʌdutọñ, ndin emaeboiyo ekaa Aikonium. <verse eid="ACT 13:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="ACT 13:52" />Ndin mme mbed emaeyọhọ ye idaara ye Adisana Sịbidịd.<verse eid="ACT 13:52" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="ACT 14" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl ye Banabas Ekaa Aikonium</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 14:1" />Ke Aikonium Pọọl ye Banabas emaesaña keed ekaiya sinakọk mme Yuu naña ekesinam. Do ammọ emaekwọrọ ikọ ke usʌñ a-akenamma uwak mme Yuu ye mme Greek enịm Abasi ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 14:2" />Ado mme Yuu i-imiikimaaha inịm ke akpanikọ emaetañ ikọ etịmede mme Gentile mfen enyʌñ ebiat ammọ esịd ebaña mme ikọd Abasi ami. <verse eid="ACT 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 14:3" />Ke ntak ado, Pọọl ye Banabas emaekpeene do enyʌñ ekwọrọ Abọọñ uko-uko, ndin Abọọñ ñko amaasọọñọ etob mfọn amọ ke adinọ mme abọsịd adudu adinam mme utịppeñkpọ ye utom idiọọñọ. <verse eid="ACT 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 14:4" />Ubakka amaaba ke ufọọd mbon Aikonium; usʌk eda ye mme Yuu, usʌk enyʌñ eda ye mme abọsịd. <verse eid="ACT 14:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 14:5" />Ndin mme Gentile ye mme Yuu emaedioomo ye mme adaukara ammọ keedekeed aditʌhọde mme abọsịd ñnyʌñ ntọọñ ammọ ke itiad. <verse eid="ACT 14:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 14:6" />Ado sia Pọọl ye Banabas emaekediọọñọ ebaña edioomo ami, ammọ emaefeeñe ekaa Listra ye Deebi ke mme abio Laikonia ye mme ñkanñkʌk idʌñ. <verse eid="ACT 14:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 14:7" />Do ammọ emaeka iso ekwọrọ eti etob abio ubọọñ Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 14:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl ye Banabas Ekaa Listra ye Deebi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 14:8" />Ke Listra amaaba awo a-akedọñọke mbʌñọ tọọñọ ke emana, a-adooho akenanam isañake. <verse eid="ACT 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 14:9" />Anye amaakpañ utọñ akop naña Pọọl atañ ikọ. Pọọl amaawuuk anyen ase anye, anyʌñ akịt ke anye amaanie mbuọdidem se ekọk anye udọñọ, <verse eid="ACT 14:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 14:10" />ndin Pọọl amaabọñ ke akpọsọñ uyio abo, “Dakka da ke ukod mfo!” Ke ami, awo ado amaatamma ke anyọñ anyʌñ atọọñọ adisaña.<verse eid="ACT 14:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 14:11" />Ke ini atu awo emaekekịt se Pọọl akenam, ammọ emaebọñ ñkpo ke usem Laikonia ete, “Mme abasi esọiyọ edi ke mbid awo!” <verse eid="ACT 14:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 14:12" />Ammọ emaekoot Banabas Seus, Pọọl ammọ ekoot Hemes, sia anye akedo akwa atañ ikọ. <verse eid="ACT 14:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 14:13" />Aku Seus, a-tembịd amọ akesannake etək-etək akpọñ abio amaakoono ñyaara enañ ye ñkpataatad adi inuaatob, sia anye ye atu awo ekeyem adinam uwa nnọọ Pọọl ye Banabas.<verse eid="ACT 14:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 14:14" />Ado ke ini abọsịd Banabas ye Pọọl ekekoppo ñkpọ ami, ammọ emaewai afọñidem ammọ enyʌñ efeeñe edọñọ atu awo, ebọñ ñkpo, ete: <verse eid="ACT 14:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 14:15" />“Mme ufan ñnyịn, nsinam ndufo enam ñkpọ ami? Ñnyịn ke idem ñnyịn idoñño mme awo nte ndufo. Ñnyịn idat eti etob isọk ndufo, ite yak ekappa ekpọñ mme ikpu-ikpu ñkpọ i-imiiwuọñọke ñkpọ ndomokeed ebịne ndu-ndu Abasi, a-akenamma anyọñ ye isọñ ye mme akpainyañ ye afịd ñkpọ se iyọhọ ke esịd. <verse eid="ACT 14:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 14:16" />Ke esed, anye amaayaak afịd mme idịd enañña se ema. <verse eid="ACT 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 14:17" />Ado anye itreke adinọ idem amọ ikọ ntiense: Anye awọt mfọnido ke adinọ ndufo edịm ato ke hefịn ye mme mfịd inwañ ke ini ammọ. Anye inọ ndufo uwak ndidia, anyʌñ ayọhọ esịd ndufo ye idaara.” <verse eid="ACT 14:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 14:18" />Kpa ye mme ikọ ami, akesʌk asọsọñ aditre atu awo adinam uwa nnọọ ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 14:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 14:19" />Ndin usʌk mme Yuu emaeto Antiọk ye Aikonium ediwọññọ mbio awo esịd. Ammọ emaetọọñ Pọọl ke itiad enyʌñ edʌt anye eben esio ke abio, ekere ke anye akpa. <verse eid="ACT 14:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 14:20" />Ado ke mme mbed ikọd Abasi emaekedikanna anye ekʌk, anye amaadakka ada anyʌñ amaana adʌk abio. Ayio akesiere, anye ye Banabas emaedaaña ekaa Deebi.<verse eid="ACT 14:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Sọọl ye Banabas Etịmme Ekaa Antiọk ke Siria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 14:21" />Ammọ emaekwọrọ eti mbʌk ke abio ado enyʌñ enam uwak atu awo ekappa edo mme mbed Abasi. Ndin ammọ emaetịmme ekaa Listra, Aikonium ye Antiọk, <verse eid="ACT 14:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 14:22" />ekesọọñọ mme mbed idem, enyʌñ edọñ ammọ esịd ete esọñ eda ke akpanikọ ye ke mbuọdidem. Ammọ emaebo mme mbed ete, “Ana ñnyịn iboiyo ke uwak ndutʌhọ idʌk abioubọọñ Abasi.” <verse eid="ACT 14:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 14:23" />Pọọl ye Banabas emaemek mme adaiwuod enọ ufọkabasi keedekeed, ndin ke akam ye utreudia emaeben ammọ enọ Abọọñ a-ammọ ekebuọttọ idem. <verse eid="ACT 14:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 14:24" />Ke emaekesaña iboiyo Pisidia, ammọ emaekewuọ Pamfilia, <verse eid="ACT 14:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 14:25" />ndin ammọ emaekekwọrọ ikọ ke Peka, enyʌñ esuuho ekesịm Atalia.<verse eid="ACT 14:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 14:26" />Tọọñọ ke Atalia ammọ emaemaana ewat ke nsʌñikañ ekewuọ Antiọk, itie e-ekeyaaha ammọ esịn ke mfọn Abasi ke utom a-ammọ ekenamma ema. <verse eid="ACT 14:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 14:27" />Ke emaekewuọ do, ammọ emaekoot afịd ufọkabasi ebon itie keed, enyʌñ etañ afịd mme ñkpọ se Abasi akedat ammọ anam, ye naña Abasi akekʌkkọ usʌñ mbuọdidem anọ mme Gentile. <verse eid="ACT 14:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 14:28" />Ammọ emaeba do ye mme mbed ekpeene.<verse eid="ACT 14:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="ACT 15" />
  <para style="s1">Esob Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 15:1" />Ubaak awo emaeto Yudia esọiyọ edi Antiọk enyʌñ etọọñọ adikpeep mme andinịm ke akpanikọ, ebo: “Ibọhọke ndufo efọọrọ edʌd ekeene edu unañña ñkpọ naña Moses akekpeep, ndufo idiinieghe adinyaaña.” <verse eid="ACT 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 15:2" />Ami amaadat akpọsọñ mfaaña ye eniin adi ke ufọọd Pọọl ye Banabas ye ammọ. Ke ntak ado, emaemek Pọọl ye Banabas edian ye usʌk mme andinịm ke akpanikọ mfen ete edọọk eka Yeruselem nọ ekekịt mme abọsịd ye mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi, ke abaña mfịna ami. <verse eid="ACT 15:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 15:3" />Ufọkabasi emaenọ ammọ eka, ndin naña ammọ ekesañake eboiyo Fonisia ye Sameria, ammọ emaetañ naña mme Gentile ekekappa esịd. Etob ami amaanem afịd mme andinịm ke akpanikọ esịd eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 15:4" />Ke ini ammọ emaekediwuọ Yeruselem, ufọkabasi ye mme abọsịd ye mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi emaedaara ammọ, ammọ emaenyʌñ ebʌk afịd se Abasi akedat ammọ anam.<verse eid="ACT 15:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 15:5" />Ubaak mbon e-ekenịmme ke akpanikọ e-eketooho ñka mme Farisi, emaedaaña eda ebo ete, “Ana mme Gentile efọọrọ edʌd enyʌñ enịm mbed Moses.”<verse eid="ACT 15:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 15:6" />Mme abọsịd ye mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi emaesoobo iwuod adikere mbaña mfịna ami. <verse eid="ACT 15:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 15:7" />Ke emaeketañ ikọ ekpeene, Pita amaadakka ada atañ ikọ anọ ammọ ate: “Nditọete, ndufo emediọọñọ ke ataa anyan ini a-akeboiyoke, Abasi amammek miin ke atu ndufo abo ke ana mme Gentile ekop eti etob eto inua mmi enyʌñ enịm ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 15:8" />Abasi, a-adiọọñọke esịd awo, amaawọt ke imidat ammọ isịn ke atu ato ke adinọ Adisana Sịbidịd asọk ammọ ukem naña anye akenam inọọ ñnyịn. <verse eid="ACT 15:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 15:9" />Abasi ikisịnne adusad ke ufọọd ñnyịn ye ammọ sia anye amaanam esịd ammọ asana ke mbuọdidem. <verse eid="ACT 15:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 15:10" />Ndin idahami, nsinam ndufo enwana adidomo Abasi idomo ke adiben akpọnọ ñkọọñ mme Gentile ke itọñ, utọ akpọnọ a-ñnyịn ye mme ete ñnyịn imiikikanna ibiom? <verse eid="ACT 15:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 15:11" />Iyoo! Ñnyịn iminịm ke ato ke mfọn Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs ke inyaaña ñnyịn, naña enyʌñ enyaaña ammọ.”<verse eid="ACT 15:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 15:12" />Afịd esob emaedop uyio enyʌñ ekpañ utọñ enọ Banabas ye Pọọl naña ammọ eketañña ebaña mme utịppeñkpọ ye mme idiọọñọ a-Abasi akenamma ato ammọ ke atu mme Gentile. <verse eid="ACT 15:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 15:13" />Ke ammọ emaekekweñe, Yems amaasio uyio abo ate, “Nditọeka ke Krais, ikpañ utọñ innọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 15:14" />Saimọn<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Greek ekoot</char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Simiọn</char><char style="ft" closed="false">asʌk ado </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Saimọn</char><char style="ft" closed="false">anyʌññọ asʌk ado Pita</char></note> Pita a-atatañ inọ ñnyịn naña Abasi akebem iso akere ñkpọ abaña mme Gentile ke adimek mme awo ke atu ammọ nnọọ idem amọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 15:15" />Mme ikọ prọfed e-edukemme ye ñkpọ ami, naña ewet ete:<verse eid="ACT 15:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 15:16" />“ ‘Ke ñkpọ ami amaaboiyo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">ami ñyaatịmme ndi ñnyʌñ ndibọp ñwuudo atayad Defid.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 15:16">Ami ñyaamaana mbọp ñwuudo amọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">ñnyʌñ mmaana ndiọñ anye nọ aba naña akesiba,<verse eid="ACT 15:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 15:17" />nọ ñyọhọnsʌhọ uduud awo eyem Abọọñ Abasi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:17">idem afịd mme Gentile e-ekereke anyịñ mmi,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 15:17">Abasi a-anamma mme ñkpọ ami abo,’<verse eid="ACT 15:17" /></para>
  <para style="q2">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 15:18" />mme ñkpọ e-emaekedọdiọọñọ ke anyan ini a-akeboiyoke.<verse eid="ACT 15:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 15:19" />“Ubiereikpe mmi ado, yak ñnyịn ikuunam ñkpọ asọsọñ anọ mme Gentile e-ekannake ebịne Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 15:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 15:20" />Utu ke ado, yak ñnyịn iwet inọ ammọ ibo yak ammọ esịññe idem ekpọñ mme ndidia e-ewaaha enọ mme ndem, ekpọñ use ye efịbe, ekpọñ unam e-efiakkakefiakka itọñ ewot, enyʌñ ekpọñ adita iyiib. <verse eid="ACT 15:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 15:21" />Sia tọọñọ ke ataa esed, emaekwọrọ mbed Moses ke afịd abio tutu mfịn ami enyʌñ ekoot anye ke mme sinakọk ke afịd usen Sabad.”<verse eid="ACT 15:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Esob Enọ Ñwed Esọk mme Gentile</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 15:22" />Ndin mme abọsịd ye mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi, ye afịd ufọkabasi emaebiide adimek awo ke atu ammọ ñnyʌñ ndọñ eka Antiọk ye Pọọl ye Banabas. Ammọ emaemek Yudas (e-ekekoodo Basabas) ye Sailas, awo iba e-ekedoññoke mme adaiwuod ke atu mme andinịm ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 15:23" />Emaenọ ammọ ñwedetob e-ekewette ntom:</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="ACT 15:23">Ñnyịn mme abọsịd ye mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi, nditọete ndufo, iwet ñwed ami</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="ACT 15:23">inọ esọk mme Gentile e-enịmme Abasi ke akpanikọ e-ebaaha ke Antiọk, Siria ye Silisia:</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="ACT 15:23">Ekọọm do-o.<verse eid="ACT 15:23" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 15:24" />Imaikop ke ubaak awo emaeto ke atu ñnyịn, akpesʌkado ammọ imiikibọọhọ ñnyịn adudu, edifịna ndufo enyʌñ etịmede esịd ndufo akeene se ammọ eketañ. <verse eid="ACT 15:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 15:25" />Ke ntoro, afịd ñnyịn imainyịmme adimek mme awo ñnyʌñ nnọọ ammọ isọk ndufo ñkọrọ mme ndima ufan ñnyịn Banabas ye Pọọl, <verse eid="ACT 15:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 15:26" />ideen e-emaekesaana itoñ uwem ammọ eyaak ke abaña anyịñ Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs Krais. <verse eid="ACT 15:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 15:27" />Ndin ñnyịn imidọñ Yudas ye Sailas edisọọñọ se ñnyịn iwet ke aditañ ikọ ami ke inua ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 15:28" />Adisana Sịbidịd ye ñnyịn imikịt ibo ke a-afọn aditre adinọ ndufo mbiomo mfen ñkan ñkpọ ifañ ami a-ndufo enieghe adinam. <verse eid="ACT 15:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 15:29" />Ana ndufo ebet mme ndidia e-ewaaha enọ mme ndem, ebet adita iyiib, ebet unam e-efiakkakefiakka itọñ ewot, enyʌñ etre use ye efịbe. Ndufo eyaenam afọn adieke ndufo ekpọññọ mme ñkpọ ami.</para>
  <para style="pmc" vid="ACT 15:29">Itie sʌñ.<verse eid="ACT 15:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 15:30" />Ke emaekesio mbon ami nọ eka, ammọ emaesọiyọ ekewuọ Antiọk, itie a-ammọ ekekootto ufọkabasi ebək enyʌñ ekappa ñwedetob ado enọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 15:31" />Mbio Antiọk emaekoot ñwed ado enyʌñ edat esịd ke ikọ nsọọñọidem ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 15:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 15:32" />Yudas ye Sailas, e-ekedooho mme prọfed, emaetañ uwak ikọ adisọọñọ mme andinịm ke akpanikọ idem. <verse eid="ACT 15:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 15:33" />Ke emaekeba do, mme andinịm ke akpanikọ ke Antiọk emaesio ammọ unyọñ ye adidiọñ emem, ke ammọ aditịmme ñnyọñ mbịne mbon e-ekedọññọ ammọ utom. <verse eid="ACT 15:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 15:34" />Sailas amaabiide adisʌhọ do. <verse eid="ACT 15:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 15:35" />Ado Pọọl ye Banabas ye uwak mbon mfen emaesuuk eba ke Antiọk enyʌñ ekwọrọ ikọ Abọọñ.<verse eid="ACT 15:35" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Atọhọ ye Banabas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 15:36" />Ke etək ini amaakeboiyo, Pọọl amaabo Banabas, “Yak ñnyịn itịmme ika ikise nditọeka mme andinịm ke akpanikọ ke afịd abio a-ñnyịn ikikwọrọke ikọ Abọọñ inọọ, inyʌñ ise naña aba ye ammọ.” <verse eid="ACT 15:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 15:37" />Banabas amaayem Yọọn, e-ekekoodo Maak, akpekeene asaña ye ammọ, <verse eid="ACT 15:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 15:38" />ado Pọọl ikikereke ke a-afọn ntoro, sia Yọọn amaakpọñ ammọ ke Pamfilia, ikinyʌññọ ikeene ammọ inam utom aba. <verse eid="ACT 15:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 15:39" />Akpọsọñ mfaña ye eniin amaaba ke ufọọd ammọ tutu akewuọ se ammọ ediañña nsaña. Banabas amaaben Maak akaa Saiprọs, <verse eid="ACT 15:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 15:40" />ado Pọọl amaamek adisana ye Sailas, ke mme andinịm ke akpanikọ emaekeyaak ammọ esịn ke ubọk mfọn Abọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 15:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 15:41" />Pọọl amaasaña aboiyo Siria ye Silisia anyʌñ asọọñọ mme ufọkabasi idem.<verse eid="ACT 15:41" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="ACT 16" />
  <para style="s1">Timoti Akeene Pọọl ye Sailas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 16:1" />Pọọl amaadisịm Deebi ndin ato do akaa Listra, itie a-mbed keed a-akekereke Timoti akedʌññọ, e-eka amọ akedooho Yuu anyʌñ anịm Yisọs ke akpanikọ, ado ete amọ akedo Greek. <verse eid="ACT 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 16:2" />Mme nditọete e-ekenịmme ke akpanikọ ke Listra ye Aikonium emaetañ nti ñkpọ ebaña Timoti. <verse eid="ACT 16:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 16:3" />Pọọl amaayem anye asaña ye imọ aka isañ, ke ntoro anye amaafọọrọ anye edʌd sia mme Yuu e-ekedʌññọ ke ukañ udo, emaediọọñọ ete amọ nte ado Greek. <verse eid="ACT 16:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 16:4" />Nte ammọ ekesañake ke abio ke abio, ammọ emaetañ se mme abọsịd ye mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi ke esob Yeruselem ekebiide enọ mme awo ete enam. <verse eid="ACT 16:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 16:5" />Ntoro ke mme ufọkabasi ekekọt ke mbuọdidem, ndin mme ufa awo emaenyʌñ edʌk edi ke usen ke usen.<verse eid="ACT 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ñkukịd Pọọl Ke Abaña Awo Masidonia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 16:6" />Pọọl ye nsaña amọ emaesaña ke afịd ñkanñkʌk Frikia ye Kalesia, kpa naña Adisana Sịbidịd aketemme ammọ abo ekekwọrọ ikọ ke idak ukara Esia. <verse eid="ACT 16:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 16:7" />Ke ammọ emaekediwuọ adaña abio Misia, ammọ emaedomo adidʌk Bitinia ado Sịbidịd Yisọs ikiyakka. <verse eid="ACT 16:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 16:8" />Ke ntoro, ammọ emaeboiyo ekpọñ Misia, ekaa Troas. <verse eid="ACT 16:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 16:9" />Ke akonayio Pọọl amaakịt ñkukịd naña awo aketo Masidonia ada akpeiye anye ate, “Kanna di Masidonia di inwam ñnyịn.” <verse eid="ACT 16:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 16:10" />Ke Pọọl amaakekịt ñkukịd ami, ñnyịn imaibeeñe idem ini keed adisio uwad ñkaa Masidonia, inịm ke akpanikọ ke Abasi ikoot abo ikikwọrọ eti etob inọ ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 16:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Lidia Akappa Esịd ke Filipai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 16:11" />Ñnyịn imaidʌk nsʌñikañ tọọñọ ke Troas iwat nnen-nnen ikiwuọ Samotras, ndin ke ayio amaakesiere, imaikiwuọ Niapolis. <verse eid="ACT 16:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 16:12" />Tọọñọ do ñnyịn imaisaña ika Filipai, awuọiso abio ke Masidonia a-Rom akekarake. Ñnyịn imaiba do ke uwak usen.<verse eid="ACT 16:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 16:13" />Ke usen Sabad, ñnyịn imaikpọñ abio ika mben inyañ, itie a-ñnyịn ikikereke ke iyaikịt itie ubọñ akam. Ñnyịn imaisuuk itie do, itọọñọ aditañ ikọ ye ibaan e-ekebonoke do. <verse eid="ACT 16:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 16:14" />Keed ke atu mbon e-ekekpañña utọñ inọọ akedo awonwaan keed a-akekereke Lidia, anyam iduod-iduod afọñ ubọọñ a-atooho abio Tiatira. Anye akedo awo a-akekponoke Abasi. Abọọñ amaatuuk anye esịd anam anye akop etob Pọọl. <verse eid="ACT 16:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 16:15" />Ke emaekeduọk anye ye mbon ufọk amọ mmọọñ, anye amaikoot ñnyịn ufọk ate, “Adieke ndufo endatta miin nte andinịm Abọọñ ke akpanikọ idi idiba ke ufọk mmi.” Anye amaikpek ñnyịn nọ ikeene anye.<verse eid="ACT 16:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekọp Pọọl ye Sailas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 16:16" />Usen keed, idaha a-ñnyịn ikisʌkkọ ikaa itie ubọñ akam, ñnyịn imaisoobo afʌn abọikpa keed a-akenieghe sịbidịd a-anye akekamake akịt ñkukịd abaña ini iso. Anye amaadat ado akọ uwak akʌk anọ mbon se ikinie anye ke aditañ se idiitịppe ke ini iso. <verse eid="ACT 16:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 16:17" />Abọikpa ami amaikeene ñnyịn ye Pọọl ke edem, abọọñ ñkpo abo, “Mbon ami edo mme isʌñutom Abasi Andikoñ Ñkan, e-etañña ñkpọ ebaña usʌñ adinyaaña inọọ ndufo.” <verse eid="ACT 16:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 16:18" />Anye amaakaa iso anam ntom ke mme uwak usen. Ke akpatre, ñkpọ ami amaayat Pọọl tutu anye amaakanna atuak ada anyʌñ aduat sịbidịd ado ate, “Ke anyịñ Yisọs Krais mmuwuuk fiin mbo awuọ anye ke idem!” Kpa idaha-idaha ado sịbidịd ado amaakpọñ anye.<verse eid="ACT 16:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 16:19" />Mme andinie afʌn abọikpa ami emaekekịt ke usʌñ unwana akʌk ammọ atre, ammọ emaemʌm Pọọl ye Sailas edʌt ammọ ekesịm anwa udua ke iso mme adaaha abio. <verse eid="ACT 16:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 16:20" />Ndin emaedat ammọ ekaa iso mme ayaraiwad, ete, “Ibon ami edoñño mme Yuu, ndin ammọ e-esịn ntịme ke abio, <verse eid="ACT 16:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 16:21" />ke adikpeep eduuwem i-imiidooho se mbed ñnyịn nte mbon Rom inyịmme me inam.”<verse eid="ACT 16:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 16:22" />Mme atu awo e-ekedaaha emaekeene eyem Pọọl ye Sailas ikọ, ndin mme ayaraiwad emaenọ uyio ete esịññe ammọ afọñ enyʌñ emia ammọ ke ukwak. <verse eid="ACT 16:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 16:23" />Ke emaekenekke emia ammọ ema, emaetop ammọ edọñ ke ñkpakọb, enyʌñ ebo andikpeme mbon ñkpakọb anekke akpeme ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 16:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 16:24" />Ke ini anye amaakebọ mme ewʌhọ ami, andikpeme mbon ñkpakọb amaadọn ammọ ke ataa esịd ufọk ñkpakọb anyʌñ abọp ukod ammọ adian ke ikpọ ndoppo eto.<verse eid="ACT 16:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 16:25" />Ke ñkpọ nte ufọọd akonayio Pọọl ye Sailas ekesʌk ebọñ akam enyʌñ ekwọ ikwọ enọ Abasi, ndin mme mbio ñkpakọb mfen ekesʌk ekpañ utọñ enọ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 16:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 16:26" />Ke unana idodanyen unyeñisọñ amaatịppe, anyeeñe afịd itiad idakisọñ ufọk ñkpakọb. Afịd mme usʌñ ufọk ñkpakọb amaakuuñọ ini keed, ñkpọnọ afịd mbio ñkpakọb enyʌñ ekpọhọ. <verse eid="ACT 16:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 16:27" />Andikpeme mbon ñkpakọb amaademme, ndin ke anye amaakekịt usʌñ ufọk ñkpakọb nte ana inwañ, anye amaasio eduad ayem adiwot idem amọ, sia anye akekere ke mbio ñkpakọb efeeñe. <verse eid="ACT 16:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 16:28" />Ado Pọọl amaasio ñkpo abo anye ate, “Kuunọọ idem mfo unọmọ! Afịd ñnyịn mmọ mi!”<verse eid="ACT 16:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 16:29" />Akpeme ñkpakọb amaabo eben utuenikañ edi, ndin anye amaasọsọp afeghe ke ñnyeñidem adʌk akeduọ ke iso Pọọl ye Sailas. <verse eid="ACT 16:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 16:30" />Ndin anye amaasịññe ammọ adi anyʌñ abịp abo, “Mme ete, nsoo ke nnie adinam nọ nnie adinyaaña?”<verse eid="ACT 16:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 16:31" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ ete, “Nịm Abọọñ Yisọs ke akpanikọ, ndin eyaunyaaña fiin, afo ye afịd ufọk mfo.” <verse eid="ACT 16:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 16:32" />Pọọl ye Sailas emaekwọrọ ikọ Abasi enọ anye ye afịd mbio mfen e-ekebaaha ke ufọk amọ. <verse eid="ACT 16:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 16:33" />Kpa akonayio ado akpeme ñkpakọb amaayet unan ammọ; ndin idaha-idaha ado anye ye afịd ufọk amọ emaebọ uduọkmmọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 16:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 16:34" />Ndin akpeme ñkpakọb amaaben ammọ akaa ufọk amọ anyʌñ akenọ ammọ ndidia. Anye amaayọhọ ye idadesịd, sia anye ye afịd ufọk amọ emaenịm Abasi ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="ACT 16:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 16:35" />Ke ayio amaakesiere, mme ayaraiwad emaedọñ ñkpoon mbon utom ammọ utom enọ akpeme ñkpakọb, ete: “Saana ibon ado yaak.” <verse eid="ACT 16:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 16:36" />Ndin akpeme ñkpakọb amaadọkkọ Pọọl ate, “Mme ayaraiwad e-enọ uyio ebo usaana fiin ye Sailas eyaak. Ke ntoro ndufo emekeme adinyọñ. Inyọñọ ke emem.”<verse eid="ACT 16:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 16:37" />Ado Pọọl amaabo mme ekamba mbon utom ate: “Ammọ emaimia ñnyịn anwa-anwa, ikpeeghe ikpe, akpesʌkado ñnyịn idooho amanaisọñ nditọ Rom, enyʌñ itop ñnyịn edọñ ke ñkpakọb. Idahami ammọ eyem adibịn ñnyịn nsio ke ndịbe? Iyoo! Yak ammọ edi ke idem ammọ ediben ñnyịn ewuọ.”<verse eid="ACT 16:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 16:38" />Mme ekamba mbio utom emaetañ ntom enọ mme ayaraiwad, ndin ke ammọ emaekekop ke Pọọl ye Sailas edoñño mme amanaisọñ mbon Rom, idem amaanyeñ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 16:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 16:39" />Ndin ammọ emaekpeiye Pọọl ye Sailas enyʌñ eben ammọ esaña ewuọ ke ñkpakọb, ekpeiye ammọ ete ekpọñ abio. <verse eid="ACT 16:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 16:40" />Ke Pọọl ye Sailas emaekewuọñọ ke ñkpakọb, ammọ emaekaa ufọk Lidia. Do ke ammọ ekesoobo ye mme ikọd Abasi ideen ye ibaan enyʌñ ekwọrọ ikọ nsọọñọidem enọ ammọ. Akema ammọ emaekpọñ do.<verse eid="ACT 16:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 16" />
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="ACT 17" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl ye Nsaña Amọ Ekaa Tesalọnika</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 17:1" />Ke Pọọl ye mme nsaña amọ emaekeboiyo ke Amfipolis ye Apolonia, ammọ emaedisịm Tesalọnika, itie a-sinakọk mme Yuu akebaaha. <verse eid="ACT 17:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 17:2" />Nte ido ammọ akesidooho, Pọọl amaadʌk akaa sinakọk, anyʌñ akefaaña mfaaña ato ikọ ñwed Abasi ye mme Yuu ke usen Sabad ita, <verse eid="ACT 17:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 17:3" />anam anwaña anyʌñ awọt ammọ abo ke Krais akena akịt ukuud anyʌñ aset ke ñkpa. Anye amaabo, “Yisọs ami ke ami idọkkọ ndufo mbo ke anye ado Krais.” <verse eid="ACT 17:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 17:4" />Usʌk mme Yuu emaekappa esịd enyʌñ ekeene Pọọl ye Sailas, ye uwak mbon Greek e-ekebaaha Abasi ye usʌk mme awuọiso ibaan.<verse eid="ACT 17:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 17:5" />Ado ubaak mme Yuu emaefịbe ufịb; ke ntoro ammọ emaekekoono mme ndiọi awo eto anwa udua, edọọñ atu awo nọ etọọñọ ntịme ke abio. Ammọ emaefeeñe ekaa ufọk Yesịn adiyem Pọọl ye Sailas mben ammọ ndi ke iso atu awo. <verse eid="ACT 17:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 17:6" />Ado ke ini ammọ imiikikịtte Pọọl ye Sailas, ammọ emaemʌm Yesịn ye mme andinịm ke akpanikọ mfen ekaa iso mme akama utom ke abio, enyʌñ ebọñ ete: “Ibon ami e-esịnne ntịme ekanna afịd ederimbod ediwuọ umi, <verse eid="ACT 17:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 17:7" />ndin Yesịn amaakoono ammọ adọñ ke ufọk amọ. Ammọ inịmme mme mbed Sisa, ado ebo ke adidem mfen a-aba, a-akereke Yisọs.” <verse eid="ACT 17:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 17:8" />Ke ammọ emaekekop ami, mme atu awo ye mme ñkpoon mbon utom abio emaetịmede esịd. <verse eid="ACT 17:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 17:9" />Ndin ammọ emaesio Yesịn ye mme mbon ako ke ubiọñ mbemiso eyaak ammọ enyọñọ.<verse eid="ACT 17:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl ye Nsaña Amọ Ekaa Beria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 17:10" />Ayio akesʌk akekịm, mme andinịm ke akpanikọ emaesio Pọọl ye Sailas enọ eka Beria. Ekekesịm udo, ammọ emaekaa sinakọk mme Yuu. <verse eid="ACT 17:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 17:11" />Mme Yuu ke ukañ Beria emaenieñe nti ido ekan mbon ukañ Tesalọnika, sia ammọ emaebọ etob ami ke ataa ayọhọ udọñ, enyʌñ eduuñọ ñwed Abasi afịd usen adikịt me se Pọọl aketañ akedo akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 17:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 17:12" />Ke ntak ami uwak mme Yuu emaenịm ke akpanikọ, ukem nte ubaak mme awuọiso ibaan Krik ye uwak ideen Krik ñko.<verse eid="ACT 17:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 17:13" />Ado ke ini mme Yuu ke Tesalọnika emaekediooño ke Pọọl asʌk akwọrọ ikọ Abasi ke Beria, usʌk ammọ emaekaa do ñko, ekesịn nsọk ke ufọọd mbon ntịme enyʌñ etịmede ammọ esịd. <verse eid="ACT 17:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 17:14" />Ndin mme andinịm ke akpanikọ emaesọp enam Pọọl aka mben esʌk, ado Sailas ye Timoti emaesọñ eba ke Beria. <verse eid="ACT 17:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 17:15" />Mme awo e-ekebenne Pọọl ekesuuk emaeben anye ekaa Aten, ndin Pọọl amaanọ uyio ate Sailas ye Timoti ibịne imọ ekpekan usọp-usọp.<verse eid="ACT 17:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akaa Aten</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 17:16" />Ke idaha a-Pọọl aketieghe abet ammọ ke Aten, esịd amaadiọọk anye eti-eti ke adikịt nte mme ubobod abasi eyọhọ idʌñ ado. <verse eid="ACT 17:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 17:17" />Ndin anye amaafaaña anyʌñ aneme ke sinakọk ye mme Yuu ye mme Krik e-ekebaaha Abasi, ukem ado ke anwa udua ke usen ke usen ye mme awo akeedodo e-ekebaaha do. <verse eid="ACT 17:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 17:18" />Ñko mme ñkpoon ntaifiọk e-ekekeeneke ukpeebñkpọ ñka Epikuriọs ye Stọik emaetọọñọ mfaaña ye anye. Usʌk ammọ emaebịp ebo, “Nsoo ke ataaññtịme ami anwanwana aditañ?” Mbio mfen emaebo, “Aba nte anye anwana adikwọrọ ikọ mbaña mme isen abasi.” Ammọ eketañ ami sia Pọọl amaakwọrọ eti mbʌk abaña Yisọs ye adised ke ñkpa. <verse eid="ACT 17:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 17:19" />Ammọ emaemʌm anye eben ekaa ekamba esob ikpaisọñ mbon Krik e-ekekoodo Ariopakus, ndin emaebo anye ete, “Akpaakan anam nọ ñnyịn idiọọñọ ufa ukpeebñkpọ a-afo atañña abaña mi? <verse eid="ACT 17:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 17:20" />Ndufo emeben mme asen akikere etañ edọñ ke utọñ ñnyịn, ndin ñnyịn ikpaima adidiọọñọ se ammọ ewuọñọ.” <verse eid="ACT 17:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 17:21" />(Ndin afịd mbon Aten ye mme isenawo e-ekedʌññọ do ikisinamma ñkpọ mfen ikan aditañ mbaña ñnyʌñ ñkpañutọñ nnọọ mme ufa akikere.)<verse eid="ACT 17:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 17:22" />Pọọl ndin amaadakka ada ke mbono mme Ariopakus atañ ate: “Ndufo mbon abio Aten! Ami mmekịt ke afịd usʌñ nte ndufo emekpono Abasi eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 17:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 17:23" />Sia naña ami ñkesaañake ñkanna ñnyʌñ nseet, akpan-akpan mme ñkpọ ukpono Abasi ndufo, ami mmaakịt itie ukpono Abasi ye mme ikọ e-ewette ete:</para>
  <para style="pc" vid="ACT 17:23">
    <char style="sc">enịm enọ abasi a-ñnyịn imiidiọọñọke.</char></para>
  <para style="m" vid="ACT 17:23">Ke adinekke ntañ, Abasi a-ami ñyemme adikwọrọ inọọ ndufo ado anye a-ndufo ekponoke, akpesʌkado ndufo imiidiọọñọke.<verse eid="ACT 17:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 17:24" />“Abasi a-akenamma ederimbod ye afịd ñkpọ ke esịd amọ ado Abọọñ anyọñ ye isọñ, ndin anye idʌññọ ke mme tembịd e-ebọppọ ke ubọk. <verse eid="ACT 17:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 17:25" />Awo inamma ñkpọ ke ubọk inọ anye sia anye iyemme ñkpọ ndomokeed, ado anye ke idem amọ anọ afịd awo uwem ye inweek ye afịd ñkpọ mfen. <verse eid="ACT 17:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 17:26" />Aketo ke awo keed anye anam afịd mme idịd, abo ammọ edʌñ ke afịd iso isọñ, anye anyʌñ abakka ini anọ ammọ ye mme itie se ana ammọ edʌñ. <verse eid="ACT 17:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 17:27" />Abasi akenam ami nọ mme awo eyem anye, ekan esaña ekpere anye, enyʌñ ekịt anye, akpesʌkado a-anye imiinyọọñọ usʌñ ikpọñ ñnyịn ndomokeed. <verse eid="ACT 17:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 17:28" />‘Sia ke anye ke ñnyịn idʌñ, inyʌñ isaña inyʌñ inie uwem.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ikọ ami ato Epimenides, afiọkñkpọ awo a-atooho abio Kret</char></note> Nte naña mme aweduto ndufo eketatañ, ‘Ñnyịn ido mme ubon amọ.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ikọ ami ato Aratus, afiọkñkpọ awo a-atooho Sisili</char></note><verse eid="ACT 17:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 17:29" />“Ndin sia ñnyịn idooho nditọ Abasi, inaaha ñnyịn ikere ke Abasi ana aba nte mbid kold me silfa me itiad, nte ubobodñkpọ a-awo adatta ifiọk ye ikike amọ abot. <verse eid="ACT 17:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 17:30" />Ke ayio ñkpọñ Abasi amaafeen anọ ammọ ke unana adidiọọñọ, ado idahami anye a-anọ iwuuk ate afịd awo ke afịd itie ekappa esịd. <verse eid="ACT 17:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 17:31" />Sia anye a-anịm usen a-anye adiikpe ikpe afịd ekondo ke unen ato ke awo a-anye akemekke anịm nte akpeikpe. Anye akenam anye aset ke ñkpa adiwọt ke anye ado akpe ikpe ado.”<verse eid="ACT 17:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 17:32" />Ke ammọ emaekekop adised ke ñkpa, usʌk ammọ emaedutuun inua, ado usʌk ammọ emaebo, “Ñnyịn iyaimaana ikop ikọ ami uto fiin.” <verse eid="ACT 17:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 17:33" />Akema, Pọọl amaakpọñ esob. <verse eid="ACT 17:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 17:34" />Ubaak awo emaekappa esịd ekeene Pọọl enyʌñ enịm ke akpanikọ. Usʌk mbon ammọ se ikinịm ekedo Dionisius, awo keed ke atu mme Aropakus, ye awonwaan a-akekereke Damadis, ye mbon mfen.<verse eid="ACT 17:34" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 17" />
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="ACT 18" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akaa Kọrint</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 18:1" />Ke mme ñkpọ ami emaekeboiyo, Pọọl amaakpọñ Aten akaa Kọrint. <verse eid="ACT 18:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 18:2" />Ke udo anye amaakịt awo Yuu keed a-akekereke Akwila, a-aketooho Pọntus. Anye aketo Itali adi ye anwaan amọ Prisila sia Klaudius amaakenọ uyio ate afịd mme Yuu ekpọñ Rom. Pọọl amaakaa akese ammọ, <verse eid="ACT 18:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 18:3" />ndin sia anye akedooho anam atayad nte Akwila ye Prisila, anye amaatie anam utom ye ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 18:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 18:4" />Anye amaanie nneme afịd Sabad ke sinakọk, adomo ukeme adinam mme Yuu ye mbon Greek ekịt ntak a-ammọ ekpenịmme ke akpanikọ.<verse eid="ACT 18:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 18:5" />Ke ini Sailas ye Timoti emaeketo Masidonia edi, Pọọl amaayaak idem amọ afịd-afịd asịn ke adikwọrọ ikọ, aben awọt mme Yuu ke Yisọs ado Krais. <verse eid="ACT 18:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 18:6" />Ado ke mme Yuu emaekefaaña ye Pọọl enyʌñ ekanna eda ke adisuesue anye, Pọọl amaasio mme afọñidem amọ asịppe anyʌñ abo ammọ ate, “Iyiib ndufo idodo ndufo ke iwuod! Ubọk mmi isịneke do, mmesana. Tọọñọ ke idahami, ami ndiika mbịne mme Gentile.”<verse eid="ACT 18:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 18:7" />Ndin Pọọl amaakpọñ sinakọk akaa ufọk Titiọs Yọstus, akpono ataa Abasi, u-ufọk amọ akediaññake atañ ye sinakọk. <verse eid="ACT 18:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 18:8" />Krispus, etubom sinakọk ye afịd ufọk amọ emaenịm Abọọñ ke akpanikọ, ndin uwak mbon Kọrint e-ekekoppo se Pọọl aketañ emaenịm ke akpanikọ enyʌñ ebọ uduọkmmọọñ.<verse eid="ACT 18:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 18:9" />Akonayio keed, Abọọñ amaatañ ikọ anọ Pọọl ke ñkukịd, ate: <char style="wj">“Kuukop ndịk; kaa iso kwọrọ, kuudop uyio.</char> <verse eid="ACT 18:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 18:10" /><char style="wj">Sia ami mmọdo mba ye afo, ndin awo ndomokeed idiinamma ntịme ye afo, idinyʌññọ unọ fiin unan sia ami mmenieñe uwak awo ke abio ami.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 18:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 18:11" />Ndin Pọọl amaatie do ke Kọrint isua keed ye ubaak akpeep ammọ ikọ Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 18:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 18:12" />Naña Kalio akedooho ataa ekamba awo ukara ke Akaya, mme Yuu ke Kọrint emaediana esịd keed enam ntịme ye Pọọl enyʌñ eben anye ekaa esob, ete: <verse eid="ACT 18:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 18:13" />“Awo ami atemme mme awo naña ekpono Abasi ke mme usʌñ i-imiisañake ke mbed Moses.”<verse eid="ACT 18:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 18:14" />Kpa ke idaha Pọọl akeyemme aditañ ikọ, Kalio amaabo mme Yuu ate: “Akpedo nte ndufo mme Yuu ekeben ikọ a-abañake ndudue me akpan ubiad mbed edi, akpaawọt ifiọk ami adikpañ utọñ inọọ ndufo. <verse eid="ACT 18:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 18:15" />Ado sia abañake mme ikọ ye anyịñ ye mbed ndufo, ibiire ikọ ado ke idem ndufo. Ami ndiidooho akpe ikpe ke utọ mme ñkpọ ado.” <verse eid="ACT 18:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 18:16" />Anye amaanam ebịne ammọ esio ke ufọk esob. <verse eid="ACT 18:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 18:17" />Ndin afịd atu awo emaekanna iso ese Sostenes etubom esob sinakọk enyʌñ emia anye ke iso ekamba akama utom ukara. Ado Kalio ikinamma nte anye anie ndubeghe ndomokeed do.<verse eid="ACT 18:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl, Prisila, Akwila ye Apọlọs Ekaa Nsio-nsio Itie</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 18:18" />Pọọl amaaba ke Kọrint ke ñkpọ nte usen ifañ. Akema anye amaakpọñ nditọeka ke Krais anyʌñ asaña ye Prisila ye Akwila ekaa Siria. Mbemiso anye akesio uwad, Pọọl amaafat ided amọ ke Senkre akeene akaaña a-anye akenamma. <verse eid="ACT 18:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 18:19" />Ammọ emaekewuọ Efisọs, itie a-Pọọl akekpọññọ Prisila ye Akwila. Anye ke idem amọ amaadʌk akaa sinakọk anyʌñ akenie nneme ye mme Yuu. <verse eid="ACT 18:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 18:20" />Ke ini ammọ ekebooho yak anye amaana atie ye mmimọ, anye ikinyịmmeke. <verse eid="ACT 18:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 18:21" />Ado ke ini anye akedakkake, anye amaanam enwọñọ abo: “Ami ñyaatịmme ndi adieke adooho uduak Abasi.” Ndin anye amaasio uwad akpọñ Efisọs. <verse eid="ACT 18:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 18:22" />Ke anye amaakebeghe ke Siseria, anye amaadọọk akewuọ Yeruselem anyʌñ akekọọm ufọkabasi ndin adisọiyọ akaa Antiọk.<verse eid="ACT 18:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 18:23" />Ke Pọọl amaaketie etək ini ke Antiọk, anye amaato do adakka isañ anyʌñ asaña ke itie ke itie ke afịd ukañ Kalesia ye Frikia, asọọñọ afịd mme mbed idem.<verse eid="ACT 18:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 18:24" />Akema awo Yuu keed a-akekereke Apọlọs, a-aketooho Aleksandra, amaadi Efisọs. Anye akedo ataifiọk a-akenieghe ataa ntotəño ifiọk ke Ñwed Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 18:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 18:25" />Emaekpeep anye ñkpọ ke usʌñ Abọọñ Abasi, ndin anye amaatañ ikọ ye ayọhọ uko anyʌñ akpeep ñkpọ nnen-nnen nnen-nnen abaña Yisọs, akpesʌkado a-anye akediọọñọke ñkpọ abaña uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn kpọd. <verse eid="ACT 18:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 18:26" />Anye amaatọọñọ aditañ ikọ uko-uko ke sinakọk. Ke Prisila ye Akwila emaekekop se anye aketañ, ammọ emaekoot anye ufọk enyʌñ ekenam usʌñ Abasi anwaña anye ayọhọ-ayọhọ.<verse eid="ACT 18:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 18:27" />Ke ini Apọlọs amaakeyem adika Akaya, nditọeka ke Krais emaesọọñọ anye ukod enyʌñ ewet ñwed enọ mme mbed ke udo ete edaara adidi amọ. Ndin ke Pọọl amaakesịm, anye amaado ekamba unwam anọ mbon e-emaekenịm ke akpanikọ ato ke mfọn Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 18:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 18:28" />Anye amaafaaña anwa-anwa ye mme Yuu ke nneme, anyʌñ awọt ato ñwed Abasi ke Yisọs ado Krais.<verse eid="ACT 18:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 18" />
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="ACT 19" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akaa Efisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 19:1" />Ke ini Apọlọs akebaaha ke Kọrint, Pọọl amaasaña usʌñ esịd abio akewuọ Efisọs. Ke udo anye amaakekịt usʌk mme andinịm ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 19:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 19:2" />Anye amaanyʌñ abịp ammọ abo, “Ndufo emaebọ Adisana Sịbidịd idaha e-ekenịmme ke akpanikọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 19:2">Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Iyoo, kpaanam ñnyịn ikoppo ke Adisana Sịbidịd aba.”<verse eid="ACT 19:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 19:3" />Ndin Pọọl amaabịp ammọ abo, “Nsoo utọ uduọkmmọọñ ke ndufo ekebọọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 19:3">Ammọ emaebọọrọ ebo, “Uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn.”<verse eid="ACT 19:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 19:4" />Pọọl amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Uduọkmmọọñ Yọọn akedo ake utua ñkpọfiọk ñkappaesịd. Yọọn akebo yak mme awo enịm anye a-adiidi ikeene imọ ke akpanikọ, a-adooho Yisọs.” <verse eid="ACT 19:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 19:5" />Ammọ ekekop ami, emaeduọk ammọ mmọọñ ke anyịñ Abọọñ Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 19:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 19:6" />Ke ini Pọọl akedotto ammọ ubọk ke iwuod, Adisana Sịbidịd amaasọiyọ adoro ammọ, ndin ammọ emaetọọñọ adisem mme usem ñnyʌñ ntañ prọfesi. <verse eid="ACT 19:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 19:7" />Ñkpọ nte ideen duob mme iba ekeba do.<verse eid="ACT 19:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 19:8" />Pọọl amaadʌk sinakọk anyʌñ akwọrọ ikọ uko-uko ke afiọñ ita, atañ ikọ abaña abioubọọñ Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 19:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 19:9" />Ado ubaak ammọ emaesọñ iwuod enyʌñ esịn adinịm ke akpanikọ, etaañ mme ndiọi ikọ ebaña ikọd Krais anwa-anwa. Ndin Pọọl amaakpọñ ammọ. Anye amaakoono mme mbed anyʌñ asinie nneme ye ammọ ke usen ke usen ke ufọk ukpeebñkpọ ke Tairanus. <verse eid="ACT 19:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 19:10" />Ami amaakaa iso ke isua iba, tutu afịd mme Yuu ye mbon Greek e-ekedʌññọ ke ñkañ Esia ekop ikọ Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 19:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 19:11" />Abasi amaadat Pọọl anam mme asaña-asaña utịppeñkpọ. <verse eid="ACT 19:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 19:12" />Mbon udọñọ emaekop nsọñidem, ebọ ñkpọkñyak, ndiọi sịbidịd enyʌñ ekpọñ mbon ñkpọnsọb ke emaeketuuk afọñinua ye eprọn a-aketuuho Pọọl idem.<verse eid="ACT 19:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 19:13" />Ado ndusʌk mme Yuu e-ekesaañake esịññe mme ndiọi sịbidịd emaedomo adikoot anyịñ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Yisọs ndot ke iwuod mbon a-dimọn akesịnne ukad. Ammọ emaebo, “Ke anyịñ Yisọs, a-Pọọl akwọrọke, ami mmiwuuk ndufo, nte iwuọñọ.” <verse eid="ACT 19:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 19:14" />Atu mbon se ikisikeene inañña ñkpọ ami ekedo nditọ ideen Sefa itiaba. Sefa akedo ekamba aku mme Yuu. <verse eid="ACT 19:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 19:15" />Usen keed idiọọk sịbidịd amaabọọrọ ammọ ate, “Yisọs, ami mmediọọñọ, ñnyʌñ ndiọọñọ Pọọl, ndin ndufo edoñño mme anie?” <verse eid="ACT 19:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 19:16" />Ndin, awo a-akenieghe idiọọk sịbidịd ami amaatamma amuum ammọ anyʌñ akan ammọ keedekeed, anekke atiim ammọ tutu ammọ efeeñe ifed ewuọñọ ke ufọk, ye iyiib ke idem.<verse eid="ACT 19:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 19:17" />Ke ini mme Yuu ye mbon Greek e-ekedʌññọ ke Efisọs ekenieghe ifiọk ebaña ñkpọ ami, ndịk amaanam ammọ, ndin anyịñ Abọọñ Yisọs amaanekke anie ekamba uteñe. <verse eid="ACT 19:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 19:18" />Uwak mbon se ikinịm Abasi ke akpanikọ emaewuọñọ edi, ediyaara mme ndiọiñkpọ ammọ anwa-anwa. <verse eid="ACT 19:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 19:19" />Uwak mbon se ikisibre idiọñ emaekoono ñwed ibọk ammọ edifọọmọ anwa-anwa. Ke emaekedian ekọmudua mme ñwed ami, amaasịm silfa tọsịn aba mme duob. <verse eid="ACT 19:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 19:20" />Ke utọ usʌñ ami, ikọ Abasi amaasuana, atara, anyʌñ akọt ke adudu.<verse eid="ACT 19:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 19:21" />Ke afịd mme ñkpọ ami emaekeboiyo, Pọọl amaabiide ke esịd amọ adika Yeruselem, asaña aboiyo ke Masidonia ye Akaya. Ndin anye amaabo, “Ami mmaakewuọ udo, ana nte nsaña ñkesịm Rom ñko.” <verse eid="ACT 19:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 19:22" />Anye amaanọ mbon unwam amọ iba, Timoti ye Erastus, eka Masidonia, ke ini anye akebaaha etək ini ke Esia.<verse eid="ACT 19:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ekamba Ntịme ke Efisọs</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 19:23" />Ke ñkpọ nte ukem ini ado ekamba mfịna amaatịppe ke abaña ikọd Krais. <verse eid="ACT 19:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 19:24" />Demitrus, awo a-akesinamma usọ silfa ake Atemis, amaadat uwak ndubeghe asọk mme anam usọ do. <verse eid="ACT 19:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 19:25" />Anye amaakoot mbono mme anam usọ ye mbon mfen e-ekesinamma utọ utom ado ate, “Mme ufan mmi, ndufo emediọọñọ ke ubọkutom a-ñnyịn inamma a-anekke asịne udod. <verse eid="ACT 19:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 19:26" />Ndufo emekịt enyʌñ ekop naña awo e-ekoodo Pọọl asaña mi akpuuño mme awo esịd anyʌñ abiaña ammọ, idooho mi ke Efisọs ikpọọñ, ado ke afịd ikpeghe Esia. Anye abo ke mme abasi e-ebotto ke ubọk idoññoke abasi ndomokeed. <verse eid="ACT 19:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 19:27" />Afanekọñ a-aba, idooho ke ubiad ndubeghe ñnyịn ikpọọñ, ado sia anye a-asịn tembịd ekamba eka abasi Atemis ye anye eka abasi ke ndek, ndin uteeñe ye ubọọñ eka abasi ami e-ekponoke ke afịd Esia ye afịd ederimbod ayaasop.”<verse eid="ACT 19:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 19:28" />Ke ammọ adikop ami, ammọ emaebịmme ke ifiobesịd, etọọñọ adibọọñ, “Ubọọñ anie Atemis ake Efisọs!” <verse eid="ACT 19:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 19:29" />Ndin ntịme amaatara ayọhọ afịd abio, mbon awo emaesọsọp ekaiya afe abio ekemʌm nsaña Pọọl, Keyọs ye Aristakus, e-eketooho Masidonia ekaiya udo. <verse eid="ACT 19:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 19:30" />Pọọl amaayem adidʌk ñkaa ñkesoobo ye atu awo, ado mme mbed ikiyakka anye aka. <verse eid="ACT 19:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 19:31" />Kpa ubaak mme akama ukara abio ado, e-ekedooho mme ufan Pọọl, emaedọñ edikpeiye anye ete akuudeedei akaa afe abio.<verse eid="ACT 19:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 19:32" />Ntịme amaakpon ke afe abio: Mme awo emaebọọñ ñkpo ntịme-ntịme, ebọñ ebaña ñkpọ anyem, ebọñ ebaña anye ako. Ataa uwak awo ikidiọọñọke se ikinam mmimọ ikaiya itie ado ke akpa ifed. <verse eid="ACT 19:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 19:33" />Ndin mme Yuu e-ekebaaha ke atu mme awo emaenək Aleksanda esio nọ akeda ke iso atu awo enyʌñ ebọọñ edọkkọ anye se akpenam. Aleksanda amaadịppe ubọk abo edop uyio nọ imọ itañ ikọ. <verse eid="ACT 19:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 19:34" />Ado ammọ ekediọọñọ ke anye ado Yuu, afịd ammọ emaekaa iso ebọñ uyio keed ke ñkpọ nte awa iba, ete: “Atemis Efisọs a-akpon!”<verse eid="ACT 19:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 19:35" />Ke akpatre, awedñwed abio amaakpan uyom, anyʌñ abo: “Mbon Efisọs ñnyịn, nte afịd ederimbod idiọọñọke ke abio Efisọs ado itie a-anaaha ekpeme tembịd ekamba Atemis ye usioidem amọ a-aketooho hefịn adiduọ? <verse eid="ACT 19:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 19:36" />Sia ndufo emaediọọñọ ke ñkpọ ami ado akpanikọ, ufọn adifịna idem me adinam ñkpọ nte mme anana akikere ibaaha. <verse eid="ACT 19:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 19:37" />Ndufo ekeben ibon ami edi mi, akpesʌkado a-ammọ imiiyịppe ñkpọ ke tembịd, inyʌññọ isappa eka abasi ñnyịn. <verse eid="ACT 19:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 19:38" />Ndin adieke Demitrus ye emọ-emọ mme anam usọ enieghe ntuaha ye awo ndomokeed <char style="add">(isʌñutom Krais)</char>, mme esob mmọdo, mme akama ukara ñko mmọdo. Yak ammọ esịn ikpe ke esob. <verse eid="ACT 19:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 19:39" />Akpedo mfịna mfen aba, ana eben eka afe mbed abio. <verse eid="ACT 19:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 19:40" />Sia naña aba ami, ekeme adiben ñnyịn ñkaa esob ke abaña se itịppe mfịn ami. Akpetịppe ntoro, ñnyịn idiikanna ifaaña ibọkkọ sia ntak ndomokeed ibaaha.” <verse eid="ACT 19:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 19:41" />Anye aketañ ami ama, anye amaasuan afe abio.<verse eid="ACT 19:41" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 19" />
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="ACT 20" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akaa Masidonia ye Greece</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 20:1" />Ke ini ntịme ami amaaketre, Pọọl amaadọñ ekoot mme mbed, ndin ke anye amaakenọ ammọ ikọ nsọọñọidem ama, anye amaakọọm ammọ unyọñ, ndin amaadakka isañ akaa Masidonia. <verse eid="ACT 20:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 20:2" />Anye amaasaña akanna afịd ukañ udo anọ mme awo uwak ikọ nsọọñọidem, ndin ke akpatre amaakewuọ Greece, <verse eid="ACT 20:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 20:3" />itie a-anye akebaaha afiọñ ita. Sia ubaak mme Yuu emaekedioomo adinam anye idiọọkñkpọ kpa ke ini anye akeyemme isaña mmọọñ ñkaa Siria, anye amaatịmme edem, adisaña aboiyo ke Masidonia. <verse eid="ACT 20:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 20:4" />Sopata, ayịn Pairọs a-aketooho Beria, Aristakus ye Sekundus, e-eketooho Tesalọnika, Keyọs awo Deebi, Timoti, Taikikọs ye Trofimus, mbio ikpeghe ukara Esia, emaekeene anye ñko. <verse eid="ACT 20:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 20:5" />Mbon ami emaebem iso ekibet ñnyịn ke Troas. <verse eid="ACT 20:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 20:6" />Ado ñnyịn imaisio uwad ikpọñ Filipai ke Usọrọ Uyo a-Yiis Miisịneke amaakeboiyo, ndin ke usen ition emaekeboiyo, ñnyịn imaikisoobo ye ammọ ke Troas inyʌñ iba ye ammọ usen itiaba.<verse eid="ACT 20:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Enam Yutikọs Aset ke Ñkpa ke Troas</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 20:7" />Ke akpa usen udua, ñnyịn imaisoobo adibuuñ uyo. Pọọl amaatañ ikọ anọ mme awo, ndin sia akenaaha anye akpọñ edem usen, anye amaakaa iso atañ ikọ tutu ufọọd akonayio. <verse eid="ACT 20:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 20:8" />Mme utuenikañ emaewak ke ubeed ufọk anyọñ a-ñnyịn ikibonoke. <verse eid="ACT 20:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 20:9" />Akparawa keed a-akekereke Yutikọs aketie ke ubenafịm, ndin akpọsọñ idab amaamʌm anye naña Pọọl akesʌkkọ akaiso atañ ikọ akpeene; ndin anye amaato ke ayọhọ anyọñ ita adiañña adiduọ ke isọñ, ado ke ini edikaaha ekebenne anye, anye amaakpakpa. <verse eid="ACT 20:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 20:10" />Pọọl amaasọiyọo akaa isọñ, akeduọ afʌk anye anyʌñ adot anye ubọk ke afara ate: “Ikiiyak idem inyeñ, anye a-adu uwem!” <verse eid="ACT 20:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 20:11" />Ndin Pọọl amaatịmme adọọk anyọñ akebuuñ uyo ata. Ke amaaketañ ikọ ye ammọ tutu usiere, anye amaakpọñ ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 20:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 20:12" />Ammọ emaeben akparawa ado enyọñ ye uwem ke akwa inemesịd.<verse eid="ACT 20:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akọọm mme Adaiwuod Ufọkabasi ke Efisọs Unyọñ</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 20:13" />Ñnyịn imaika iso iwat ke nsʌñikañ, ika abio Asọs nọ ñnyịn ikiben Pọọl. Anye akebo ñnyịn inam ntom sia anye akesaña ke ukod akaa Troas. <verse eid="ACT 20:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 20:14" />Ndin ke anye amaakedisoobo ye ñnyịn ke Asọs, ñnyịn imaiben anye ke nsʌñikañ ika Mitiliin. <verse eid="ACT 20:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 20:15" />Edem usen, imaisio uwat ikiwuọ nsakiso Kiọs. Edem usen, ñnyịn imaikiwuọ Samos; ndin usen keed amaakeboiyo, ñnyịn imaikiwuọ Miletus. <verse eid="ACT 20:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 20:16" />Pọọl amaabiide adiwat mboiyo Efisọs, mbaak anye adikibiat ini ke ukañ Esia, sia anye akebaaha itọk-itọk abo yak ise me iyaikan ikiwuọ Yeruselem ke usen Pentikọs.<verse eid="ACT 20:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 20:17" />Ke Miletus, anye amaadọñ eka Efisọs ekekoot mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi inọ imọ. <verse eid="ACT 20:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 20:18" />Ammọ emaekedi, anye amaabo ammọ ate: “Ndufo emediọọñọ tọọñọ ke akpa usen a-ami ñketọọhọ ñkpad ke Esia, naña ami ñkedu uwem ye ndufo afịd ini. <verse eid="ACT 20:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 20:19" />Ami mmaanam utom nnọ Abasi ke ataa nsuukidem ye mmọọñayịd, ke ufọọd akpọsọñ idomo a-aketooho mme ndịbe-ndịbe edioomo ibak a-mme Yuu ekenieghe embaña miin. <verse eid="ACT 20:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 20:20" />Ndufo emediọọñọ ke ami ñkibiada ini adikwọrọ mbaña ñkpọ keed akeedodo a-adiinwam ndufo, ado ñkikpeep ndufo anwa-anwa ñnyʌñ nsaña ke ufọk ke ufọk. <verse eid="ACT 20:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 20:21" />Ami mmekwọrọ nnọ mme Yuu ye mme Greek nte ammọ ekappa esịd ekeene Abasi, enyʌñ enie mbuọdidem ke Abọọñ ñnyịn Yisọs.<verse eid="ACT 20:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 20:22" />“Idahami, ami mmedakka naña Sịbidịd andat miin usʌñ, ñkaa Yeruselem. Ndiọọñọke se idiikitịppe innọ miin ke udo. <verse eid="ACT 20:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 20:23" />Ukweeñe se ami ndiọọñọ ado ke kwa abio, Adisana Sịbidịd andʌt utọñ abo ke ñkpakọb ye ukuud mmọdo ena embet. <verse eid="ACT 20:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 20:24" />Kpayeado, ami mmebiire ke mbatta uwem mmi ke baaba ñkpọ ndomokeed, ñkpekap ñkan mfeghe nduba mmi mma, ñnyʌñ ñkweeñe utom a-Abọọñ Yisọs annọọhọ miin, utom aditie ntiense nnọọ eti etob a-atooho ke mfọn Abasi.<verse eid="ACT 20:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 20:25" />“Idahami, ami mmediọọñọ ke ibaaha awo ndomokeed ke atu ndufo a-ami ñkekwọrọke etob abioubọọñ Abasi nnọ a-adiimaana iñkịt miin iso aba. <verse eid="ACT 20:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 20:26" />Ke ntoro, ami idọkkọ ndufo mfịn ami ke ami nnieghe ubiomikpe ke iyiib awo ndufo ndomokeed. <verse eid="ACT 20:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 20:27" />Sia ami ñkidaaha edem ke adikwọrọ mme uduak Abasi inọọ ndufo. <verse eid="ACT 20:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 20:28" />Ikpeme idem ndufo ye afịd atu edọñ a-Adisana Sịbidịd inịmme ndufo nte mme andikpeme, ido mme akpemeedọñ ufọk Abasi<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ataa uwak ikpañwed ewet </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ake </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Abọọñ</char></note> a-anye akedeppe ke iyiib<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Usʌk ebo </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ye </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">iyiib Ayịn amọ awodeen</char></note> amọ. <verse eid="ACT 20:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 20:29" />Ami mmediọọñọ ke mmaakpọñ, mme ndiọi ewaikọd eyaedʌk ke atu ndufo, idiinyʌññọ itua atu edọñ mbọm. <verse eid="ACT 20:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 20:30" />Kpa ke atu ndufo, mme awo eyaedakka eda, etañ nduyʌttọ ikọ nọ ekan edʌt mme mbed enọ idem ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 20:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 20:31" />Ikpeme ndin! Itoiyo ke afịd isua ita a-ami ñkebaaha ye ndufo, ami ñketreke adidʌt afịd awo utọñ akonayio ye uweemeayio ke mmọọñayịd.<verse eid="ACT 20:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 20:32" />“Idahami, ami mmiyaak ndufo nnọ Abasi ye ikọ mfọn amọ a-akanna inọọ ndufo adudu nsọọñọnda, anyʌñ inọ ndufo udeeme ke atu mbon e-enamma esana. <verse eid="ACT 20:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 20:33" />Ami nsịnne anyen ke silfa me kold me afọñ awo ndomokeed. <verse eid="ACT 20:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 20:34" />Ndufo ke idem ndufo emediọọñọ ke ñkedat ubọk mmi ami ñnwana idem ñyem se iñkem ye se ikem mbon nsaña mmi. <verse eid="ACT 20:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 20:35" />Ke afịd ñkpọ se ami ñkenam, ami ñkiwọt ndufo ke ato ke akpọsọñ utom ntom ke ñnyịn inie adinwam mbon mmemidem, inyʌñ itoiyo ikọ a-Abọọñ Yisọs akebooho ate: <char style="wj">‘a-Afọn adinọnọ akan adibọbọ.’</char> ”<verse eid="ACT 20:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 20:36" />Ndin ke Pọọl amaaketañ ikọ ama, anye amaatọọñọ edọñ ye afịd ammọ abọñ akam. <verse eid="ACT 20:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 20:37" />Afịd ammọ emaetuaha, efat Pọọl enyʌñ etʌm anye inua. <verse eid="ACT 20:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 20:38" />Ammọ emaefʌhọ akpan-akpan ebaña ikọ a-anye aketañña abo ke ammọ idiikịtte anye iso aba. Ndin ammọ emaedat anye isañ ekesuuk ke nsʌñikañ.<verse eid="ACT 20:38" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 20" />
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="ACT 21" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akaa Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 21:1" />Ke ñnyịn imaikidaaña ikpọñ ammọ, imaikpọñ esʌk inyʌñ iwat nnen-nnen ika Kọs. Imaikaa Rodes edem usen, inyʌñ ito do ika Patara. <verse eid="ACT 21:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 21:2" />Imaikịt nsʌñikañ nte aboiyo aka Fonisia, ndin ñnyịn imaidʌk do inyʌñ isio uwad. <verse eid="ACT 21:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 21:3" />Ke ñnyịn imaikida ikịt Saiprọs, imaiwọññọ idʌk usuuk amọ, iwat iboiyo ika Siria. Ñnyịn imaibeghe ke Tai, sia ke udo ke akena nsʌñikañ ñnyịn akesịññe mbiomo. <verse eid="ACT 21:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 21:4" />Ñnyịn imaiyem mme mbed do ikịt, imainyʌñ iba ye ammọ usen itiaba. Ato ke se Sịbidịd akeyaara, ammọ emaedọkkọ Pọọl ete yak anye akuukaa Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 21:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 21:5" />Ado ke ini ñnyịn amaakekem adikpọñ, ñnyịn imainyọñọ inyʌñ ika iso ke usʌñ isañ ñnyịn. Afịd mme mbed, ñkọrọ ibaan ammọ ye nditọ ammọ emaidat ñnyịn isañ ewuọ ke abio, ndin ñnyịn imaitọọñọ edọñ do ke esʌk ibọñ akam. <verse eid="ACT 21:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 21:6" />Ke imaikikọọm afịd awo unyọñ, ñnyịn imaikidʌk nsʌñikañ ndin ammọ emaetịmme enyọñ ufọk.<verse eid="ACT 21:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 21:7" />Ñnyịn imaikaiso ke isañ ñnyịn ito Tai idikibeghe ke Tolemais, a-ñnyịn ikikọọmọ mme nditọeka ke Krais inyʌñ itie ye ammọ usen keed. <verse eid="ACT 21:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 21:8" />Ke imaikinyọñ edem usen, ñnyịn imaikisịm Siseria inyʌñ iba ke ufọk Filib akwọrọ eti etob, keed ke atu awo itiaba ado. <verse eid="ACT 21:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 21:9" />Anye amaanie nditọ ibaan inaañ i-imiikidọiyọ ebe, e-ekesitañña prọfesi.<verse eid="ACT 21:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 21:10" />Ke ñnyịn imaikiba do uwak usen, prọfed keed a-akekereke Akabọs amaato Yudia adi. <verse eid="ACT 21:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 21:11" />Ke anye amaakesaña adi itie ñnyịn, amaaben ñkpaha isịn Pọọl abọp ubọk ye ukod amọ anyʌñ abo ate, “Adisana Sịbidịd abo ate, ‘Ntom ke mme Yuu ke Yeruselem ediibọp andinie ñkpaha ami, eyaenyʌñ eyaak anye enọ mme Gentile.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 21:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 21:12" />Ke ñnyịn imaikikop ñkpọ ami, ñnyịn ye mbon udo imaikpeiye Pọọl ite yak anye akuukaa Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 21:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 21:13" />Ndin Pọọl amaabọọrọ ate, “Nsinam nọ ndufo etua enyʌñ enam esịd anduọ? Ami mmebeeñe idem, idooho nọ embọọp ke idʌk kpọd, ado adikpa ke Yeruselem ke ntak anyịñ Abọọñ Yisọs.” <verse eid="ACT 21:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 21:14" />Ke ini ñnyịn imiikikanna ikpʌhọ anye esịd, ñnyịn imaisịññe idem ikpọñ, inyʌñ ibo, “Yak uduak Abọọñ adat itie.”<verse eid="ACT 21:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 21:15" />Ke ado amaakeboiyo, ñnyịn imaitʌm idem, inyʌñ idọọk ika Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 21:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 21:16" />Usʌk ke atu mme ntiense e-eketooho Siseria emaesaña ye ñnyịn tọọñọ ke Siseria enyʌñ iben ñnyịn ekaa ufọk Mmasọn, itie a-akenaaha ñnyịn iba. Anye akedo awo Saiprọs ye keed ke atu mme ataa akpa ntiense.<verse eid="ACT 21:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akewuọ Yeruselem</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 21:17" />Ke ñnyịn imaikidiwuọ Yeruselem, mme nditọeka ke Krais emaedaara adidi ñnyịn. <verse eid="ACT 21:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 21:18" />Edem usen Pọọl ye ñnyịn imaikaa ikise Yems, ndin afịd mme adaiwuod ufọkabasi emaeba. <verse eid="ACT 21:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 21:19" />Pọọl amaakọọm ammọ, anyʌñ atañ ayọhọ-ayọhọ se Abasi akenam ke atu mme Gentile ato ke utom amọ.<verse eid="ACT 21:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 21:20" />Ke ammọ emaekekop ami, ammọ emaetooro Abasi. Ndin ammọ emaebo Pọọl: “Ayịneka, akpakʌb uwak tọsịn mme Yuu e-enịm ke akpanikọ, ndin afịd ammọ enie ekamba udọñ ke abaña mbed. <verse eid="ACT 21:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 21:21" />Ado emaetañ enọ ammọ ete ke afo akpeep afịd mme Yuu e-edʌññọ ke atu mme Gentile ate ewọññọ ekpọñ mbed Moses, ekuufọọrọ nditọ ammọ edʌd, ekuunyʌñ edu uwem ekeene eduuwem ñnyịn. <verse eid="ACT 21:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 21:22" />Nsoo ke ñnyịn idiinam? Ammọ, ke akpanikọ, eyaekop ke afo amedi. <verse eid="ACT 21:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 21:23" />Ndin, nam se ñnyịn udọkkọ fiin. Mme ideen inaañ mmọdo ye ñnyịn e-ekenamma akaaña. <verse eid="ACT 21:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 21:24" />Ben ideen ami, wuana ye ammọ ke usọrọ adinam idem asana nyʌñ kpe akʌk a-anaaha nte ammọ ekpe nọ ato do ammọ ekan enam nọ efat ided iwuod ammọ. Ndin afịd awo eyaediọọñọ ke akpanikọ ndomokeed isịneke ke mme ikọ e-etañña udian fiin, ado ke afo ke idem mfo asʌk adu uwem ke nsuukiwuod anọ mbed. <verse eid="ACT 21:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 21:25" />Amaado mme Gentile e-enịmme ke akpanikọ, ñnyịn imiwet se ñnyịn ikibiire inọ esọk ammọ ite yak ammọ ediañña idem ekpọñ ndidia e-ewaaha enọ ndem, ekpọñ adita iyiib, ekpọñ unam e-efiakkakefiakka itọñ ewot, enyʌñ ekpọñ use ye efịbe.”<verse eid="ACT 21:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 21:26" />Edem usen, Pọọl amaanam idem amọ asana ye mme ideen ado. Ndin anye amaakaa tembịd adinọ ntọd mbaña usen ye ini se adinam unam idem ammọ asana adiitre, nọ enam uwa enọ ammọ keedekeed.<verse eid="ACT 21:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Emʌm Pọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 21:27" />Ke akeyakka etək ini usen itiaba ado adikweeñe, usʌk mme Yuu e-eketooho ikpeghe Esia emaekịt Pọọl ke tembịd. Ammọ emaenam afịd atu awo esịn ntịme ndin emaemʌm Pọọl, <verse eid="ACT 21:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 21:28" />enyʌñ esio ñkpo ete, “Mbon Isrel ñnyịn, inwam ñnyịn! Awo ami ado andikpeeb mme awo ke afịd itie se imiidooho ke ufọn mbon ñnyịn ye mbed ñnyịn, ye itie ami. Ndin ke akanna ado, anye a-aben mbon Greek adʌk tembịd anyʌñ asappa adisana itie ami.” <verse eid="ACT 21:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 21:29" />(Ammọ emaedadak ekịt Trofimus a-aketooho Efisọs ye Pọọl ke abio, ndin ekekere ke Pọọl akeben anye adʌk adi tembịd.)<verse eid="ACT 21:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 21:30" />Ntịme amaadʌk afịd abio, ndin mme awo emaefeeñe eto nsio-nsio itie edi. Emaemʌm Pọọl, edʌt anye esio ke tembịd; ini keed ini keed emaebeet mme inuaatob. <verse eid="ACT 21:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 21:31" />Ke ini ammọ ekenwanake adiwot anye, etob amaakewuọ adaiso ekọñ Rom ate ke abio Yeruselem akeba ke ataa ekamba ntịme. <verse eid="ACT 21:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 21:32" />Idaha-idaha ado, adaiso ekọñ amaakoono mme ikpọawo ekọñ ye mbon ekọñ efeeñe edọñọ atu awo. Ke mme asịn ntịme ami emaekekịt adaiso ekọñ ye mbon ekọñ amọ, ammọ emaetre aditịm Pọọl.<verse eid="ACT 21:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 21:33" />Adaiso ekọñ amaasaña adi, anyʌñ amʌm Pọọl anọ uyio ate ebọp anye ke ñkpọnọ iba. Ndin anye amaabịp me Pọọl ado anie, ñko me nsoo ke anye akenam. <verse eid="ACT 21:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 21:34" />Usʌk ke atu awo emaebọọñ ñkpọ ke usʌñ keed, usʌk ke usʌñ mfen, ndin sia adaiso ekọñ imiikikanna ibọ akpanikọ ato ke ntak akpọsọñ uyom, anye amaanọ uyio ate eben Pọọl ekesịn ke badịk ekọñ. <verse eid="ACT 21:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 21:35" />Ke Pọọl amaakesịm udodukod, afai ke atu awo amaakpon tutu akena mbon ekọñ ededịppe anye. <verse eid="ACT 21:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 21:36" />Atu awo se ikikeene emaekaa iso ebọọñ, “Iben anye isio!”<verse eid="ACT 21:36" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Atañ Ikọ Anọ Atu Awo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 21:37" />Ndin ke ini mbon ekọñ ekeyemme ediben Pọọl ndʌk ñkaa badịk ekọñ, anye amaabịp adaiso ekọñ ate, “Akpaayak nọ ntañ ikọ unọ?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 21:37">Anye amaabọọrọ abo, “Awuọ afo amenọ usem Krik isem? <verse eid="ACT 21:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 21:38" />Idooho afo ado awo Iyib a-aketọọñọke nsọñiwuod ye ukara anyʌñ akoono mbon afai tọsịn inaañ aka anaan ini keed ko?”<verse eid="ACT 21:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 21:39" />Pọọl amaabọọrọ ate, “Ami ndo Yuu. Nto Tasọs ke Silisia, amanaisọñ ataa ñwuọnda idʌñ. Mbọk yak ami ntañ ikọ nnọ atu awo.”<verse eid="ACT 21:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 21:40" />Ke Pọọl amaakebọ adudu ato adaiso ekọñ, anye amaada ke udodukod anam idiọọñọ ke ubọk anọ atu awo. Ke afịd awo emaekedop uyio, anye amaatañ anọ ammọ ke usem Aramaik:<verse eid="ACT 21:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 21" />
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="ACT 22" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 22:1" />“Nditọete ideen ye mme ete, ikpañ utọñ ndin nọ ñkañ idem mmi.”<verse eid="ACT 22:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 22:2" />Ke ammọ emaekekop naña anye atañ ikọ anọ ammọ ke usem Aramaik ammọ emaenekke enọ ñkpañutọñ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:2">Do ke Pọọl akebo ate: <verse eid="ACT 22:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 22:3" />Ami ndo awo Yuu, ñkemana ke Tasọs ke Silisia, ado ñkedikpon ke abio ami. Ami ñkebọ ataa ayọhọ ukpeeb nto Kamaliel ke mbed mme eteete ñnyịn. Mmaamʌm ñnyʌñ nsịn idem ke abaña ñkpọ Abasi ukem nte afịd ndufo enamma mfịn ami. <verse eid="ACT 22:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 22:4" />Ami mmaakọbọ mme andikeene usʌñ Krais ami tutu akesịm ñkpa. Mmaamuum ideen ye ibaan ñnyʌñ ntop ammọ ndọñ ke ufọk ñkpakọb, <verse eid="ACT 22:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 22:5" />kpa nte ekamba aku ye afịd ñkpoon mbon Esob e-edoññoke Yuu ekemeke editie ntiense mbaña. Ami mmaabọ ñwed nto ammọ ñko nọ ñkoono nsọk mme nsaña ammọ ke Damaskọs; ndin ñkeka do adiben mbon se ikiba do ñnyọñ ndi Yeruselem nte mbon ñkpakọb nọ edinọ ammọ ufen.<verse eid="ACT 22:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 22:6" />“Ke ñkpọ nte ufọọd uweemeayio, ke ñkanika duob mme iba, ke mmaakedikpere Damaskọs, ekamba unwana ikañ a-aketooho hefịn amaayamma inikeed inikeed añkanna miin akʌk. <verse eid="ACT 22:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 22:7" />Ami mmaaduọ ke isọñ, ñnyʌñ ñkop naña uyio ambo miin ate, <char style="wj">‘Sọọl, Sọọl, nsoo ido ntak a-afo añkọbọke miin?’</char><verse eid="ACT 22:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 22:8" />“Ami mmaabọọrọ, ‘Afo ado anie, Abọọñ?’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:8">“Anye amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">‘Ami ndo Yisọs, awo Nasared a-afo akọbọke.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 22:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 22:9" />Mbon e-ekesañake ye ami emaekịt unwana ikañ, ado ammọ ikidiọọñọke uyio andikitañ ikọ ye ami.<verse eid="ACT 22:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 22:10" />“Ami mmaabịp mbo, ‘Abọọñ, nsoo ke ami ndiinam?’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:10">“Ndin Abọọñ amaambo, <char style="wj">‘Dakka da, ñnyʌñ kaa Damaskọs. Ke udo eyaekudọkkọ afịd se e-emaekenịm ebo yak afo anam.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 22:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 22:11" />Ndin sia ami mmiikikanna ñkịt ñkpọ ato ke unwana ikañ ado, mme nsaña mmi emaemmʌm miin ubọk, tutu ami ñkewuọ Damaskọs.<verse eid="ACT 22:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 22:12" />“Awo keed a-akekereke Ananayas amaadinse miin. Anye amaasiteeñe Abasi ayọhọ-ayọhọ nte mbed atemmeke, ñko afịd mme Yuu e-ekedʌññọ do emaekpono anye eti-eti, enyʌñ etañ nti ikọ ebaña anye. <verse eid="ACT 22:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 22:13" />Anye amaadida añkpere miin, anyʌñ abo, ‘Ayịneka mmi Sọọl, mọọnọ ñkpọ!’ Ndin ami mmaamọọnọ anye kpa ke idaha ado.<verse eid="ACT 22:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 22:14" />“Akema anye amaabo: ‘Abasi mme eteete ñnyịn amaumek fiin nọ afo adiọọñọ uduak amọ anyʌñ akịt Andido Andinen, anyʌñ akop mme ikọ ato inua amọ. <verse eid="ACT 22:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 22:15" />Afo ayaado ntiense amọ anọ afịd awo ke abaña se afo akịt ye se akop. <verse eid="ACT 22:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 22:16" />Ndin idahami nsoo ke afo ada abet? Dakka da, bọ uduọkmmọọñ nyʌñ yet mme idiọọkñkpọ mfo fep ke adikoot anyịñ amọ.’<verse eid="ACT 22:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 22:17" />“Ke ini ami mmaaketịmme ñnyọñ Yeruselem, nsʌk mbọñ akam ke tembịd, ami mmaakịt ñkukịd, <verse eid="ACT 22:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 22:18" />ñnyʌñ ñkịt naña Abọọñ atañ ikọ annọ miin. Anye amaambo miin ate, <char style="wj">‘Sọp idem kpọñ Yeruselem ini keed sia mme awo mi idiinyịmmeke ikọ ntiense mfo ambañake miin.’</char><verse eid="ACT 22:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 22:19" />“Ami mmaabọọrọ nte, ‘Abọọñ, ibon ami e-ediọọñọ ke ami ñkesisaña ke sinakọk ke sinakọk adisịn ke ufọk ñkpakọb ñnyʌñ mmia mbon u-unịmme fiin ke akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 22:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 22:20" />Ñko ke ini ekeduọkkọ iyiib Stifịn, e-ekewotto ke ntak akedooho ntiense ke mbuọdidem amọ ke afo, ami ñkeda do nnọ unyịmme, ñnyʌñ ñkpeme mme afọñidem mbon e-ekewotto anye.’<verse eid="ACT 22:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 22:21" />“Ndin Abọọñ amaambo miin ate, <char style="wj">‘Kaa, ami ñyaunọ fiin aka anyan usʌñ abịne mme Gentile.’</char> ”<verse eid="ACT 22:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Amanaisọñ Ayịn Rom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 22:22" />Atu awo emaenọ Pọọl ñkpañutọñ tutu anye atañ ikọ amọ ama. Ndin ammọ emaebenne uyio esio ñkpo, ete: “Yak eben awo ami esio ke iso isọñ! Anye idotto adidu uwem!”<verse eid="ACT 22:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 22:23" />Ke ammọ ekesʌkkọ ebọñ ñkpọ, enyʌñ etoomo mme afọñ ammọ esio ntọñ ke anyọñ, <verse eid="ACT 22:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 22:24" />adaiso ekọñ amaanọ uyio ate eben Pọọl ekesịn ke badịk ekọñ. Anye amaanọ uyio ate emia Pọọl enyʌñ eduuñọ anye nọ anye atañ ntak a-mme awo ekebọññọ ñkpo ebaña anye ntom. <verse eid="ACT 22:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 22:25" />Naña enyannake anye enịm adimia ke ikpa, Pọọl amaabịp sentudiọn a-akedaaha do abo, “Nte mbed a-ayak nọ ndufo emia amanaisọñ awo Rom ke ini awo imiibiommo anye ikpe diin?”<verse eid="ACT 22:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 22:26" />Sentudiọn akekop ami, anye amaabịne adaiso ekọñ aketañ anọ anye abo: “Nsoo ke afo adiinam? Awo ami ado amanaisọñ awo Rom.”<verse eid="ACT 22:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 22:27" />Adaiso ekọñ amaabịne Pọọl anyʌñ akebịp abo, “Tañ nnọ ise, nte afo ado amanaisọñ awo Rom?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:27">Anye amaabọọrọ ate, “Ii, se ndo adodo.”<verse eid="ACT 22:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 22:28" />Ndin adaiso ekọñ amaabo ate, “Akena ami ñkpe uwak akʌk nọ enam nọ ami ndo amanaisọñ.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:28">Pọọl amaabọọrọ abo, “Ado ami ndo amanaisọñ tọọñọ ke emana.”<verse eid="ACT 22:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 22:29" />Mbon e-ekenaaha nte ebịp anye mbuume emaesịññe idem ekpọñ anye ataa idahado. Adaiso ekọñ ke idem amọ amaadịkke, ke anye amaakedidiọọñọ ke anye akesịn Pọọl amanaisọñ awo Rom ke ñkpọnọ ukwak.<verse eid="ACT 22:29" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl ke Iso Sanhidrin</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 22:30" />Adaiso ekọñ amaayem adiduuñọ ndiọọñọ ataa akpan ntak a-mme Yuu ekedotto Pọọl ikọ. Ndin, ke edem usen, anye amaasaana Pọọl ayaak, anyʌñ anọ uyio abo yak mme ñkpoon aku ye mbon esob Sanhidrin edʌk mbono. Ndin anye amaaben Pọọl adi anyʌñ anam anye ada ke iso ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 22:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 22" />
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="ACT 23" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 23:1" />Pọọl amaawuuk anyen ase mbon esob Sanhidrin anyʌñ abo ammọ ate, “Nditọeka mmi, ami mmenam iso utom mmi nnọ Abasi ke eti esịd tutu usen mfịn ami.” <verse eid="ACT 23:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 23:2" />Anye aketañ ntoro, ekamba aku Ananayas amaanọ uyio abo mbon e-ekedaaha ekpere Pọọl emia anye inua. <verse eid="ACT 23:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 23:3" />Pọọl amaabo anye ate, “Abasi ayaumia fiin, afo udedeppe ndibene! Afo atie do adikpe ikpe innọ miin ke ido mbed, ado afo ke idem mfo abiat mbed ke adinọ uyio ibo emmia miin!”<verse eid="ACT 23:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 23:4" />Mbon se ikida ikpere Pọọl emaebo, “Afo anam die asọñ ekamba aku Abasi anyen?”<verse eid="ACT 23:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 23:5" />Pọọl amaabọọrọ ate, “Nditọeka mmi, ami ñkidiọọñọke ke anye ado ekamba aku, sia e-ewet ebo: ‘Kuutañ idiọọk ikọ ubaña andikara mbon ndufo.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 23:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 23:6" />Ndin Pọọl, a-amaakediọọñọ ke usʌk ammọ edo mme Sadusi usʌk edo mme Farisi, anye amaakoot mbon esob Sanhidrin ke akpọsọñ uyio abo, “Nditọeka mmi, ami ndo Farisi, nto ubon Farisi ñko. Ami nda ke ikpe sia mmenie idodanyen ke adised mme akpañkpa.” <verse eid="ACT 23:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 23:7" />Ke anye amaaketañ ami, ikọ amaasakka ke atu mme Farisi ye mme Sadusi ndin mbono amaabakka iba. <verse eid="ACT 23:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 23:8" />(Mme Sadusi ebo ke adised ke ñkpa ibaaha, ñko ke mme enyere ye mme sịbidịd ibaaha, ado mme Farisi e-enịm afịd mme ñkpọ ami ke akpanikọ.)<verse eid="ACT 23:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 23:9" />Akpọsọñ ntịme amaasakka, ndin usʌk mme andikpeeb mbed e-ekedoññoke mme Farisi emaedaaña eda enyʌñ efaaña ke akpọsọñ uyio ete, “Ñnyịn ikịtte ñkpọ se idiọọk ke awo ami. Akpedo anam anye ado sịbidịd me enyere atañ ikọ anọ anye-e?” <verse eid="ACT 23:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 23:10" />Utọk amaakpon eti-eti, ndin adaiso ekọñ amaakop ndịk ke ammọ eyaewai Pọọl mbai-mbai. Anye amaanọ uyio abo mbon ekọñ eka ekeben anye ke adudu eka ekesịn ke badịk ekọñ.<verse eid="ACT 23:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 23:11" />Ke akonayio ayọhọ usen iba, Abọọñ amaada akpere Pọọl anyʌñ abo anye, <char style="wj">“Sọñ esịd! Naña nte afo amaaketie ntiense ambaña miin ke Yeruselem, ntoro ana afo atie ntiense ke Rom.”</char><verse eid="ACT 23:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Edioomo Adiwot Pọọl</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 23:12" />Ke ayio amaakesiere mme Yuu emaedʌk edioomo enyʌñ eta unwọñọ ete mmimọ idiidiaha ndidia inyʌññọ inwọñ mmọọñ tutu mmimọ iwot Pọọl. <verse eid="ACT 23:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 23:13" />Mbon se ikisịne ke edioomo ami emaewak ekan ideen aba. <verse eid="ACT 23:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 23:14" />Ammọ emaekaa ekebeeñe ñkpoon aku ye mme ñkpisọñ ebo, “Ñnyịn imidat ekamba unwọñọ ite ke ñnyịn idiidiaha ndidia tutu ñnyịn iwot Pọọl. <verse eid="ACT 23:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 23:15" />Do ndin, ndufo ye mme esob Sanhidrin iwet ñwed inọ adaiso ekọñ nọ edat anye edi iso ndufo nọ atie nte eyem ibọ anye afịd akpanikọ ke abaña ikpe amọ. Ñnyịn imibeeñe idem adiwot anye mbemiso anye adiwuọ mi.”<verse eid="ACT 23:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 23:16" />Ado ke ayịn ayịneka awonwaan Pọọl amaakekop edioomo ami, anye amaakaa badịk ekọñ akedọkkọ Pọọl.<verse eid="ACT 23:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 23:17" />Ndin Pọọl amaakoot keed ke atu mme sentudiọn ate, “Ben akparawa ami kaa ke iso adaiso ekọñ sia anye a-anie ñkpọ aditañ nnọọ anye.” <verse eid="ACT 23:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 23:18" />Anye amaaben anye akaa iso adaiso ekọñ.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 23:18">Sentudiọn amaanyʌñ akebo ate, “Pọọl, awo ñkpakọb, akedọñ eñkoot, ndin abo yak mben akparawa ami usọk sia anye anie se ayem aditañ unọọ.”<verse eid="ACT 23:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 23:19" />Adaiso ekọñ amaamʌm akparawa ami ke ubọk, adat anye asịkke akaa mbeñ keed akebịp abo, “Nsoo ke afo ayem aditañ innọ miin?”<verse eid="ACT 23:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 23:20" />Anye amaabo ate, “Mme Yuu e-edioomo adubo fiin yak anọ Pọọl adi ke iso esob Sanhidrin ñkpọñ nọ aba nte ke a-aba ataa akpanikọ a-ammọ eyemme adikop nto Pọọl. <verse eid="ACT 23:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 23:21" />Kuunyịmme unọọ ammọ sia e-ewak ekan awo aba ke atu ammọ e-edịbeke ke usʌñ ebet edimʌm anye. Ammọ emaeta unwọñọ ebo ke mmimọ idiidiaha ndidia, inyʌññọ inwọñ ñkpọ, tutu mmimọ iwot anye. Ammọ ebeeñe idem idahami, etie ebet afo adinyịmme ebeeñe ammọ.”<verse eid="ACT 23:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 23:22" />Adaiso ekọñ amaasio anye unyọñ, anyʌñ adʌt anye utọñ ate, “Kuutañ unọọ awo ndomokeed ke afo ametañ ñkpọ ami annọ miin.”<verse eid="ACT 23:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Esio Pọọl Enọ Aka Siseria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 23:23" />Ndin etubom ekọñ amaakoot sentudiọn iba anyʌñ anọ ammọ uyio ate, “Isio mbon ekọñ ikie iba, ye mbon ekọñ e-ewatta enañmbakara ata mme duob ye mme atobidañ ikie iba eka Siseria akonayio ami ke ñkanika usʌkkeed. <verse eid="ACT 23:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 23:24" />Inọ mme enañmbakara nọ eben Pọọl enyʌñ ekpeme anye dek-dek ekenọ Feliks adaiwuod ukara.”<verse eid="ACT 23:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 23:25" />Anye amaawet ñwedetob ntom:<verse eid="ACT 23:25" /></para>
  <para style="pmo">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 23:26" />Klaudius Lisias,</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="ACT 23:26">anọ esọk ataa ekamba adaiwuod ukara, Feliks:</para>
  <para style="pmo" vid="ACT 23:26">Mmukọọm-o!<verse eid="ACT 23:26" /></para>
  <para style="pm">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 23:27" />Mme Yuu ekemʌm awo ami ndin eyem adiwot anye, ado ami ye mbon ekọñ mmi imainyaaña anye sia mmaakediọọñọ ke anye ado amanaisọñ awo Rom. <verse eid="ACT 23:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 23:28" />Ami ñkeyem adidiọọñọ se inam ammọ edot anye uyio. Ke ntak ado ami mmaaben anye ndi ke iso esob Sanhidrin ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 23:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 23:29" />Ami ñkekop ke ndoduyio amọ akebaña ikọ mbed ammọ, ado ubiomikpe amọ ikidotto se ekpewowot me adisịn anye ke ñkpakọb. <verse eid="ACT 23:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 23:30" />Ke ini ami mmaakekop idiọọk ndịbe edioomo a-ndusʌk ammọ ekenamma ebaña uwem ete ami, ami mmaanọ anye usọk fiin ini keed. Ami mmaanyʌñ mbo yak mbon e-edotto anye uyio editañ mfịna a-ammọ enieghe ye anye ke iso mfo.<verse eid="ACT 23:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 23:31" />Ndin mbon ekọñ, ke adinam uyio ami, emaeben Pọọl ke akonayio ekesịm Antipatris. <verse eid="ACT 23:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 23:32" />Edem usen ammọ emaebo mbon ekọñ enañmbakara edat Pọọl eka, ndin ammọ emaetịmme enyọñọ badịk ekọñ. <verse eid="ACT 23:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 23:33" />Ke mbio ekọñ enañmbakara emaekekesịm Siseria, ammọ emaenọ adaiwuod ukara ñwedetob ado enyʌñ eyaak Pọọl esịn anye ke ubọk. <verse eid="ACT 23:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 23:34" />Adaiwuod ukara amaakoot ñwedetob ado ndin amaabịp Pọọl ikpeghe abio a-anye aketooho. Ke anye adidiọọñọ ke anye ato Silisia, <verse eid="ACT 23:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 23:35" />anye amaabo, “Ami ñyaakop ikpe mfo ke ini mbon u-udotto fiin uyio emaedisịm mi.” Ndin anye amaanọ uyio ate enịm Pọọl ke idak ukpeme ke akwere ufọk Herọd.<verse eid="ACT 23:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 23" />
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="ACT 24" />
  <para style="s1">Ikpe Pọọl ke Iso Feliks</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 24:1" />Ke usen ition amaakeboiyo, ekamba aku Ananayas amaadika Siseria asaña ye ubaak mme ñkpisọñ, ye akpe ikpe keed a-akekereke Tetulus, ndin ammọ emaekama se ediitañ idian Pọọl ke iso adaiwuod ukara, Feliks. <verse eid="ACT 24:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 24:2" />Ke ini ekekoodo Pọọl adi, Tetulus amaaben ikọ ikpe amọ anịm ke iso Feliks ntom: “Ñnyịn iminem esịd ke emem a-abaaha ke ukara mfo ye ukeme a-afo anieghe adida ñkịt ini iso, a-adatta mme ufa nti ñkpọ adi ke abio ami. <verse eid="ACT 24:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 24:3" />Ke afịd-afịd usʌñ ye afịd itie, ataa eti Feliks, ñnyịn imikịt inyʌñ ukọọm fiin ataa eti-eti. <verse eid="ACT 24:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 24:4" />Ado mbaak ñnyịn idudat fiin ika anyan, ami mmukpe fiin ubọk nte ke etək ini yak afo akpañ utọñ inọ ñnyịn ke mfọnido mfo.<verse eid="ACT 24:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 24:5" />“Ñnyịn imiyaara ikịt ke awo ami ado awo ntịme, a-anamma nọ mme Yuu ke afịd ederimbod esịn ntịme. Anye ado aboiyo iso awo anọ afịd mbon ñka Nasared, <verse eid="ACT 24:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 24:6" />amaanyʌñ adomo adiwuut tembịd: Ke ntoro ñnyịn imaimʌm anye. <verse eid="ACT 24:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 24:7" />Ñnyịn ikpaikibiire ikpe amọ naña asaña akekem ye mbed ñnyịn. Ado Laisias adaiso ekọñ amaadibọ ñnyịn anye ke ñkanubọk. <verse eid="ACT 24:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 24:8" />Afo umauduuñọ anye ke idem mfo, ayaakan adiọọñọ akpanikọ abaña afịd se ñnyịn itañ ami ibaña anye.”<verse eid="ACT 24:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 24:9" />Mme Yuu mfen emaenyʌñ ediana edot anye uyio adisọọñọ mbo ke mme ñkpọ se etañ ami edo akpanikọ.<verse eid="ACT 24:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 24:10" />Ndin, ke ini adaiwuod ukara amaakenọ Pọọl idiọọñọ ke ubọk abo atañ ikọ, anye amaabọọrọ ate: “Ami mmediọọñọ mbo ke afo amedo abiideikpe idịd ñnyịn ami ke uwak isua; ke ntoro annem miin esịd adikañ idem mmi. <verse eid="ACT 24:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 24:11" />Afo amekeme adibịp ndiọọñọ ke iboiyoke usen duob mme iba tọọñọ ami ñkedọọk ñka Yeruselem adikikpono Abasi. <verse eid="ACT 24:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 24:12" />Mbon se indot miin uyio ikiñkịtte miin nte nniin eniin ye awo ke tembịd me adinam mme atu awo esịn ntịme ke sinakọk me ke itie akeedodo ke abio. <verse eid="ACT 24:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 24:13" />Ndin ammọ idiikanna isọọñọ ke iso mfo ke se mmimọ itañ indian miin ado akpanikọ. <verse eid="ACT 24:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 24:14" />Ado ami mmenyịmme ke ami ñkpono Abasi mme eteete ñnyịn ñkeene Usʌñ Krais, a-ammọ ebooho ke ado idiọọk ñka. Ami mmenịm afịd ñkpọ a-asañake akekem ye Mbed Moses ye se ewet ke ñwed mme Prọfed. <verse eid="ACT 24:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 24:15" />Ndin ami mmenie ukem idodanyen ke Abasi kpa naña ibon ami enie, nte ke afịd awo, nti ye ndiọi, eyaeset ke ñkpa. <verse eid="ACT 24:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 24:16" />Ke ntoro, ami mmesidomo afịd ini adinam akikere esịd mmi asana ke iso Abasi ye ke iso awo.<verse eid="ACT 24:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 24:17" />“Ke uwak isua amaakeboiyo, ami mmaadi Yeruselem adiben mme enọ nsọk mbon mmi nọ enọ mme uweene ye mme enọ ima esịd. <verse eid="ACT 24:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 24:18" />Ami mmaanịm idem mmi asana ke ini ammọ ekeñkịtte miin ke afe tembịd naña nnam ñkpọ ami. Atu awo ikibaaha ye ami, ñko ñkisịnne mfịna. <verse eid="ACT 24:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 24:19" />Ado a-aba mme Yuu e-etooho Esia, a-akpekenaaha eba mi ke iso mfo nọ endot ikọ adieke ammọ enieghe ñkpọ adidat imbiom miin ikpe. <verse eid="ACT 24:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 24:20" />Amaaboiyo ado, mbon e-ebaaha mi akpena etañ idiọọk ñkpọ a-ammọ ekekịtte ke idem mmi ke ini ñkedaaha ke iso esob Sanhidrin. <verse eid="ACT 24:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 24:21" />Ibọhọke ñkpọ keed a-ami ñkebọññọ ñkpo ke ini ñkesʌkkọ nda ke iso ammọ mbo: ‘Ado ke ntak adised ke ñkpa ke ami nda ke ikpe ke iso ndufo mfịn ami.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 24:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 24:22" />Ndin Feliks, a-amaakemeghe anyʌñ adiọọñọ Usʌñ Krais amaasio ikpe anịm usen mfen, abo, “Ke ini Lisias, adaiso ekọñ amaadi, ami ñyaabiide ikpe mfo.” <verse eid="ACT 24:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 24:23" />Anye amaanọ sentudiọn uyio abo akpeme Pọọl, ado yak anye anie ifuuro anyʌñ ayak mme ufan amọ enọ anye unwam ke se anye ayem.<verse eid="ACT 24:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 24:24" />Ke usen ifañ amaakeboiyo, Feliks amaasaña ye anwaan amọ Drusila, awonwaan Yuu, adi. Anye amaadọñ ekekoot Pọọl anyʌñ akpañ utọñ akop naña anye atañ ikọ abaña mbuọdidem ke Krais Yisọs. <verse eid="ACT 24:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 24:25" />Naña Pọọl akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ abaña adinenido, mfarakeidem ye ubiideikpe a-adiidi, Feliks amaakop ndịk anyʌñ abo anye ate, “Ado akem diin! Amekeme ika. Ke ini a-adiifọn ye ami, ñyaadọñ nọ ukoot fiin.” <verse eid="ACT 24:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 24:26" />Feliks amaadot anyen ke Pọọl ayainọ imọ ubọkedem, ke ntak ado anye amaasidọñ ekoot anye ndin-ndin anyʌñ anie nneme ye anye.<verse eid="ACT 24:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 24:27" />Isua iba amaakeboiyo, Pọsiọs Festus amaadidat itie Feliks, ado sia Feliks akeyemme inam mfọn nnọọ mme Yuu, anye amaayaak Pọọl asịn ke ufọk ñkpakọb.<verse eid="ACT 24:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 24" />
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="ACT 25" />
  <para style="s1">Ikpe Pọọl ke Iso Festus</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 25:1" />Usen ita amaakeboiyo ke Festus akediwuọ ikpeghe ukara ado, anye amaato Siseria akaa Yeruselem, <verse eid="ACT 25:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 25:2" />ndin mme ñkpoon aku ye mme etubom mme Yuu emaeben ikpe Pọọl ekenịm anye ke iso. <verse eid="ACT 25:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 25:3" />Ammọ emaekpeiye Festus ebo inọ mmimọ mfọn, anọ Pọọl adi Yeruselem, sia ammọ emaebeeñe idem adidịbe ke usʌñ ñwot anye. <verse eid="ACT 25:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 25:4" />Ado Festus amaabọọrọ, “E-emọmʌm Pọọl enịm ke Siseria, ñko ami ke idem mmi ñyaasọp ñkaa do. <verse eid="ACT 25:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 25:5" />Yak ubaak mme adadusʌñ ndufo eñkeene miin eka, ndin adieke anye adueghe ñkpọ ndomokeed, ammọ ekeme adikoot anye ikpe ke udo.”<verse eid="ACT 25:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 25:6" />Ke Festus amaakeba do ye ammọ ke ñkpọ nte usen itiaita me duob, anye amaakaa Siseria. Edem usen anye amaakoot esob anyʌñ anọ uyio ate eben Pọọl edi iso imọ. <verse eid="ACT 25:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 25:7" />Ke Pọọl amaakediwuọ esob, mme Yuu e-eketooho Yeruselem edi emaeda ekanna anye ekʌk, enyʌñ etaañ uwak ndiọi ikọ edot anye, ado ammọ ikikanna iwọt ke ikọ se ammọ edot anye akedo akpanikọ.<verse eid="ACT 25:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 25:8" />Akekem Pọọl amaadifaaña idem amọ abo ate: “Ami ndueghe ñkpọ mbaña mbed mme Yuu me ake tembịd me ake Sisa.”<verse eid="ACT 25:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 25:9" />Ado Festus, a-akeduakka adiwọt mme Yuu ufọn amaabo Pọọl, “Nte afo amebeeñe idem adika Yeruselem ñkeda ikpe ke iso mmi ke abaña mme ikọ u-udotto fiin mi?”<verse eid="ACT 25:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 25:10" />Pọọl amaabọọrọ, “Ami nda ke iso esob Sisa a-akpenaaha akpe ikpe mmi. Ami ndueghe mme Yuu ndomokeed, nte afo atʌmmọ adiọọñọ. <verse eid="ACT 25:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 25:11" />Ado adieke ami ndueghe ñkpọ a-adotto ñkpa, ami nsịnne adikpa, ado akpedo uyio a-mme Yuu endotto idooho akpanikọ, awo ndomokeed inieghe unen adiñkappa miin nnọọ ammọ. Ami mmeben ikpe mmi ñketʌmọ Sisa!”<verse eid="ACT 25:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 25:12" />Ke Festus amaakedioomo ye mbon esob amọ ama, anye amaabo, “Sia adooho afo amenọ ebeeñe mfo esọk Sisa, iso Sisa ke afo uduuka!”<verse eid="ACT 25:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Festus Abọ Item Ato Adidem Akrippa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 25:13" />Usen ifañ akeboiyo, Adidem Akrippa ye Benis emaekewuọ Siseria adikikọọm Festus. <verse eid="ACT 25:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 25:14" />Sia ammọ emaekeba ke Siseria uwak usen, Festus amaaben mfịna Pọọl aneme anọ adidem abo ate, “A-aba awo mi a-Feliks akekpọññọ ke ñkpakọb. <verse eid="ACT 25:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 25:15" />Ke ini ami ñkekaaha Yeruselem, mme ikpọ aku ye mme ñkpisọñ mme Yuu emaeben anye edi esob enyʌñ ebo nọ ebiere ikpe ñkpa enọ anye.<verse eid="ACT 25:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 25:16" />“Ami mmaadọkkọ ammọ ke mbed eduuwem Rom iyakka ebiom awo ikpe ke ini awo imiinọọhọ anye ufañ nọ akañ idem amọ ke iso mbon e-edotto anye ikọ. <verse eid="ACT 25:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 25:17" />Ammọ emaekedi mi, ami ñkibiada ini, mmaakoot esob ke edem usen, mbo eben Pọọl edi. <verse eid="ACT 25:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 25:18" />Ado mbon e-ekekoodo anye ikpe ekedakka eda aditañ ikọ, ammọ ikitañña ibaña idiọọk ñkpọ ndomokeed se ami ñkekere mbaña a-Pọọl anamma. <verse eid="ACT 25:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 25:19" />Utu ke ado, utọk ammọ ye anye akebaña edu ukpono Abasi, ye awo e-ekoodo Yisọs, a-amaakekpa, a-Pọọl asʌkkọ abo ke mmọdo ke uwem. <verse eid="ACT 25:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 25:20" />Sia ndiikikanna nduuñọ utọ ñkpọ ami, ami mmaabo me anye anyịmme adika Yeruselem nọ ekekpe ikpe amọ ke abaña mme ikọ e-etañña edot anye. <verse eid="ACT 25:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 25:21" />Ado Pọọl amaabeeñe ate yak eben ikpe imọ esọk Sisa, ndin ami mmaanọ uyio nte emʌm anye enịm tutu ñkan nnọ anye esọk Sisa.”<verse eid="ACT 25:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 25:22" />Festus aketañ ami ama, Adidem Akrippa amaabo anye, “Ami ke idem mmi ñkpaama adikop nto Pọọl.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 25:22">Ndin Festus amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Ayaakop ato anye ñkpọñ.”<verse eid="ACT 25:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Eben Pọọl Ekaa Iso Akrippa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 25:23" />Edem usen, Akrippa ye Benis emaedi uko-uko, edidʌk ufọk esob, esaña ye mme ikpọ awuọiso mbon ekọñ ye mme awuọiso awo ke abio. Festus amaanọ uyio ate eben Pọọl edʌk edi. <verse eid="ACT 25:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 25:24" />Ndin Festus amaabo: “Adidem Akrippa ye afịd awo se iba mfịn ami ye ñnyịn, ise awo ami! Afịd idịd mme Yuu e-enam ebeeñe ebaña anye ennọ ke Yeruselem ye mi ke Siseria, enyʌñ ebọñ ñkpo ete ke ikpinaaha anye aba ke uwem aba. <verse eid="ACT 25:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 25:25" />Ado ami ke idem mmi mmeyʌkkọ ke anye inamma ñkpọ ndomokeed a-adotto ñkpa, ado sia anye ke idem amọ amaakebeeñe abo Sisa akpe ikpe imọ, mmaabiide adinọ anye aka Rom. <verse eid="ACT 25:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 25:26" />Ado ami nnieghe ataa akpan ñkpọ adiwet nnọọ Adidem mbaña anye. Ke ntoro, ami mmeben anye ndi ke iso afịd ndufo, akpan-akpan iso mfo, Adidem Akrippa, nọ ato ke utịd nduuñọ ami, ami nnie ñkpọ se ñwet. <verse eid="ACT 25:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 25:27" />Sia ami ñkere ke ufọn ibaaha adinọ awo ñkpakọb aka Rom ke ini awo miitʌmmọ itañ se ndiọiñkpọ anye anam.”<verse eid="ACT 25:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 25" />
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="ACT 26" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 26:1" />Ndin Adidem Akrippa amaabo Pọọl ate, “Mmunọ ufañ aditañ ñkpọ mbaña idem mfo.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 26:1">Pọọl amaasio ubọk anyan ndin atọọñọ adikañ idem amọ ate, <verse eid="ACT 26:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 26:2" />“Adidem Akrippa, ñkere ke ami mmenie ataa mfọniso adida ke iso mfo mfịn ami adifaaña mbaña afịd ndoduyio a-mme Yuu endotto miin, <verse eid="ACT 26:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 26:3" />akpan-akpan ke ntak a-adooho afo amenekke adiọọñọ eduuwem ye ndukpakka mfaaña mme Yuu. Ke ntoro, ami mmubeeñe fiin mbo yak anie ime akpañ utọñ annọ miin.<verse eid="ACT 26:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 26:4" />“Afịd mme Yuu e-ediọọñọ usʌñ naña ami ndʌñ ye ammọ tọọñọ ke uyịn mmi, ke ntọọñọ uwem mmi ke idịd ñnyịn ye ke Yeruselem. <verse eid="ACT 26:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 26:5" />Ammọ endiọọñọ miin ekpeene, ekpaenyʌñ etie ntiense, adieke ammọ emaaha, ebo ke ami mmaanekke mbre ñka edu ukpono Abasi ñnyịn ke adidu uwem nte Farisi. <verse eid="ACT 26:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 26:6" />Idahami, akeene ntak idodanyen a-ami nnieghe ke se Abasi amaakenwọñọ anọ mme eteete ñnyịn ke ami nda ke ikpe mfịn ami. <verse eid="ACT 26:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 26:7" />Ami ado enwọñọ e-esiin duob mme iba ñnyịn enieghe idodanyen adibọ naña ammọ ekpono Abasi ke eti esịd uweemeayio ye akonayio. Adidem Akrippa, ato ke idodanyen ami ke mme Yuu endot miin ikọ. <verse eid="ACT 26:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 26:8" />Ntak a-awo ndomokeed ke atu ndufo akpekereke ke idooho akpanikọ ke Abasi a-anam awo aset ke ñkpa-a?<verse eid="ACT 26:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 26:9" />“Ami ñko mmaabiide nte ke akpena nnam afịd se akpena enam adibiọọñọ anyịñ Yisọs, awo Nasared. <verse eid="ACT 26:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 26:10" />Ami ado se ami ñkenam ke Yeruselem. Ke adudu mme ikpọ aku ami mmaamuum uwak ndisana ikọd Abasi ndọñ ke ufọk ñkpakọb ndin ke ini ekebiireke ñkpa enọ ammọ, ami mmaanyịmme mbo ewoot ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 26:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 26:11" />Uwak ini, ami mmaasaña ke mme sinakọk adinọ ammọ ufen, ñnyʌñ ñyem usʌñ naña ammọ ekpemiom Yisọs. Ato akpọsọñ usua añkenieghe mbaña ammọ, mmaakọbọ ammọ tutu ñkewuọ mme asen abio.<verse eid="ACT 26:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 26:12" />“Ke usʌñ isañ mmi keed, ami ñkeka Damaskọs ke adudu ye uyio ñkpoon aku. <verse eid="ACT 26:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 26:13" />O Adidem Akrippa, ke ufọọd uweemeayio ñkanika duob mme iba, ke ini ami ñkesʌkkọ nsaña ke usʌñ, ami mmaakịt unwana a-aketooho hefịn, ayamma akan utịn, añkanna miin ye mme nsaña mmi akʌk. <verse eid="ACT 26:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 26:14" />Afịd ñnyịn imaiduọññọ ke isọñ, ndin ami mmaakop uyio a-akembooho miin ke usem Aramaik<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26:14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Me ke </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Hibru</char></note> ate, <char style="wj">‘Sọọl, Sọọl, nsoo ido ntak a-afo añkọbọke miin? Asọsọñ afo aditịgha eto nsọọbọ ñkukịm.’</char><verse eid="ACT 26:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 26:15" />“Ndin mmaabịp nte, ‘Afo ado anie, Abọọñ?’</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 26:15">“Abọọñ amaabọọrọ ate, <char style="wj">‘Ami ndo Yisọs a-afo akọbọke.</char> <verse eid="ACT 26:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 26:16" /><char style="wj">Idahami, dakka da ke ukod mfo. Ami mmeyaara idem uwọt fiin adumek fiin nte asañautom ye ntiense ke se afo akịt ambaña miin ye se ami nduuwọt fiin.</char> <verse eid="ACT 26:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 26:17" /><char style="wj">Ami ñyaunyaaña fiin nsio ke ubọk mbon ndufo ye ke ubọk mme Gentile. Ami ñyem adudọñ fiin nnọọ ammọ,</char> <verse eid="ACT 26:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 26:18" /><char style="wj">nọ aketat ammọ anyen anyʌñ anam ammọ ekappa ekpọñ ekịm ebịne unwana, ekpọñ adudu Setan, ebịne Abasi, nọ ammọ ebọ adifeen ke mme idiọọkñkpọ enyʌñ enie itie ke atu mbon e-emaenam esana ato ke mbuọdidem ke idem mmi.’</char><verse eid="ACT 26:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 26:19" />“Ke ntak ami, Adidem Akrippa, ñkisọññọ iwuod ke ntak ñkukịd a-aketooho hefịn. <verse eid="ACT 26:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 26:20" />Akpa, tọọñọ ye mbon e-ebaaha ke Damaskọs ye ke Yeruselem ye ke afịd Yudia, ye mme Gentile ñko, ñkekwọrọ mbo ammọ ekappa esịd ekeene Abasi enyʌñ ewọt ke mmimọ imikappa esịd ato ke mme adinam ammọ. <verse eid="ACT 26:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 26:21" />Ke ntak ami ke mme Yuu ekemmʌm miin ke akwere tembịd eyem adiñwot. <verse eid="ACT 26:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 26:22" />Ado mmenie unwam Abasi tutu asịm mfịn ami; ke ntoro ami mmeda mi aditañ ke esịd akpanikọ nnọ etək-etək ye ekamba ukem-ukem. Ntañña ñkpọ ndomokeed ñwuọ ñkpọñ se Moses ye mme prọfed emaeketatañ ke ayaatịppe, <verse eid="ACT 26:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 26:23" />ke Krais ayaabọ ufen, ndin nte akpa awo a-adiiset ke ñkpa, ayaadat etob unwana asọk mbon amọ ye mme Gentile.”<verse eid="ACT 26:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 26:24" />Naña Pọọl akesʌkkọ atañ ikọ afaaña idem amọ, Festus amaabọñ ñkpo ate, “Pọọl, afo amedamma! Akpọsọñ ifiọk ukpeeb mfo a-anam nọ afo adamma.”<verse eid="ACT 26:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 26:25" />Pọọl amaabọọrọ ate, “Ataa eti adaiwuod ukara Festus, ami ndammake. Se ami ntañ ado akpanikọ anyʌñ asaña ye eti akikere. <verse eid="ACT 26:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 26:26" />Adidem ameghe ye mme ñkpọ ami, ndin mmekeme itañ ikọ nnọ anye uko-uko. Mmenịm mbo ke ibaaha ñkpọ ami ndomokeed a-afeppe anye ke anyen sia ibaaha se ekenam ndịbe-ndịbe. <verse eid="ACT 26:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 26:27" />Adidem Akrippa, nte afo amenịm mme prọfed ke akpanikọ? Mmediọọñọ ke amenịm.”<verse eid="ACT 26:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 26:28" />Ndin Akrippa amaabịp Pọọl abo, “Afo amekere abo ke utọ etək ini ntom ke akpaakan añkappa miin esịd nọ ndo Kristian?”<verse eid="ACT 26:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 26:29" />Pọọl amaabọọrọ anye ate, “Me etək me anyan ini, ami mbọñ akam mbo Abasi akpekap anam, idooho afo ikpọọñ, ado afịd mbon e-ekpañña utọñ ennọọ miin mfịn, ekpekap eba nte ami ke esioho mme akpọnọ ami efep.”<verse eid="ACT 26:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 26:30" />Adidem, adaiwuod ukara, Benis ye mbon e-eketieghe ye ammọ emaedaaña eda. <verse eid="ACT 26:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 26:31" />Ammọ emaekpọñ ubeed ado ndin ke ini ammọ enemeke ye emọ-emọ, ndin emaebo ete, “Awo ami inamma ñkpọ ndomokeed a-adotto ñkpa me ñkpakọb.”<verse eid="ACT 26:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 26:32" />Ndin Akrippa amaabo Festus ate, “Ekpaekesaana awo ami eyaak akpedo anye ikibeeñeke ibo esio ikpe eka iso Sisa.”<verse eid="ACT 26:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 26" />
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="ACT 27" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akaa Rom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 27:1" />Ke emaekenyịmme nọ ñnyịn isaña ke mmọọñ ika Itali, emaekpọñ Pọọl ye mbon ñkpakọb mfen enọ Yuliọs, awo sentudiọn keed ke atu mbon se ikisikpeme Adidem Akọstọs. <verse eid="ACT 27:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 27:2" />Ñnyịn imaidʌk nsʌñikañ ke Adramitium a-akenaaha asio aka mme nsio-nsio esʌk ke Esia. Ñnyịn ikisaña ye Aristakus, awo a-aketooho Masidonia ke Tesalọnika.<verse eid="ACT 27:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 27:3" />Imaikiwuọ Sidọn ke ayọhọ usen iba, ndin Yuliọs amaanekke afọn ido ye Pọọl, ayak anye awuọ akese mme ufan amọ nọ enọ anye se ayem. <verse eid="ACT 27:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 27:4" />Imaito do imaana ikiwuọ akpa, iwat ke mben ñkpere Saiprọs a-akefọnnọ sia ayobio amaifịna ñnyịn. <verse eid="ACT 27:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 27:5" />Ke ñnyịn imaikiwat iboiyo akpa akpọññọ mben esʌk Silisia ye Pamfilia, imaikibeghe ke Mira, a-akebaaha ke abio Lisia. <verse eid="ACT 27:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 27:6" />Do ke sentudiọn akisịn ñnyịn ke nsʌñikañ Aleksandra a-akekaaha Itali. <verse eid="ACT 27:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 27:7" />Ñnyịn ikikanna iwat inyọọñ usʌñ, ndin ke ataa uwak usen amaisọñ ñnyịn idem adiwuọ Nidus. Ke ini ayobio imiikiyakka ñnyịn ibeghe ke udo, ñnyịn imaiwat ikiwuọ ukañ Kret a-akefọnnọ, a-akedaaha ke nsakiso Salmọn. <verse eid="ACT 27:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 27:8" />Akedo akpọsọñ ñkpọ ñnyịn adiwat ke mben esʌk tutu ikiwuọ itie e-ekoodo Fe Hafịns, a-akpereke abio Lasi.<verse eid="ACT 27:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 27:9" />Imaibiat ini ke usʌñ ikpeene, ñko uwad akedido ñkpọ afanekọñ sia akedo ini Usen Adifeen<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27:9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">A-adooho Yọm Kipọọ</char></note> a-amaakeboboiyo. Ndin Pọọl amaanọ ammọ item abo, <verse eid="ACT 27:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 27:10" />“Mme ete, mmekịt ke afanekọñ ayaaba ke isañ ñnyịn, ayaanyʌñ adat ekamba nsobo anọ nsʌñikañ, ye mbiomo ye uwem ñnyịn ñko.” <verse eid="ACT 27:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 27:11" />Ado sentudiọn, a-adooho etubom ekọñ awo ikie, akekpañ utọñ anọ se awad nsʌñikañ ye andinie nsʌñikañ eketañ, utu ke akpañ utọñ anọ Pọọl. <verse eid="ACT 27:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 27:12" />Sia mben esʌk ado imiikifọnnọ ke ini akpọsọñ ekarika, uwak awo emaebiire ebo yak emaana ewat eka iso tutu ekesịm Foniks a-akefọnnọ se eba ke ini akpọsọñ ekarika. Foniks akedo esʌk mbeghe ke Kret, a-akedaaha ke usuuk usobutịn ye adoro usobutịn.<verse eid="ACT 27:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ayobio</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 27:13" />Ke ini ifuuro-ifuuro afịm usuuk aketọọñọke adifịme, ammọ emaekere ke ado ataa eti ini adika isañ, ndin emaedʌt añkọ esịn, ewat esio, ekaa ukañ esʌk Kret. <verse eid="ACT 27:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 27:14" />Ikikpeeneke, ataa ekamba afịm unyekisọñ e-ekekoodo afịm Anyọñ-anyọñ amaato isu mmọọñ adi. <verse eid="ACT 27:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 27:15" />Ke ayobio ami amaakedisoobo nsʌñikañ, anyʌñ adisọñ ubọk akan nsʌñikañ, imaisaana iyaak inọ ayobio nọ iben ñnyịn aweere. Ñnyịn imaiwat ifrọ ke edem unaisọñ. <verse eid="ACT 27:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 27:16" />Naña ñnyịn ikiboiyoke ikiwuọ etək isu a-akereke Kauda, ñnyịn ikikanna adimʌm ubom unyaaña nsʌñikañ ñkama, <verse eid="ACT 27:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 27:17" />ndin ammọ emaedʌt anye esịn ke esịd ubom. Akem ammọ emaesio udʌk ke idak nsʌñikañ adimʌm anye ñkama nọ asọñ. Sia idem amaanyeñ ammọ ke iyaisịp ke utatan Saitis, ammọ emaeyaak añkọ esịn ke mmọọñ nọ ayobio awat nsʌñikañ naña ama. <verse eid="ACT 27:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 27:18" />Naña ayobio akesʌkkọ anekke itịm ñnyịn ke idem, mme awat nsʌñikañ emaetọọñọ itoomo mbiomo ndọñ ke mmọọñ ke ayọhọ usen iba. <verse eid="ACT 27:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 27:19" />Ke ayọhọ usen ita, ammọ emaetop udʌk umʌm nsʌñikañ esịn ke mmọọñ. <verse eid="ACT 27:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 27:20" />Ke uwak usen, awo ikikanna ikịt utịn me ntantaafiọñ; ado ayobio akesʌk aka iso afịme, ndin ñnyịn imaiduọọk idodanyen adibọkkọ ye uwem.<verse eid="ACT 27:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 27:21" />Ke mme awo emaeketie anyan ini idiaha ndidia, Pọọl amaadakka ada ke iso ammọ anyʌñ abo: “Akpekena ndufo ekop item mmi idaha ñkebooho ke ndufo isio uwat ikpọñ Kret, ndin afịd nsobo ye unọmọ ami ikpisịmme ndufo. <verse eid="ACT 27:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 27:22" />Ado idahami, ibo ndufo isọñ idem, sia uwem awo ndufo ndomokeed idiitakka, nsʌñikañ ikpọọñ adiibiara. <verse eid="ACT 27:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 27:23" />Akonayio ñkpọñ a-akeboiyoke enyere Abasi annieghe miin, a-ami ñnyʌññọ nnam ñkpọ nnọ amaabiọññọ ke ñkañ mmi, <verse eid="ACT 27:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 27:24" />anyʌñ ambo miin, ‘Pọọl, kuufeghe ndịk. Ana afo ada ikpe ke iso Sisa; Abasi ke mfọn amọ a-anyʌñ anyaaña afịd awo e-ewatta ye afo.’ <verse eid="ACT 27:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 27:25" />Ke ntoro, isọñ idem sia mmenie mbuọdidem ke Abasi nte ke ayaasu kpa naña anye akendọkkọ. <verse eid="ACT 27:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 27:26" />Ado nsʌñikañ ñnyịn ayaasịp ke isu mmọọñ keed.”<verse eid="ACT 27:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Nsʌñikañ Asịp</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 27:27" />Ke akonayio ayọhọ usen duob mme inaañ, nte ayobio akesʌkkọ iben ñnyịn aka iso ye edem ke Akpainyañ Adriatik, mme awad nsʌñikañ emaekere ke imikpere unaisọñ. <verse eid="ACT 27:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 27:28" />Ammọ emaedomo enyʌñ ekịt ke mmọọñ aketəñọ ikpad ikie mme edịb.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte mita 37</char></note> Etək ini akeboiyo, ammọ emaemaana edomo enyʌñ ekịt ke mmọọñ aketəño ikpad anaañ mme duob<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27:28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ñkpọ nte mita 27</char></note>. <verse eid="ACT 27:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 27:29" />Ato ke ufeghe ndịk nsʌñikañ adikituagha ke itiad, ammọ emaesuuk añkọ inaañ eto ke itak ubom, enyʌñ ebọñ akam ebo ayio anwaña. <verse eid="ACT 27:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 27:30" />Mme awad nsʌñikañ emaedomo adifeeñe ñkpọñ nsʌñikañ ndin emaesuuk ubom unyaaña esịn ke mmọọñ mbemiso esuuk añkọ. <verse eid="ACT 27:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 27:31" />Ndin Pọọl amaabo sentudiọn ye mme mbon ekọñ ate, “Ibọhọke mme awo ami esọñ esịne ke nsʌñikañ, awo idiikanna inyaaña ndufo.” <verse eid="ACT 27:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 27:32" />Ndin mbon ekọñ ado emaekpok mme udʌk e-ekemʌmmọ ubom ekama eyaak ubom adifoofuum ke anyọñ mmọọñ.<verse eid="ACT 27:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 27:33" />Ayio akekpere adisiere, Pọọl amaakpeiye afịd ammọ ate edia ndidia, “Usen duob mme inaañ ado ami ndufo idiaha ñkpọ ndomokeed, enyʌñ eba ke akpọsọñ ayeemensia. <verse eid="ACT 27:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 27:34" />Ami mmibeeñe ndufo mbo edia ñkpọ, ana edia ñkpọ nọ edu uwem. Eyaebọkkọ ndin ided iwuod ndufo ndomokeed idiitakka.” <verse eid="ACT 27:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 27:35" />Pọọl aketañ ami ama, anye amaaben uyio akama anyʌñ anọ Abasi ekọọm ke iso afịd ammọ. Ndin amaabuuñ anyʌñ atọọñọ adita. <verse eid="ACT 27:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 27:36" />Ammọ emaebọ idọñesịd enyʌñ etọọñọ idia ndidia. <verse eid="ACT 27:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 27:37" />Afịd ñnyịn se ikiba ke nsʌñikañ ikido awo ikie iba mme ata mme duob mme itiokeed (276). <verse eid="ACT 27:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 27:38" />Ammọ emaekedia naña ammọ ekeyeyem, emaetoomo mme abakpa e-ekesʌhọke edọñ ke inyañ nọ nsʌñikañ ayakka.<verse eid="ACT 27:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 27:39" />Ke ini ayio asiereke, ammọ ikidiọọñọke ukañ adooho isọñ, ado emaekịt adịk a-akenieghe esʌk utatan a-ammọ ekebiireke ebo ekpekan, yak enam nsʌñikañ asịp ke ndo. <verse eid="ACT 27:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 27:40" />Ammọ emaekpịkke mme ubọkekọp ubom esịññe eyaak edọñ ke isọñ inyañ, enyʌñ etaat mme udʌk e-ekemʌmmọ mme eba nsʌñikañ ekama, edịppe afada iso ewuuk enyʌñ ewat ekaa ukañ esʌk. <verse eid="ACT 27:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 27:41" />Ado ukod mmọọñ amaaben nsʌñikañ aketọ ke utatan ndin anye amaasịp. Iso ubom amaabʌhọ ke esịd utatan, ikanna ifakka iwuọ aba, ndin itak ubom amaabʌñọ mbai-mbai ato naña inua akpa akesʌk aka iso atọ nsʌñikañ.<verse eid="ACT 27:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 27:42" />Mbon ekọñ emaedioomo adiwoot mbon ñkpakọb e-ekedọñọke ke nsʌñikañ mbaak ammọ ediwọk mmọọñ efeeñe. <verse eid="ACT 27:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 27:43" />Ado sentudiọn ikiyemme ñkpọ anam Pọọl ndin anye ikiyakka ammọ enam uduak ami. Anye amaanọ uyio ate mbon se inọ ewọk iwọk eto etamma, ewọk ekewuọ abod. <verse eid="ACT 27:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 27:44" />Akena mbon mfen ekama mme adukpọk miidooho ekama ñkprañ ubom esaña ekewuọ abod. Ke ntoro, afịd awo emaekewuọ abod ke uwem ye ifuuro.<verse eid="ACT 27:44" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 27" />
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="ACT 28" />
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Adibeghe ke Malta</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 28:1" />Ke imaikisịm unaisọñ ke ifuuro, do ke ñnyịn ikididiọọñọ ke isu mmọọñ ado akekere Malta. <verse eid="ACT 28:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 28:2" />Mbon idʌñ ado emaenekke efọn ido ye ñnyịn. Ke ntak atueb ye edịm akedeppe, ammọ emaidaara ñnyịn ke adibara ikañ inọọ nọ iwue. <verse eid="ACT 28:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 28:3" />Pọọl amaatañña abek ifia nọ ekama ebara ikañ, ndin anye akesịn ikañ, idiọọk udʌkikọd amaawuọ awaña anye ke ubọk, ato ufiob ikañ. <verse eid="ACT 28:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 28:4" />Mbon idʌñ ado ekekịt naña udʌkikọd awaña Pọọl ke ubọk, ammọ emaebo emọ-emọ, “Ana ado awo ami ado awodawo; akpesʌkado a-anye amaakebọkkọ ke akpainyañ, ndem Usiene idiọọk ñkpọ iyakka anye adu uwem.” <verse eid="ACT 28:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 28:5" />Ado Pọọl amaasịppe udʌkikọd ado asịn ke ikañ, ñkpọ inamma anye. <verse eid="ACT 28:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 28:6" />Mbon awo ado ekekere ke anye ayaayọọk, imiidooho anye aduọ akpa adiyok-adiyok, ado akekpeene nọ ammọ imiikịtte nte ñkpọ anam anye, ammọ emaekpəhọ akikere ebo ke anye ado abasi.<verse eid="ACT 28:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 28:7" />Amaaba akwere i-imiikinyọọñọ usʌñ, a-Publius, ekamba andikara abio ado, akenieghe. Anye amaidaara ñnyịn anyʌñ inọ ñnyịn ndidia ye itie nnaa usen ita nte isenawo ke ufọk amọ. <verse eid="ACT 28:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 28:8" />Ndin idem ikisọññọ ete Publius; ufiobidem ye utọrọ iyiib akenam anye anaana ke ikʌk. Pọọl amaakese anye, ndin ke amaakebọñ akam ama, amaadot anye ubọk anyʌñ akọk anye udọñọ. <verse eid="ACT 28:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 28:9" />Ami akekweeñe, mbon mfen e-ekedọñọke ke idʌñ ado emaewuọñọ edibọ ukọk. <verse eid="ACT 28:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 28:10" />Ami amaanam ammọ ikpono ñnyịn ke uwak usʌñ, inọ ñnyịn mme ñkpọ se ikiyem ke ini ikibooho ikpọñ ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 28:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Adiwuọ Rom</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 28:11" />Ke afiọñ ita amaakeboiyo, ñnyịn imaikpọñ ke nsʌñikañ a-akedidianna abet ekarika akweeñe ke isu mmọọñ ado. Nsʌñikañ ami aketo Aleksandra, anie iso mme amanamba abasi e-ekoodo Kastọ ye Poluks. <verse eid="ACT 28:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 28:12" />Ñnyịn imaiwuọ Sirakus, inyʌñ ikitie do usen ita. <verse eid="ACT 28:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 28:13" />Tọọñọ do, imaisio uwad ikiwuọ Rekium. Edem usen, afịm usuuk amaatọọñọ afịme, ndin ke ayọhọ usen iba imaikiwuọ Putioli. <verse eid="ACT 28:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 28:14" />Ke udo ke ñnyịn ikisoobo ye ikọd Abasi e-ekikoodo ñnyịn ebo idiba ye ammọ udua keed. Ndin ñnyịn imaikiwuọ Rom. <verse eid="ACT 28:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 28:15" />Ke mme ikọd Abasi ke Rom emaekekop ke ñnyịn isʌk idi, ammọ emaenam isañ tutu ekewuọ Afe Mbono Apius ye mme Itie Ukama Isen Ita nọ edisoobo ye ñnyịn. Pọọl amaakọọm Abasi, anyʌñ abọ idọñesịd ke adikịt ibon ado. <verse eid="ACT 28:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 28:16" />Ñnyịn ikikisịm Rom emaenyịmme Pọọl adʌñ ke idem amọ ikpọọñ, ado emaenọ awo ekọñ akpeme anye.<verse eid="ACT 28:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Pọọl Akwọrọ Ikọ ke Rom ke Idak Ukpeme</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 28:17" />Usen ita amaakeboiyo, Pọọl amaakoot mbono mme adaiwuod mme Yuu. Ammọ emaekediboho, Pọọl amaabo ammọ ate: “Nditọeka mmi ke Krais, akpesʌkado a-ami mmiidueghe mbon ñnyịn me mbed mme eteete ñnyịn, emaemmʌm miin ke Yeruselem enyʌñ eñkappa enọ mbon Rom. <verse eid="ACT 28:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 28:18" />Ammọ emaenduuñọ miin enyʌñ eyem adinsaana ñyaak, sia ami ñkidueghe mbed ndomokeed a-adotto ñkpa. <verse eid="ACT 28:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 28:19" />Ado mme Yuu emaefaaña, ndin akena ami mben ikpe mmi ñka iso Sisa sia mmaaketʌmọ anye. Ke aditịm ntañ, ami ñkinieghe akikere adikoot mbon mmi ikpe. <verse eid="ACT 28:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 28:20" />Ke ntak ami ke ami ñyem adisoobo ñnyʌñ nneme nneme ye ndufo. Sia ato ke ntak idodanyen Isrel ke ensịn miin ke ñkpọnọ ami.”<verse eid="ACT 28:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 28:21" />Ammọ emaebọọrọ, “Ñnyịn ibọọhọ ñwedetob ndomokeed u-ubañake fiin ito Yudia, inyʌññọ iba awo ndomokeed ke atu mme ikọd Abasi a-atooho udo adi adinọ etob me atañ idiọọk ñkpọ ubaña fiin. <verse eid="ACT 28:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 28:22" />Ado ñnyịn imiyem adikop akikere mfo, sia ñnyịn imidiọọñọ ke mme awo ke afịd itie etaañ ikọ edot atu mme akpono Abasi ami.”<verse eid="ACT 28:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 28:23" />Ammọ emaedot usen enyʌñ ebeeñe idem adisoobo ye Pọọl, enyʌñ esaña ye ataa uwak awo ekaa itie a-anye akedʌññọ. Tọọñọ ke ubakusen tutu ndubiayio, Pọọl amaanam anwaña ammọ, akwọrọ abioubọọñ Abasi anwa-anwa anọ ammọ, anwana adinam ammọ ekịt ye anye ufọn adinịm Yisọs ke akpanikọ a-atooho ke Mbed Moses ye ake mme Prọfed. <verse eid="ACT 28:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 28:24" />Ubaak awo emaenịm ikọ amọ ke akpanikọ, ado ubaak ikinịmme. <verse eid="ACT 28:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 28:25" />Ke ntoro ammọ emaefaaña ke atu idem ammọ enyʌñ etọọñọ adinyọñọ ke Pọọl amaaketañ akpatre ikọ ami: “Adisana Sịbidịd aketañ akpanikọ anọ mme eteete ndufo ato ke prọfed Aisaiya abo ate:<verse eid="ACT 28:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 28:26" />“ ‘Kaa ke tañ nọ ibon ami,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:26">“Ndufo eyaekop, ado idiinwañake ndufo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:26">ndufo eyaekịt ado idiimọọnọke.”<verse eid="ACT 28:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 28:27" />Sia esịd ibon ami adoro ufiọọn;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">ammọ ikoppo ñkpọ ke utọñ ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">ñko enyʌñ ebọọp anyen ammọ.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:27">Mmiidooho ntoro anyen ammọ ekpaekịt ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">utọñ ammọ ekpaenyʌñ ekop ñkpọ,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">ñkpọ akpaanyʌñ anwaña ammọ,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:27">ndin ammọ ekappa esịd, etịmme edi, ndin ami ñkpaakọk ammọ.’<verse eid="ACT 28:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 28:28" />“Ke ntoro, ami ñyem ndufo ediọọñọ ke e-enọ adinyaaña Abasi ami esọk mme Gentile, ndin ammọ eyaekpañ utọñ.” <verse eid="ACT 28:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 28:29" />Anye amaaketañ mme ikọ ami ama, mme Yuu emaedaaña enyọñọ, esʌk efaaña mbiaak-mbiaak ke idem ammọ.<verse eid="ACT 28:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 28:30" />Pọọl amaadʌñ do ke ufọk a-anye akekpeeghe ke idem amọ ke afịd isua iba anyʌñ adaara afịd awo se ikidi idise anye. <verse eid="ACT 28:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 28:31" />Anye amaakwọrọ abioubọọñ Abasi anyʌñ akpeep mme awo ñkpọ abaña Abọọñ Yisọs Krais uko-uko, ndin awo ndomokeed ikidomoke adikpan anye.<verse eid="ACT 28:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 28" />
</usx>